arred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeAgent/commits/2e85f5e01dcb6270e715c380474c057d2c99ca59/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T19:16:02Z","email":"99821070+izzywdev@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Israel Weinberg"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T19:16:02Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(frontend): remediate high and critical dependency advisories (#829)\n\nRemediates frontend high/critical dependency advisories using patched\nHappy DOM, Vitest/V8 coverage and the tinyglobby-based typescript-eslint\ndependency path. Removes source-map-js indexed-map denial of service\n(GHSA-68fv-2mgg-jv7q) with 1.2.2 and typography selector CPU exhaustion\n(GHSA-rj75-hqrm-r3gf) with parser 7.1.6. High-severity audit enforcement\nremains enabled.\n\nThe parser override is scoped only to @tailwindcss/typography, whose\ncurrent supported release still pins 6.0.10. Five permanent regressions\nvalidate byte-identical typography components/variants against the\nparser-6 baseline across modern, prefixed, legacy and custom-class\ncontexts, covering all 29 modifiers and 29 variants in each context plus\nactual Tailwind 4 prose CSS compilation. Baselines use the exact\nexisting application typography configuration. npm''s offline\npackage-lock-only resolver accepts the final package/lock pair; npm\naudit reports zero vulnerabilities. Independently downloaded\nsource-map-js and parser tarball SHA512 values match public npm\nintegrity. Private identity pins and reviewer wiring remain unchanged.\n\nPreserves current main escalation/UI/Helm/image work. Removes\nsecret-bearing vault resolver logs and fails closed for missing\ncredentials instead of fabricating keys; existing resolver regressions\ncover missing credentials and redaction. Keeps inherited Python\nformatting and vendored registration synchronization fixes.\n\nValidation: all CI/CD, Test Suite, Security Scans and Harden workflows\npassed on the preceding source-map-js-only head\n5dc68660f3915e5209a26e1f00a95c1017abbb2e. The latest parser\ncompatibility tests (5) pass locally; all three new blobs were read back\nand matched exact hashes. Current head\n5188aa8ebda84a46cdd2edacb53a826247a7f9a7 needs fresh ordinary CI/review.\nLocal full app install still stops at HTTP 401 fetching the existing\nprivate GitHub Packages identity package, so no local full\nbuild/typecheck claim is made for this last change.\n\nThe review workflow recognizes CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN and passes it to\nthe subscription rung before API providers. Actual review run\n37452137310 attempted that path but returned 401 Invalid bearer token.\nPresence of the repository secret does not establish validity; required\nreviewer/MCP checks remain blockers until a real reviewer succeeds. No\nrequired checks were disabled or waived, and no production deployment is\nclaimed.\n\nSupply-chain remediation update (commit 0565c080): the unresolved\nSemgrep finding on `.github/workflows/security.yml` is closed.\n`actions/upload-artifact` is pinned to immutable commit\n`ea165f8d65b6e75b540449e92b4886f43607fa02` (v4.6.2), matching the\nrepository''s existing fleet pin. Workflow YAML validation and diff\nchecks passed; uploaded blob `61b971fde4143f67e460ef209bbee931185d678f`\nand remote tree `bd953aa60aaade7fccc0f87a418b6fbd9620dd20` match\nlocally. Fresh Harden Gate, Security Scans and A2A Maintain pass; the\nsecurity review thread auto-resolved. Functional CI and the FuzeAgent\nTest Suite now pass. Fuze Code Review and MCP remain blocked by the\nexisting reviewer-provider credential failures; no approval, merge or\nproduction deployment is claimed.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"bd953aa60aaade7fccc0f87a418b6fbd9620dd20","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeAgent/git/trees/bd953aa60aaade7fccc0f87a418b6fbd9620dd20"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeAgent/git/commits/2e85f5e01dcb6270e715c380474c057d2c99ca59","verification":{"payload":"tree bd953aa60aaade7fccc0f87a418b6fbd9620dd20\nparent 82fc6a6c4c9f6dcf3a49dadf0d8984c5a4b73ba6\nauthor Israel Weinberg <99821070+izzywdev@users.noreply.github.com> 1791314162 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791314162 +0300\n\nfix(frontend): remediate high and critical dependency advisories (#829)\n\nRemediates frontend high/critical dependency advisories using patched\nHappy DOM, Vitest/V8 coverage and the tinyglobby-based typescript-eslint\ndependency path. Removes source-map-js indexed-map denial of service\n(GHSA-68fv-2mgg-jv7q) with 1.2.2 and typography selector CPU exhaustion\n(GHSA-rj75-hqrm-r3gf) with parser 7.1.6. High-severity audit enforcement\nremains enabled.\n\nThe parser override is scoped only to @tailwindcss/typography, whose\ncurrent supported release still pins 6.0.10. Five permanent regressions\nvalidate byte-identical typography components/variants against the\nparser-6 baseline across modern, prefixed, legacy and custom-class\ncontexts, covering all 29 modifiers and 29 variants in each context plus\nactual Tailwind 4 prose CSS compilation. Baselines use the exact\nexisting application typography configuration. npm''s offline\npackage-lock-only resolver accepts the final package/lock pair; npm\naudit reports zero vulnerabilities. Independently downloaded\nsource-map-js and parser tarball SHA512 values match public npm\nintegrity. Private identity pins and reviewer wiring remain unchanged.\n\nPreserves current main escalation/UI/Helm/image work. Removes\nsecret-bearing vault resolver logs and fails closed for missing\ncredentials instead of fabricating keys; existing resolver regressions\ncover missing credentials and redaction. Keeps inherited Python\nformatting and vendored registration synchronization fixes.\n\nValidation: all CI/CD, Test Suite, Security Scans and Harden workflows\npassed on the preceding source-map-js-only head\n5dc68660f3915e5209a26e1f00a95c1017abbb2e. The latest parser\ncompatibility tests (5) pass locally; all three new blobs were read back\nand matched exact hashes. Current head\n5188aa8ebda84a46cdd2edacb53a826247a7f9a7 needs fresh ordinary CI/review.\nLocal full app install still stops at HTTP 401 fetching the existing\nprivate GitHub Packages identity package, so no local full\nbuild/typecheck claim is made for this last change.\n\nThe review workflow recognizes CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN and passes it to\nthe subscription rung before API providers. Actual review run\n37452137310 attempted that path but returned 401 Invalid bearer token.\nPresence of the repository secret does not establish validity; required\nreviewer/MCP checks remain blockers until a real reviewer succeeds. No\nrequired checks were disabled or waived, and no production deployment is\nclaimed.\n\nSupply-chain remediation update (commit 0565c080): the unresolved\nSemgrep finding on `.github/workflows/security.yml` is closed.\n`actions/upload-artifact` is pinned to immutable commit\n`ea165f8d65b6e75b540449e92b4886f43607fa02` (v4.6.2), matching the\nrepository''s existing fleet pin. Workflow YAML validation and diff\nchecks passed; uploaded blob `61b971fde4143f67e460ef209bbee931185d678f`\nand remote tree `bd953aa60aaade7fccc0f87a418b6fbd9620dd20` match\nlocally. Fresh Harden Gate, Security Scans and A2A Maintain pass; the\nsecurity review thread auto-resolved. Functional CI and the FuzeAgent\nTest Suite now pass. Fuze Code Review and MCP remain blocked by the\nexisting reviewer-provider credential failures; no approval, merge or\nproduction deployment is claimed.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid"