github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/commits/4b938ae76452c18261ce306ed8c4c66090165f27"}],"sha":"988c10837b4c5e5d0ad151820ffcbc4bd7c4dd82","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/commits/988c10837b4c5e5d0ad151820ffcbc4bd7c4dd82"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83823539?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fred-labs","id":83823539,"login":"fred-labs","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzODIzNTM5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/commits/4b938ae76452c18261ce306ed8c4c66090165f27/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-26T15:27:27Z","email":"fred-labs@mailbox.org","name":"fred-labs"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-26T15:27:27Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"A waiting command''s exit codes are defined once, and every list of them is rendered (#719)\n\n`vast campaign wait` and `vast image wait` are branched on by exit status, but\ntheir codes were written out by hand in the command''s help, the MCP next_step\nstrings, the run prompt, the docs, the skill and several comments, and the\ncopies disagreed about which codes exist.\n\nThe codes are now members of an enum in robovast.execution.wait_exit\n(CampaignWaitExit, ImageWaitExit), each with a short label, a meaning and\nwhether it leaves the waited-on work running. The commands raise the members.\nEverything that lists the codes renders them from the enum: the --help via a\ndocstring decorator, the start_campaign and image-build next_step strings and\nthe run prompt via summary(), and the one table in docs/client.rst via a new\nwait-exit-codes Sphinx directive, which other pages link to. Prose elsewhere\nnames a member instead of a number.\n\ntests/execution/test_wait_exit_codes_sync.py fails on a wait exit code stated\nby number in docs/, skills/, hooks/ or src/, on a wait command exiting with\nanything but a member of its enum or never with one of them, on a help text\nmissing a member, and on a second docs table.\n\nAlso: `vast image wait` exits with BUILT explicitly on success, and the\nhealth-finding example in docs/mcp.rst shows a stuck-sim-time finding.","tree":{"sha":"469e43c8e799c0e35c81bec18c868182fed5e29b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/git/trees/469e43c8e799c0e35c81bec18c868182fed5e29b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/git/commits/4b938ae76452c18261ce306ed8c4c66090165f27","verification":{"payload":"tree 469e43c8e799c0e35c81bec18c868182fed5e29b\nparent cd894a89ca1ce27d369a1e9709033e5fbaad9fce\nauthor fred-labs <fred-labs@mailbox.org> 1790436447 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790436447 +0200\n\nA waiting command''s exit codes are defined once, and every list of them is rendered (#719)\n\n`vast campaign wait` and `vast image wait` are branched on by exit status, but\ntheir codes were written out by hand in the command''s help, the MCP next_step\nstrings, the run prompt, the docs, the skill and several comments, and the\ncopies disagreed about which codes exist.\n\nThe codes are now members of an enum in robovast.execution.wait_exit\n(CampaignWaitExit, ImageWaitExit), each with a short label, a meaning and\nwhether it leaves the waited-on work running. The commands raise the members.\nEverything that lists the codes renders them from the enum: the --help via a\ndocstring decorator, the start_campaign and image-build next_step strings and\nthe run prompt via summary(), and the one table in docs/client.rst via a new\nwait-exit-codes Sphinx directive, which other pages link to. Prose elsewhere\nnames a member instead of a number.\n\ntests/execution/test_wait_exit_codes_sync.py fails on a wait exit code stated\nby number in docs/, skills/, hooks/ or src/, on a wait command exiting with\nanything but a member of its enum or never with one of them, on a help text\nmissing a member, and on a second docs table.\n\nAlso: `vast image wait` exits with BUILT explicitly on success, and the\nhealth-finding example in docs/mcp.rst shows a stuck-sim-time finding.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqt+RfCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAADqsQAKI3BiEVDTsgJAhfePQIDw3G\njjoThoiXUYTB7XCPr2aqRbU6JZmRamWDe5aKNranZ0chjvLprjY4ZH9yc3AtYFDv\nXjC+Mf0dlzvDD1ppqCHMtDap9y6ex589SeFzf5IVuynJqX8QeZKxOVzkrT0SmYOX\nFCvMa53aqCwmy0krOf6Mp/+uaODS/RVN1zN0b/UvA3FoZhlDUgZ0BVVIAlutLBAk\ncc4hzreV50CbKkbwZtAfGzv+5R/fXneJvOu9OF2QXIgi1ta1V8irI3251XCmXU13\nsaE/XMvxcUCYNzU22MyY3IwIU4lCOBjUDleS2SnRlK4i2gUv2XhD3GdknxPApqsq\ng52s8xbbArqOneMdoLOmh7kQ/nS8ErzHFNbk9yti+OZ3sCYQf7Z7aJvd7eDYChbC\ni4NwkigQRSK4ykz6iTpWNhOL9xClAqZJ7Hx0lodEtNAmqHDXIX32b0l4pjgmWXJ3\nQQORvYOfOXaPo6XC3VperNI0EDLwScknsYacnrZ9krGpBIWZ+Nc3XMQDwZNGqe0E\nfKAic6Z76JZzfxEjDa+5jRRRablZ6taKU4kQJXH0IGnaQ3W+Rz/b/MOb9D9s5/Ux\nONPZs6l3drIx0fldOaYU9E1gkAfJpebZEumaTGKt9bP3jiUIpHJvQN9htnT4NvGS\nwle3ClbZj0eqDOaHabFr\n=PiSO\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-26T15:27:27Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-