s{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fred-labs","id":83823539,"login":"fred-labs","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzODIzNTM5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/commits/2118ecacb242e5fffb67dbbdc5a16987bc69039e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-26T15:21:12Z","email":"fred-labs@mailbox.org","name":"fred-labs"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-26T15:21:12Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"An exec that stages a configuration arranges the aux runner first (#706)\n\n* An exec that stages a configuration arranges the aux runner first\n\nexec_in_container with a config_name composes the .vast to stage that\nconfiguration, and composition reaches whatever it asks a container for:\nthe simulator backend''s input-files query, a variation''s helper image, a\ngenerator''s. The exec path composed without entering the service''s\naux-runner context, so on a service with no local docker every such exec\nwas refused with AuxContainerUnavailable, although preview and validation\nof the same file compose fine.\n\nstage() now runs inside _aux_runner_context, held and keyed on the source\nwith the preview tag, so a file previewed and then exec''d shares one warm\ncontainer. A bare-image exec composes nothing and still starts nothing.\n\n* Say that exec_in_container''s config_name names a configuration, not a file\n\nThe source picks the .vast (a workspace''s config_path, or what a campaign recorded);\nconfig_name picks one of the configurations it expands into, as preview_configurations\nnames them. docs/mcp.rst shows the lookup and a check of one configuration against both\nsources.","tree":{"sha":"8dda1a5187f7e801feec1f51ed810774300d3f51","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/git/trees/8dda1a5187f7e801feec1f51ed810774300d3f51"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/git/commits/2118ecacb242e5fffb67dbbdc5a16987bc69039e","verification":{"payload":"tree 8dda1a5187f7e801feec1f51ed810774300d3f51\nparent a981dc71016a489c1be7f773b94c45d9032b7853\nauthor fred-labs <fred-labs@mailbox.org> 1790436072 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790436072 +0200\n\nAn exec that stages a configuration arranges the aux runner first (#706)\n\n* An exec that stages a configuration arranges the aux runner first\n\nexec_in_container with a config_name composes the .vast to stage that\nconfiguration, and composition reaches whatever it asks a container for:\nthe simulator backend''s input-files query, a variation''s helper image, a\ngenerator''s. The exec path composed without entering the service''s\naux-runner context, so on a service with no local docker every such exec\nwas refused with AuxContainerUnavailable, although preview and validation\nof the same file compose fine.\n\nstage() now runs inside _aux_runner_context, held and keyed on the source\nwith the preview tag, so a file previewed and then exec''d shares one warm\ncontainer. A bare-image exec composes nothing and still starts nothing.\n\n* Say that exec_in_container''s config_name names a configuration, not a file\n\nThe source picks the .vast (a workspace''s config_path, or what a campaign recorded);\nconfig_name picks one of the configurations it expands into, as preview_configurations\nnames them. docs/mcp.rst shows the lookup and a check of one configuration against both\nsources.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqt+LoCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAASoQAFMCIMxRPXpVEn2K1dFDwdNf