773b94c45d9032b7853","sha":"a981dc71016a489c1be7f773b94c45d9032b7853","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/commits/a981dc71016a489c1be7f773b94c45d9032b7853"}],"sha":"2118ecacb242e5fffb67dbbdc5a16987bc69039e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/commits/2118ecacb242e5fffb67dbbdc5a16987bc69039e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83823539?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fred-labs","id":83823539,"login":"fred-labs","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzODIzNTM5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/commits/a981dc71016a489c1be7f773b94c45d9032b7853/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-26T14:59:54Z","email":"fred-labs@mailbox.org","name":"fred-labs"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-26T14:59:54Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"A running campaign whose batch has finished every run is not called queued (#707)\n\nstall_report withheld its verdict for a campaign flagged as waiting for\ncluster capacity and said \"every job of the current batch is queued ...\nnone can complete\" -- without comparing the batch''s finished runs with its\ntotal. A capacity-wait flag that outlives the batch''s last run therefore\nproduced that sentence about a batch whose runs had all finished, while the\ncampaign was collecting results or moving on to postprocessing.\n\nA batch whose runs have all finished (completed plus no_result reaches\ntotal) now gets its own verdict ahead of the capacity one: no verdict is\npossible, since no run is left for the per-run budget to measure, and the\ntext says the campaign is doing its work after the runs. The same case\nwithout a capacity wait is no longer judged against the per-run budget\neither, for the reason the non-running phases are not.","tree":{"sha":"818c73491b4846ae96d49822f5c47512d6c1f3d6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/git/trees/818c73491b4846ae96d49822f5c47512d6c1f3d6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/git/commits/a981dc71016a489c1be7f773b94c45d9032b7853","verification":{"payload":"tree 818c73491b4846ae96d49822f5c47512d6c1f3d6\nparent 86a553389212c20675d4b7dd01705ee70deeaf6d\nauthor fred-labs <fred-labs@mailbox.org> 1790434794 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790434794 +0200\n\nA running campaign whose batch has finished every run is not called queued (#707)\n\nstall_report withheld its verdict for a campaign flagged as waiting for\ncluster capacity and said \"every job of the current batch is queued ...\nnone can complete\" -- without comparing the batch''s finished runs with its\ntotal. A capacity-wait flag that outlives the batch''s last run therefore\nproduced that sentence about a batch whose runs had all finished, while the\ncampaign was collecting results or moving on to postprocessing.\n\nA batch whose runs have all finished (completed plus no_result reaches\ntotal) now gets its own verdict ahead of the capacity one: no verdict is\npossible, since no run is left for the per-run budget to measure, and the\ntext says the campaign is doing its work after the runs. The same case\nwithout a capacity wait is no longer judged against the per-run budget\neither, for the reason the non-running phases are not.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqt93qCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAt+YQAGlLXz7LGYeQiKg5V3gTMYJH\nQRuqb12uvp67S9I1knHe1SnxtMps0RO0VF1nuzVTvPpu+Ec+sf5gcJ5OWyclka1q\ne9hJX4cFcxsorjJI0t43bMjjyXYonqLAoTGoU67KJxAmVjxI1uASCfAM5aB3/+GZ\n5Myak7kBL36rc5dtRqMdFiQO+rSo/SpJMclOanF68mdAV7l3gGQDs8AOadaV7THF\nmR+cNwIcpF9Fwi1HTvAJsNUpeltVHsIH9Onf19BoCyxDirGcSyLP1lomFYq98EUR\nZUw1yPRQ+OLWJG4GAVFG5BaHVRbuMsgS2TdsMI+qa8n0yF30i6I5ifyMuXggBXDh\nl4BvWupGa5TXeYU4EnLsGkilySwrgzJWAAVgmH23Vu+AhZviB6Tk4ucPVFbtxWdt\nU/sGNaMUwDmwmzVoqP83E0TYgjIGEmVnTbSfrU1xxWc4xO3XSzDz2mYYqZq7FiFR\nkZokgl0SPl/3NY4Z/3w/xVkwhpMe0+1MDaJ/eaMHGev7sucr8er6o7TZ056uPDj9\nGQRXb6BMdHW/nnrAezR6M6Wtl+X7zuGetWYmSJzmrIvzrIl4+pkEpp4TZ2DEH1nD\nizYA74PiUFApHcFxJpEZmxJjCPxfho98cEfOIMEY1dccKnt9EvHgkN0927F6EK8U\nCWmxbzSDt8ujoRagJd8D\n=Rf6b\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-26T14:59:55Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cps-test-lab/robovast/commit/a981dc71016a489c1be7f773b94c45d9032b7853","node_id":"C_kwDOPVaL7doAKGE5ODFkYzcxMDE2YTQ4OWMxYmU3Zjc3M2I5NGM0NWQ5MDMyYjc4NTM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cps-test-lab/robovast/commit/86a553389212c20675d4b7dd01705ee70deeaf6d","sha":"86a553389212c20675d4b7dd01705ee70deeaf6d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/commits/86a553389212c20675d4b7dd01705ee70deeaf6d"}],"sha":"a981dc71016a489c1be7f773b94c45d9032b7853","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/commits/a981dc71016a489c1be7f773b94c45d9032b7853"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83823539?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fred-labs","id":83823539,"login":"fred-labs","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzODIzNTM5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/commits/86a553389212c20675d4b7dd01705ee70deeaf6d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-26T14:58:18Z","email":"fred-labs@mailbox.org","name":"fred-labs"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-26T14:58:18Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"A simulation screenshot is kept and addressable, not only inline (#708)\n\nget_simulation_screenshot returned the render as inline image content and\nthen deleted it, and the POST route deleted its copy once the response was\nsent. An image that exists only inline in a reply cannot be attached,\nsaved or handed on, so a caller that needed the file had to render again\nthrough a route it could not keep either.\n\nThe service now keeps each render in a bounded store (ROBOVAST_SCREENSHOTS,\ndefault ~/.robovast/cache/screenshots): a render stays for 24 hours after\nit was made and at most 200 are kept, the oldest removed first, pruned\neach time one is kept. It is named by a fresh random id and served at\nGET /campaigns/<id>/screenshots/<name>; the POST response names it in\nContent-Location. campaign_screenshot returns a ScreenshotFrame carrying\nthe local path and that name, the HTTP client reads the name off the\nheader, and resolve_campaign_screenshot backs the route (refused by name\nover HTTP, as the scene-asset resolver is). The MCP tool returns the image\nand, beside it, {url, kept_for_s}, with url built the way read_file''s is\nand omitted when there is no origin or nothing was kept.","tree":{"sha":"e93b59d00b459f47bad813688c4ef546415db815","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/git/trees/e93b59d00b459f47bad813688c4ef546415db815"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/git/commits/86a553389212c20675d4b7dd01705ee70deeaf6d","verification":{"payload":"tree e93b59d00b459f47bad813688c4ef546415db815\nparent 5f4417a20f010b059f6e4d33453f39b9ebbcd82d\nauthor fred-labs <fred-labs@mailbox.org> 1790434698 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790434698 +0200\n\nA simulation screenshot is kept and addressable, not only inline (#708)\n\nget_simulation_screenshot returned the render as inline image content and\nthen deleted it, and the POST route deleted its copy once the response was\nsent. An image that exists only inline in a reply cannot be attached,\nsaved or handed on, so a caller that needed the file had to render again\nthrough a route it could not keep either.\n\nThe service now keeps each render in a bounded store (ROBOVAST_SCREENSHOTS,\ndefault ~/.robovast/cache/screenshots): a render stays for 24 hours after\nit was made and at most 200 are kept, the oldest removed first, pruned\neach time one is kept. It is named by a fresh random id and served at\nGET /campaigns/<id>/screenshots/<name>; the POST response names it in\nContent-Location. campaign_screenshot returns a ScreenshotFrame carrying\nthe local path and that name, the HTTP client reads the name off the\nheader, and resolve_campaign_screenshot backs the route (refused by name\nover HTTP, as the scene-asset resolver is). The MCP tool returns the image\nand, beside it, {url, kept_for_s}, with url built the way read_file''s is\nand omitted when there is no origin or nothing was kept.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqt92KCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAchQQAHAZ1MHVJHFT7GxNPsAzZcgu\nr0EcrdKPJMl5046EYLIvjIC+ms0+65tJ72XuiXKXQUQQoxN9UnuNZdfy/aXlgoW0\n83udb92DROpvmzPhaivL5yHCfoeHlvmGq5GuQh8ppAIoWEuIDR01XvBQZCafRkZb\n//KacDISFHjtGnRbO5QtHYQoX9lgq/rvMRZc8EZA8yhyFXnxXAdLxIBlqaGe2ePp\nX4Q9CwrDk9hagOBe+fCG8uC8LAfEwiVBzQgSDFiu0V3pDIMxxEMyVvjCMUK2AKwj\nWavrew4VFUllUIrHsU0aPAJ12bkxqHfDIRZg+3vAHdmr//g+NvIdGo/vQVzA2onh\nFDtbXpYF+lpnS710ViWZq3ZHjOwUlzGTpVPU9uPe8dcPlRrYu57k5m6Rr6pU8NC4\nFLdiveOKgW5njgjBY7+LtVoKYvqA6I92Pm5UJavfVPi5Gav8iXCfcm3lswv1kxUQ\n59dUyOeQmbGWfMPpVl6KKXfmCq7jyWPidpvuSOR3KURSIyxF5CjBm2KruqFyjoeM\nxk5DMJjlJMraDjxXAY7LlQe6c5KnfNaPmVmbhHBGSQq8XxWWaXL3e2rYrCVyti1d\nXSnGNgfn6RCrWFIkEEVb4m/vCGDmkXVOPC9aQUm4h1vcerFHjMbxWuNTYWtCNWBT\n18ja1dvncbDgbIKgmlO1\n=ccUv\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-26T14:58:19Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com