tarred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/commits/5f4417a20f010b059f6e4d33453f39b9ebbcd82d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-26T14:54:26Z","email":"fred-labs@mailbox.org","name":"fred-labs"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-26T14:54:26Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"MCP start_campaign takes the image tag the CLI''s --image-project-tag sets (#709)\n\nThe CLI passes --image-project-tag to the service as the request''s\nimage_project_tag, but the MCP start_campaign tool exposed no such\nparameter. An MCP-started campaign therefore resolved RoboVAST family\nimages at the service''s own tag -- often a floating one -- with no way to\npin a release for a run that must be reproducible.\n\nstart_campaign now takes image_project_tag and passes it on the create\nrequest; with from_campaign it is refused by name, as the other arguments\na retrigger replays from its record are. Documented in mcp.rst and in the\nprecedence list in images.rst.","tree":{"sha":"62390cc5753e02a67753138ed2e653b7b093217d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/git/trees/62390cc5753e02a67753138ed2e653b7b093217d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/git/commits/5f4417a20f010b059f6e4d33453f39b9ebbcd82d","verification":{"payload":"tree 62390cc5753e02a67753138ed2e653b7b093217d\nparent 13b639344e79aae1bff5f3f299817265c8841c80\nauthor fred-labs <fred-labs@mailbox.org> 1790434466 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790434466 +0200\n\nMCP start_campaign takes the image tag the CLI''s --image-project-tag sets (#709)\n\nThe CLI passes --image-project-tag to the service as the request''s\nimage_project_tag, but the MCP start_campaign tool exposed no such\nparameter. An MCP-started campaign therefore resolved RoboVAST family\nimages at the service''s own tag -- often a floating one -- with no way to\npin a release for a run that must be reproducible.\n\nstart_campaign now takes image_project_tag and passes it on the create\nrequest; with from_campaign it is refused by name, as the other arguments\na retrigger replays from its record are. Documented in mcp.rst and in the\nprecedence list in images.rst.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqt9yiCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAtKIQAE7T95tQA1RE2trGbepUNCXA\nNK4MmOTbeLkKWo+N4R0fw15thmjtIXom5kDK8yO+rFOG7QhAanXK4+T8Bi+WW5Lx\nksFfy13Oa+Lhc2oUVU8UdPaB/IwTz9CmgSFgRiP7PQSRnYPgHTLpTD/sEkHi1x7u\nX9Mg3A46WmEhTBup3wWm/68Lumw7t2pECJPbgKfKEpdJ6NR6qkv98v78Zf7JlpyM\ndEDCYgoGoRKg6ZUk+y/fuN5ZFxa40sdOPCaGnLKDZB84i9RFORdyJlvJLm+17il0\ncAMAtbE0778upDzCz3OR9ziTxDMhgx0s8NMLncwRlmf5QqMJQsSL1ihBzlSMPF0i\nA9PZjkY7SyKE8xQeLwKID6FdDKfdlkDq4Yq+iqoEG/2OzFnwmKSuwPDaPPQPS3Sj\n4iYxttdOsukRlXSrkRBtau+zQhGBdF3LWc5vN6Jh6g3MRB5rVEqVGY3gcoYs0eT+\n1nRvZ8O8VHYDUlSPNEym29lPPsMczII9aj9Xoy/qcbYlc1W8NoQxP6Ppt0eyLCQS\nHLOrCjIJxUc2tPqvuTSL4uy0UrM7V9c+hHzfxWOqCVuaFXTm63eLxoKN1Ku/xrEf\nt+FN2jkoUC375nc2hGyBYyqLCa8jLLk6mqfaDYozdIhiAHuZQcqgRjNU2lfozZll\n8hhV8DBPzeKViyQdd5tO\n=h8Bl\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-26T14:54:26Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cps-test-lab/robovast/commit/5f4417a20f010b059f6e4d33453f39b9ebbcd82d","node_id":"C_kwDOPVaL7doAKDVmNDQxN2EyMGYwMTBiMDU5ZjZlNGQzMzQ1M2YzOWI5ZWJiY2Q4MmQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cps-test-lab/robovast/commit/13b639344e79aae1bff5f3f299817265c8841c80","sha":"13b639344e79aae1bff5f3f299817265c8841c80","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/commits/13b639344e79aae1bff5f3f299817265c8841c80"}],"sha":"5f4417a20f010b059f6e4d33453f39b9ebbcd82d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/commits/5f4417a20f010b059f6e4d33453f39b9ebbcd82d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83823539?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fred-labs","id":83823539,"login":"fred-labs","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzODIzNTM5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/commits/13b639344e79aae1bff5f3f299817265c8841c80/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-26T14:13:57Z","email":"fred-labs@mailbox.org","name":"fred-labs"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-26T14:13:57Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"The world check reports what the simulator warns about a world''s start state (#715)\n\nA world whose reset state puts one body inside another loads, compiles\nand passes validate_project, and the contact solver then flings the\nbodies apart on the first steps of every run -- a failure that surfaces\nlater and looks like a controller or protocol fault.\n\nThe describe the world check asks for now resets the world when the\nsimulator supports it, and its reply carries `warnings`, each\n{check, message, hint} in the simulator''s words (roqsim: two bodies\nplaced inside one another). Each becomes an `advice` problem naming the\nworld, the check, the message and the hint, so `valid` is unchanged:\nthe simulator does not refuse such a world either, and an overlap may\nbe intended. Nothing here knows which checks a simulator has. A reset\nthat raises comes back as `errors.reset` and is an error, since no run\nof that world reaches its first step. An image whose simulator reports\nno `warnings` is described exactly as before.\n\ndescribe_world carries the same `warnings` on every surface -- the\ninterface model, the service, the MCP tool, the CLI and the generated\nAPI types -- and `vast workspace world` prints them. It also prints\neach component under its `address` again rather than the `key` the\nsimulator''s reply no longer has.","tree":{"sha":"b9503fcb76b8d2800c8408a1db520522cb1ce69e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/git/trees/b9503fcb76b8d2800c8408a1db520522cb1ce69e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/git/commits/13b639344e79aae1bff5f3f299817265c8841c80","verification":{"payload":"tree b9503fcb76b8d2800c8408a1db520522cb1ce69e\nparent e12d77bf9d4f5d10b486730070ee5a44f21cbfcd\nauthor fred-labs <fred-labs@mailbox.org> 1790432037 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790432037 +0200\n\nThe world check reports what the simulator warns about a world''s start state (#715)\n\nA world whose reset state puts one body inside another loads, compiles\nand passes validate_project, and the contact solver then flings the\nbodies apart on the first steps of every run -- a failure that surfaces\nlater and looks like a controller or protocol fault.\n\nThe describe the world check asks for now resets the world when the\nsimulator supports it, and its reply carries `warnings`, each\n{check, message, hint} in the simulator''s words (roqsim: two bodies\nplaced inside one another). Each becomes an `advice` problem naming the\nworld, the check, the message and the hint, so `valid` is unchanged:\nthe simulator does not refuse such a world either, and an overlap may\nbe intended. Nothing here knows which checks a simulator has. A reset\nthat raises comes back as `errors.reset` and is an error, since no run\nof that world reaches its first step. An image whose simulator reports\nno `warnings` is described exactly as before.\n\ndescribe_world carries the same `warnings` on every surface -- the\ninterface model, the service, the MCP tool, the CLI and the generated\nAPI types -- and `vast workspace world` prints them. It also prints\neach component under its `address` again rather than the `key` the\nsimulator''s reply no longer has.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqt9MlCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA+uMQAHx0EHVcSeHbeoN4hP6/4U/U\n23Z7qR3HOGSXyQNUGu2FdKoNS3g8Cxi3kYxMqXhsgQIQ0San252paSyteUQWrCZc\nkiSMbJy2yXMsihbBpV/2Su6Ho46He6vGRqmjNlqzWjyfn2bXFLkjjRxWwRAvAYaN\n80T0/5GKCDAezcS8yprMgq5/IB8WqndgA+SLHPBmSOjv0UVYVun2lMB7XDyLS+Mo\nt2SQ3Lr1rQ+x7HbDamNJYseaBnqiEVuq0taX3swkN1IszUDFsziRdA8r+MesWu3M\nYaLX6DPhCgBGngA/cUcGOs0C2Qsp4Krcx7xt5yYyrF+/SupjHYdvAjI7gME/LsOw\ntnwB7voN1Du2bPog14uqLUnHMDR1hdTkpZVDG4MQyTTcqntd3XoUWWMum67w1bfa\nTDUsgx4FGfPBIlqmMIODnwC/R91OB0wBOiNg7CNzeyt4K3qarqyjEXXFOGzmmVA9\nRu/GXgPkCQhZtaEh/N