acy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fred-labs","id":83823539,"login":"fred-labs","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzODIzNTM5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/commits/e12d77bf9d4f5d10b486730070ee5a44f21cbfcd/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-26T07:05:38Z","email":"fred-labs@mailbox.org","name":"fred-labs"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-26T07:05:38Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"An admission pass is linear in the queue and reads the cluster outside its lock (#699)\n\n* An admission pass is linear in the queue, not quadratic\n\nEvery campaign''s poll drains the whole global queue under the queue''s\nlock. For each item it refused, the pass recounted that owner''s PLANNED\nitems by walking the queue again, and on a full cluster nearly every\nitem is refused -- so a pass was quadratic in the queue depth. A deep\nqueue then held the lock for seconds per pass, and with several\ncampaigns polling, every service call that reads the queue waited\nbehind it.\n\nThe pass now counts each owner''s PLANNED items once and lowers the\ncount as it creates them.\n\nA test counts item reads over one refusing drain at two queue depths,\nso the guard is deterministic rather than timed.\n\n* An admission pass reads the cluster outside the queue''s lock (#700)\n\nEvery campaign''s poll drains the global queue, and each drain read the\ncluster''s budget -- a pod listing across all namespaces and a node\nlisting -- while holding the queue''s lock. Every status and refusal read\nand every other campaign''s poll waited out that API round trip.\n\nThe drain now checks under the lock whether anything is placeable, reads\nthe budget with the lock released, and takes the lock again to place.\nThe in-flight ledger is applied to the reading under the lock, so a job\nanother pass created meanwhile is still charged through the ledger and\none released meanwhile is at worst still charged by the reading. When\ntwo passes store readings out of order, the one asked for later is kept.\nA drain with nothing to place still reads nothing.\n\nThe paused-campaign refusal counts each owner''s planned items in one\npass rather than walking the queue once per paused owner.","tree":{"sha":"a0890c421903c43ca0eac4e37cecb0843725edce","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/git/trees/a0890c421903c43ca0eac4e37cecb0843725edce"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/git/commits/e12d77bf9d4f5d10b486730070ee5a44f21cbfcd","verification":{"payload":"tree a0890c421903c43ca0eac4e37cecb0843725edce\nparent 0aae64b58c963de104414f493749f2be8b5ba3a9\nauthor fred-labs <fred-labs@mailbox.org> 1790406338 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790406338 +0200\n\nAn admission pass is linear in the queue and reads the cluster outside its lock (#699)\n\n* An admission pass is linear in the queue, not quadratic\n\nEvery campaign''s poll drains the whole global queue under the queue''s\nlock. For each item it refused, the pass recounted that owner''s PLANNED\nitems by walking the queue again, and on a full cluster nearly every\nitem is refused -- so a pass was quadratic in the queue depth. A deep\nqueue then held the lock for seconds per pass, and with several\ncampaigns polling, every service call that reads the queue waited\nbehind it.\n\nThe pass now counts each owner''s PLANNED items once and lowers the\ncount as it creates them.\n\nA test counts item reads over one refusing drain at two queue depths,\nso the guard is deterministic rather than timed.\n\n* An admission pass reads the cluster outside the queue''s lock (#700)\n\nEvery campaign''s poll drains the global queue, and each drain read the\ncluster''s budget -- a pod listing across all namespaces and a node\nlisting -- while holding the queue''s lock. Every status and refusal read\nand every other campaign''s poll waited out that API round trip.\n\nThe drain now checks under the lock whether anything is placeable, reads\nthe budget with the lock released, and takes the lock again to place.\nThe in-flight ledger is applied to the reading under the lock, so a job\nanother pass created meanwhile is still charged through the ledger and\none released meanwhile is at worst still charged by the reading. When\ntwo passes store readings out of order, the one asked for later is kept.\nA drain with nothing to place still reads nothing.\n\nThe paused-campaign refusal counts each owner''s planned items in one\npass rather than walking the queue once per paused owner.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqt27CCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAxYoQAKNndykd1YS0jfNNaDwSKpcH\nsPi1VdWLIQ20zOTq3HhMJBh9ejXNfwl/H2nqaE2n+AyenooKZZNXRJVdzHDlZ45n\nIC2hS04gBf+dlxMLfxDdUS6tM1VFJNo9KnKfr6GDfn36LLNNHx5lq9PtRGgfsROE\n8q/ol5ed/jC3gSGO5cXplA5wpeHLWkSYYlqUGzGhvk4HvI3L+g0P9RY7qCqj1ByV\nBWuaCUZ8hXxXGcp8mnisuFGO3TSYkdgKdRrvuFPMFA2gj15L0ufnVigpfVfZQQA5\nvZgVzDInfl5gcPkYbayJollT0E91OfN12hZLVtkeT+gxwuKFk9z915DHbroJSEW7\nMa2A7+wuAoq9Iwqt9Epk68FlQ5ZFgAbLW6PkAjEMaKUwuzHYoNc+LapW2VF+ucuW\nfyt/0TNfW63TOoWnZemisqlPvCX9dUYMMQo4liI4xOOFZk37A8HicbpXJrtWPAQ5\nAo3Mu3fs/KgzrihHesQ43gj9yDGrGG8/stogO3FOXKpfb8vPKOJ9ZzgcJZpudTtg\noByA7+Dne5d+ng40tRMwS5DHp6BGktBcNkD/tds/0EWJ9wI+TE8O7FhmiPFIGxfo\nKzMrs5mtiItjBU0+cpvOo7t36G1wWRM