_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fred-labs","id":83823539,"login":"fred-labs","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzODIzNTM5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/commits/0aae64b58c963de104414f493749f2be8b5ba3a9/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-25T06:27:43Z","email":"fred-labs@mailbox.org","name":"fred-labs"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-25T06:27:43Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"An archived campaign is read as archived on the exec path too (#692)\n\nReading a campaign''s own ``_config/`` has a policy, and ``validate_config`` states it: a\nworkspace is editable, so an undeclared key there is a misspelling worth refusing, while an\narchived campaign already ran, cannot be edited, and refusing a key it ran without makes a\nfinished campaign unreadable rather than catching anything. Three readers follow it. The\nexec path does not, and it is the one that answers \"what did that run actually see?\" -- so\na campaign carrying a key the schema has since retired cannot be opened at all, and its\nowner has no edit available, because the file is the record.\n\nBoth of its reads now take the lenient policy when the source is a campaign, and the strict\none when it is a workspace. The refusal is unchanged for authoring and launching, which is\nwhere a retired key is worth a hard stop: there the file can still be fixed.","tree":{"sha":"afbfa7850838afa206da55ac60afec7e4f02811f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/git/trees/afbfa7850838afa206da55ac60afec7e4f02811f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/git/commits/0aae64b58c963de104414f493749f2be8b5ba3a9","verification":{"payload":"tree afbfa7850838afa206da55ac60afec7e4f02811f\nparent 230d150029fbd7993e4022bad080c2b4bb9d527c\nauthor fred-labs <fred-labs@mailbox.org> 1790317663 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790317663 +0200\n\nAn archived campaign is read as archived on the exec path too (#692)\n\nReading a campaign''s own ``_config/`` has a policy, and ``validate_config`` states it: a\nworkspace is editable, so an undeclared key there is a misspelling worth refusing, while an\narchived campaign already ran, cannot be edited, and refusing a key it ran without makes a\nfinished campaign unreadable rather than catching anything. Three readers follow it. The\nexec path does not, and it is the one that answers \"what did that run actually see?\" -- so\na campaign carrying a key the schema has since retired cannot be opened at all, and its\nowner has no edit available, because the file is the record.\n\nBoth of its reads now take the lenient policy when the source is a campaign, and the strict\none when it is a workspace. The refusal is unchanged for authoring and launching, which is\nwhere a retired key is worth a hard stop: there the file can still be fixed.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqthRfCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA7AoQAKXRYQKc84hqrdzsoP/4jcsf\nWuznbN8dVNzoJCiLI1snsjMwakXhuEbBLXgdhVBjmVIXPE3iy5FC4bxS/gNFOS9m\n0ZIrxm0WwpBgqDBcTnTUZgtKTOg/rqpCYuydTQuYGBP2HL2YFuiaVw3ZWacQryuE\nJTMXgpc1Yoz3rjX2ID1MCUUChfDM0mb52uYPwXkN0U0sF8ABtR9biDwlWAOHNFoX\nMaqFS/764AOdVURmwZz0jijVINoiP/ZZayfAQMuQX+gqWIUPnOfcCdIcPmzplkqI\nqOT+yHBd1Q9KpR1g6SK36ry9I8jKrHCN/hoTrx7zbWLxM11OwJFUZw8Qm6e4FV/s\n4RQ3WL5aaGBXjw7R5Kl1Upp8/xEPbZbAHle1k2PSF0dUKH+neusOr+7Hzvh7QPkr\n5tPelFu6vY2VdADd1kjkVbHmcqbEpTNsl8IZyKWA3cq1GK