bs/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/commits/8651c9966723f9d269abe4e013286823b2ac15dd/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-24T15:03:19Z","email":"fred-labs@mailbox.org","name":"fred-labs"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-24T15:03:19Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"A release''s changelog is the few changes a user must know about (#693)\n\n* The changelog check refuses a merge cited twice\n\nThe skill says every merge in the range is cited exactly once and that the check enforces it,\nbut the check only asked that each was cited at all. A merge in two entries is one change told\ntwice, or two changes that belong on one line; either way the section is not minimal. The\ncheck now names every merge cited more than once.\n\n* The skill writes the section''s parts as headings the linter accepts\n\nBold lines used as headings are refused by the repository''s Markdown lint, and a line that starts with a merge number reads as a heading without its space. The skill now asks for level-three headings and an Internal sentence that starts with words.\n\n* No space inside the heading marker''s code span\n\nThe linter refuses a code span with a trailing space.\n\n* A release''s changelog is the few changes a user must know about\n\nA section that cited every merge read as the git history retold, a hundred lines for a user who\nneeds to know what to change and what they can now do. The section is now one flat list of at\nmost fifteen entries, each a bold topic and one line on what changed, citations optional and\nnever counted toward its length. There is no Internal entry: refactors, tests, CI and pin bumps\nstay in the history, where a reader who wants them already looks.\n\ncheck holds a section to that shape: entries, at most fifteen, each ''- **Topic** — ...'' and at\nmost 160 characters before its citations, no headings or prose between them, and no number\nthat is not a merge in the range. The completeness and cited-once rules are gone with the\nshape that needed them.\n\n* A changelog cites its pull requests as links, and lists only what a user would want to hear\n\nA number in rendered release notes leads nowhere. collect now prints the link to cite each\nmerge by -- its pull request, or its commit where it had none -- read from the GitHub\nrepository origin names, and check refuses a bare number, a link into another repository and\na link to a different number than it names. check needs to know the repository for that, so\nwithout a GitHub origin it asks for --repository rather than passing unchecked links.\n\nFifteen entries is a ceiling. The skill says so: a release with four changes a user would want\nto hear about has four entries, and none is added to fill the list.","tree":{"sha":"df478b284df0e6f3cee973c4d6397a59bf630196","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/git/trees/df478b284df0e6f3cee973c4d6397a59bf630196"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/git/commits/8651c9966723f9d269abe4e013286823b2ac15dd","verification":{"payload":"tree df478b284df0e6f3cee973c4d6397a59bf630196\nparent ff1fa1b0fdcd5c2d74f9feadb1020d5b06c59bf5\nauthor fred-labs <fred-labs@mailbox.org> 1790262199 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790262199 +0200\n\nA release''s changelog is the few changes a user must know about (#693)\n\n* The changelog check refuses a merge cited twice\n\nThe skill says every merge in the range is cited exactly once and that the check enforces it,\nbut the check only asked that each was cited at all. A merge in two entries is one change told\ntwice, or two changes that belong on one line; either way the section is not minimal. The\ncheck now names every merge cited more than once.\n\n* The skill writes the section''s parts as headings the linter accepts\n\nBold lines used as headings are refused by the repository''s Markdown lint, and a line that starts with a merge number reads as a heading without its space. The skill now asks for level-three headings and an Internal sentence that starts with words.\n\n* No space inside the heading marker''s code span\n\nThe linter refuses a code span with a trailing space.\n\n* A release''s changelog is the few changes a user must know about\n\nA section that cited every merge read as the git history retold, a hundred lines for a user who\nneeds to know what to change and what they can now do. The section is now one flat list of at\nmost fifteen entries, each a bold topic and one line on what changed, citations optional and\nnever counted toward its length. There is no Internal entry: refactors, tests, CI and pin bumps\nstay in the history, where a reader who wants them already looks.\n\ncheck holds a section to that shape: entries, at most fifteen, each ''- **Topic** — ...'' and at\nmost 160 characters before its citations, no headings or prose between them, and no number\nthat is not a merge in the range. The completeness and cited-once rules are gone with the\nshape that needed them.\n\n* A changelog cites its pull requests as links, and lists only what a user would want to hear\n\nA number in rendered release notes leads nowhere. collect now prints the link to cite each\nmerge by -- its pull request, or its commit where it had none -- read from the GitHub\nrepository origin names, and check refuses a bare number, a link into another repository and\na link to a different number than it names. check needs to know the repository for that, so\nwithout a GitHub origin it asks for --repository rather than passing unchecked links.\n\nFifteen entries is a ceiling. The skill says so: a release with four changes a user would want\nto hear about has four entries, and none is added to fill the list.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqtTu3CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAANmoQAAriFqJWY7xIcsCehM++P0fz\nA3c2wf+PaKvLFs2mQ91cQxqd0BCzXIIc2ypv6EM0aMUlKJUUU1f9G62Q+IhBIcG4\nADvVfHzt4SXb9Wj0VZnTIT2jZz/w2tDajkHuGrArDSJ8FXwEX1xCcTNjUa5DXv1f\nxKRnQHIa/pahPtigQ838C45MnAuwBWdBGqpxQlnIsiwCDhHEbNoxtR35RlEp0IuJ\nGzl/CPgvAi3CPXpiEJhjPIlBQi68PcbFsI9eCSH7Iwm0m/UhtwlxLeiUJBTgQzXj\nfkRlwofyme3gX7B93ve/oRJtszLlBgm/5IM5MLSxqS9WVT32eNCw8N3HgXmnVHn7\n5bj600LTv4ORnbe5r/w8W9fuSKvKtFvLZJe3IiiOPyiPkZPiIf/EPnQSts/2OD5F\npNkJj2ySWjJPERK6HpwMNROYZf0GnHMolTEKWJD08Dx1v8UUfpuPtxuNOg3Ik27W\ny5KMuoo7O/n/EKZ7fo9Si2YrEtqD2IXil6KI9hnU3p7xJSn6lUyfpFwUrXkRqrq1\neK0G0zhDGP8sOKEuBAUxQp2yRYjCcEvLHx9XYVwm0YMWbREZf60ZzEcD3nZBdI3e\nh147OI3qOM2Vi8yfK5zRj4LPxvP7kd5qgUba87hIICXpkWJpQK4PtzkY0mgutD73\n8ETn/X+LZZ4NXWpvKuoC\n=wRTm\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-24T15:03:20Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cps-test-lab/robovast/commit/8651c9966723f9d269abe4e013286823b2ac15dd","node_id":"C_kwDOPVaL7doAKDg2NTFjOTk2NjcyM2Y5ZDI2OWFiZTRlMDEzMjg2ODIzYjJhYzE1ZGQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cps-test-lab/robovast/commit/ff1fa1b0fdcd5c2d74f9feadb1020d5b06c59bf5","sha":"ff1fa1b0fdcd5c2d74f9feadb1020d5b06c59bf5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/commits/ff1fa1b0fdcd5c2d74f9feadb1020d5b06c59bf5"}],"sha":"8651c9966723f9d269abe4e013286823b2ac15dd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/commits/8651c9966723f9d269abe4e013286823b2ac15dd"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83823539?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fred-labs","id":83823539,"login":"fred-labs","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzODIzNTM5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/commits/ff1fa1b0fdcd5c2d74f9feadb1020d5b06c59bf5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-24T15:02:28Z","email":"fred-labs@mailbox.org","name":"fred-labs"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-24T15:02:28Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Do not offer the self-upgrade on a deployment pinned to a version (#691)\n\n* Do not offer the self-upgrade on a deployment pinned to a version\n\nThe admin page''s Upgrade stamps the Deployment''s restart annotation, so\nthe new pod re-pulls the reference the Deployment already names. On a\ndeployment set up with a fixed ROBOVAST_PROJECT_TAG that either changes\nnothing or, on a tag that was re-pushed, lands on bytes the pin was\nchosen to keep out.\n\nupgrade_info now reports such a deployment as unsupported whenever its\nimage names anything but the floating tag (a release, a dated set, a\ndigest), with the way to move the pin: set ROBOVAST_PROJECT_TAG and run\n`vast service upgrade`. upgrade_service already refuses what\nupgrade_info does not support, force or not, and the page already shows\nthe reason in place of the button, so every client gets the same answer.\n\n* A branch''s image tag floats as latest does, so a deployment on one is still rolled\n\nCI publishes the family under `latest` and under the default branch''s name on every push to\nit, and under `pr-<n>` on every push to a pull request. All three move, and a roll is how a\ndeployment running one reaches what was pushed; only a release version, a date or a digest is\na version chosen for the deployment. is_floating_image_tag says which is which, beside the\nconstant it extends, and a test holds the branch tag to the one branch image.yml builds.","tree":{"sha":"6509c76b1f2f89b73e98a7cd3e49041c646b185c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/git/trees/6509c76b1f2f89b73e98a7cd3e49041c646b185c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/git/commits/ff1fa1b0fdcd5c2d74f9feadb1020d5b06c59bf5","verification":{"payload":"tree 6509c76b1f2f89b73e98a7cd3e49041c646b185c\nparent d564198103b6dd4516edb6b3eba67330ad2c1199\nauthor fred-labs <fred-labs@mailbox.org> 1790262148 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790262148 +0200\n\nDo not offer the self-upgrade on a deployment pinned to a version (#691)\n\n* Do not offer the self-upgrade on a deployment pinned to a version\n\nThe admin page''s Upgrade stamps the Deployment''s restart annotation, so\nthe new pod re-pulls the reference the Deployment already names. On a\ndeployment set up with a fixed ROBOVAST_PROJECT_TAG that either changes\nnothing or, on a tag that was re-pushed, lands on bytes the pin was\nchosen to keep out.\n\nupgrade_info now reports such a deployment as unsupported whenever its\nimage names anything but the floating tag (a release, a dated set, a\ndigest), with the way to move the pin: set ROBOVAST_PROJECT_TAG and run\n`vast service upgrade`. upgrade_service already refuses what\nupgrade_info does not support, force or not, and the page already shows\nthe reason in place of the button, so every client gets the same answer.\n\n* A branch''s image tag floats as latest does, so a deployment on one is still rolled\n\nCI publishes the family under `latest` and under the default branch''s name on every push to\nit, and under `pr-<n>` on every push to a pull request. All three move, and a roll is how a\ndeployment running one reaches what was pushed; only a release version, a date or a digest is\na version chosen for the deployment. is_floating_image_tag says which is which, beside the\nconstant it extends, and a test holds the branch tag to the one branch image.yml builds.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqtTuECRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAk5sQAA2oxpvORpoUbziYsoXzFFJl\nmbu0ge4Uv2vdbTfj7oeV8dogaWlWl2T0QMIaF2YWl0i4I3PCvlk84VkI/6AWckrt\nmzdScr9m/O8qdDH1jDaFujLptcMKuVln0BILmQdLa47PuyMryZ2HhS0SMgYPCoDP\nHoFskSjrWuDAZmvB6kd0fb6q2kPAhO2Z2tvwIR0lj80+wTd/eLly/l9rrAsY6/87\nXX1GPMXuv6uo5vl4VGbQwXrJwH1D+Q9fhD3/RFf4mwY+CwxIto9XfIo9+tBqA96h\n4ZC2GGFIJ/pevF+5XUGpX323eTZQJCSg+M7DZrug9f7Zet5MCMmGPpgjLUwG1ZLG\nlR/Q6plQ4C0U19p/ZCdOYB6yLNJU206Cl1FOt/IhLAaDVeeeubwv457X8HbyyZfR\nUJ7mtCVgZWRGFMWdDliPjWx/UIUaQ+S4p5aRKmijrk+Pvb1uBm2kPgfGvP3DDoQt\nDjsp96Sg4BAEv3i3azXdgYUkYCxI1Jw/js6MeNlrAYBtpTEMJ14DCRJ8coAie5vz\nSuvPmRzkmbhBekZ