ollowers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fred-labs","id":83823539,"login":"fred-labs","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzODIzNTM5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/commits/d564198103b6dd4516edb6b3eba67330ad2c1199/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-24T13:56:37Z","email":"fred-labs@mailbox.org","name":"fred-labs"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-24T13:56:37Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"A changelog skill: the release''s section from the merges since the last tag, reviewed before it is committed (#674)\n\nThe only notes a release had were a GitHub Release body written after the tag. Every merge\non main is a squash commit carrying its pull request''s title, number and description, so\ngit alone holds what a changelog is written from.\n\nskills/changelog/changelog.py collects one block per merge in the range (number, title,\nfirst paragraph, areas of the tree touched), checks that a version''s CHANGELOG.md section\ncites every merge in the range and nothing outside it, and prints the section as the\nrelease body. SKILL.md fixes the section''s shape -- Removed, Added, Changed, Fixed, Images\nand packaging, Internal -- one line per change a user notices, citing the merges that made\nit, and stops for the user''s review before anything is committed.\n\nAGENTS.md names CHANGELOG.md as the one place history lives, since every other page\ndescribes the is-state; the developer guide puts the section before the rc.","tree":{"sha":"e634a45d6423744c1fcd4aa6ed945ee5028d95a4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/git/trees/e634a45d6423744c1fcd4aa6ed945ee5028d95a4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/git/commits/d564198103b6dd4516edb6b3eba67330ad2c1199","verification":{"payload":"tree e634a45d6423744c1fcd4aa6ed945ee5028d95a4\nparent ee485e51dea361172d5450ef3f265afe6d106673\nauthor fred-labs <fred-labs@mailbox.org> 1790258197 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790258197 +0200\n\nA changelog skill: the release''s section from the merges since the last tag, reviewed before it is committed (#674)\n\nThe only notes a release had were a GitHub Release body written after the tag. Every merge\non main is a squash commit carrying its pull request''s title, number and description, so\ngit alone holds what a changelog is written from.\n\nskills/changelog/changelog.py collects one block per merge in the range (number, title,\nfirst paragraph, areas of the tree touched), checks that a version''s CHANGELOG.md section\ncites every merge in the range and nothing outside it, and prints the section as the\nrelease body. SKILL.md fixes the section''s shape -- Removed, Added, Changed, Fixed, Images\nand packaging, Internal -- one line per change a user notices, citing the merges that made\nit, and stops for the user''s review before anything is committed.\n\nAGENTS.md names CHANGELOG.md as the one place history lives, since every other page\ndescribes the is-state; the developer guide puts the section before the rc.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqtSwVCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAOeIQAFa0afhLk12swQx5m98rZ4Cf\nPpE2Vj9yPQQh21hNz+JlDsef9DongmYLyGTvEfFuD6LGCA+HU9EaHwG/T5iwNEzX\nZOvLApw64cnlsMxIQSKiP5a8CLlyPTDB/MwL6o6Lmb8L7GKNRRqNnWXtEGm6FjgH\npliuTbylcCe7SL3WVHwSmxB/mHIYHSQ7hidn11OCynL5