"sha":"a88fdecb745ffcca2c9646e7f105b41afe546af3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/commits/a88fdecb745ffcca2c9646e7f105b41afe546af3"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83823539?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fred-labs","id":83823539,"login":"fred-labs","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzODIzNTM5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/commits/5c0852fcfa01c0626a49f406708fd813207195bc/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-24T10:30:25Z","email":"fred-labs@mailbox.org","name":"fred-labs"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-24T10:30:25Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Our own log lines carry their level, so a severity filter can find them (#690)\n\nThe line prefix was parsed for the shape a ROS node writes and for nothing else. A campaign''s\ninfrastructure log is written by our own logging, which wears the stdlib''s stamp, so every\nline of it read as unmarked and fell to the keyword scan -- which is wrong in both\ndirections. An ERROR of ours classified as a warning, so asking a failed campaign for its\nsevere lines returned none while the log said on its own line what had failed; and an INFO\nof ours that merely relays the word \"error\" classified as a warning too, which is the false\npositive a level marker exists to prevent.\n\nThat stamp is now parsed like the other two, for its level, its logger and its timestamp,\nso a line of ours is classified by the verdict it states. A line wearing no stamp at all\nstill falls to the keyword scan: a bash echo has no level, and giving it one would invent a\nverdict its producer never gave.\n\nThe postprocessing verdict is assembled into the campaign''s section rather than logged, so\nit carried no stamp to read. It is now written wearing one.","tree":{"sha":"dd30fbcb0efa48a8dec578dd3f556b0e7a53982a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/git/trees/dd30fbcb0efa48a8dec578dd3f556b0e7a53982a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/git/commits/5c0852fcfa01c0626a49f406708fd813207195bc","verification":{"payload":"tree dd30fbcb0efa48a8dec578dd3f556b0e7a53982a\nparent 59572c05daa80c9a63c696e20b36a515ea567456\nauthor fred-labs <fred-labs@mailbox.org> 1790245825 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790245825 +0200\n\nOur own log lines carry their level, so a severity filter can find them (#690)\n\nThe line prefix was parsed for the shape a ROS node writes and for nothing else. A campaign''s\ninfrastructure log is written by our own logging, which wears the stdlib''s stamp, so every\nline of it read as unmarked and fell to the keyword scan -- which is wrong in both\ndirections. An ERROR of ours classified as a warning, so asking a failed campaign for its\nsevere lines returned none while the log said on its own line what had failed; and an INFO\nof ours that merely relays the word \"error\" classified as a warning too, which is the false\npositive a level marker exists to prevent.\n\nThat stamp is now parsed like the other two, for its level, its logger and its timestamp,\nso a line of ours is classified by the verdict it states. A line wearing no stamp at all\nstill falls to the keyword scan: a bash echo has no level, and giving it one would invent a\nverdict its producer never gave.\n\nThe postprocessing verdict is assembled into the campaign''s section rather than logged, so\nit carried no stamp to read. It is now written wearing one.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqtPvBCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAgTQQAKsCGWe2kmIlKQcaLLrfAiuv\nu4jMR6IgvqZNWAQglRXIIk9rYdKRA0VhQuOs53hWZnq4IJJnVxqcbBMh7WnsiND7\noeVqX5DRyHLL9V1PO2yXSNJDCispXiMCeU3fBOlN5dDKTQRIuCEPOJBYeLzih/ka\npkaq1EChjcTxZnHTkX8mFsfpRny92pzImpMukqaGxF4kIKVXBH2hgxSPAj45cUKP\nduaR3HGNvZ+pE4PI/zMjXZzQJBNsdutWFVz3AFsw5EajWfno8PWSU73VxRaMf5cG\nvp20srGfyklZf3b41/N08/7tWzajfqPG0CAzj3ibT5wx55DeBmYsG61BXdkRDSGb\nddVHntNJSf50q8I6lEQJE53iEuUm0k0RxHYFvcMF/amaFK1rGb5n0kWDvJB4p4ca\nyDYnVQHQP3SZ//y5COF30e5Gtdiu/MVbmB3MjsSvXxPzFz8EMo8BZbL3/4B/Crpo\ndbiZQi8SFv8k2LIzEtPujyn+ZNdjEaRfmT4YcVYCjRFmb1P1N1X9jOF4TrWy/iTx\nJ11fIypkx8PotT78957YeRtlUA/9apsmqbK2Gvbtfpby2JMaqnTx/Xs7ySTs9BVZ\nZKoOgvn/B+uWTtecPbszOr1neylesonOLgENAjZP+m6CGVWTsj6tQC9yg5Bzt+VA\n0mwas+cmfwdXMjEmtJ8R\n=Gs3m\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-24T10:30:26Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cps-test-lab/robovast/commit/5c0852fcfa01c0626a49f406708fd813207195bc","node_id":"C_kwDOPVaL7doAKDVjMDg1MmZjZmEwMWMwNjI2YTQ5ZjQwNjcwOGZkODEzMjA3MTk1YmM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cps-test-lab/robovast/commit/59572c05daa80c9a63c696e20b36a515ea567456","sha":"59572c05daa80c9a63c696e20b36a515ea567456","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/commits/59572c05daa80c9a63c696e20b36a515ea567456"}],"sha":"5c0852fcfa01c0626a49f406708fd813207195bc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/commits/5c0852fcfa01c0626a49f406708fd813207195bc"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83823539?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fred-labs","id":83823539,"login":"fred-labs","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzODIzNTM5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/commits/59572c05daa80c9a63c696e20b36a515ea567456/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-24T10:29:57Z","email":"fred-labs@mailbox.org","name":"fred-labs"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-24T10:29:57Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"The part that failed keeps its log (#689)\n\nA postprocessing part delivers its log from the container that runs the steps, and the\nconverter runs ahead of that one as an init container -- so a part whose conversion fails\ndelivers nothing at all. The campaign''s section is rebuilt from what the parts delivered\nonce they are done, and a part with no file was skipped, which left the one part whose\noutput explains the failure as the one part absent from the section, and overwrote the live\noutput that had explained it.\n\nThe pods are still there when the verdict is taken, so that is where their logs are now\nread and kept for the parts that delivered none -- the last moment they can be read at all.\nA part that did deliver one keeps it: that file is the part''s own account of itself, and\nthis is a pod read taken afterwards. A part that still has no log is named in the section\nwith the reason, rather than left out of it, since a part silently absent reads as a part\nthat never ran.","tree":{"sha":"4599b26ae56ec414c26ac55f4d02b3dcd84a9837","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/git/trees/4599b26ae56ec414c26ac55f4d02b3dcd84a9837"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/git/commits/59572c05daa80c9a63c696e20b36a515ea567456","verification":{"payload":"tree 4599b26ae56ec414c26ac55f4d02b3dcd84a9837\nparent ab38ca0a7e7fbcef8dbdfd39d3d21787b05b3f4c\nauthor fred-labs <fred-labs@mailbox.org> 1790245797 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790245797 +0200\n\nThe part that failed keeps its log (#689)\n\nA postprocessing part delivers its log from the container that runs the steps, and the\nconverter runs ahead of that one as an init container -- so a part whose conversion fails\ndelivers nothing at all. The campaign''s section is rebuilt from what the parts delivered\nonce they are done, and a part with no file was skipped, which left the one part whose\noutput explains the failure as the one part absent from the section, and overwrote the live\noutput that had explained it.\n\nThe pods are still there when the verdict is taken, so that is where their logs are now\nread and kept for the parts that delivered none -- the last moment they can be read at all.\nA part that did deliver one keeps it: that file is the part''s own account of itself, and\nthis is a pod read taken afterwards. A part that still has no log is named in the section\nwith the reason, rather than left out of it, since a part silently absent reads as a part\nthat never ran.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqtPulCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAUoQQACYC/qNRdNMk3iI9gYOtj4+t\nHbQN4JLkQhmuLVpZYDyNXNrfsGZpPQG2PBf1mwejGxZb6bzBWZG8pT9OIMOsA+vo\nIG5VT0SG5jIS7bQiWnU5O32uh2xGgo6IFmwu19SlgQ+umZbkDQmIsNT0kE11c1hO\nRz1g/oWqdDjeFTAlD0xnwLdWNcncEHUBAJiZAKxI3LYrcNjkz5duO77aFFVgNOcO\nZtHpT/pZqzjjMGwKnD+9enTv8Ol2UhhmmbWXHoHVwOpbhAvKLuNvPu88h06qsazy\nUQmX8/+haiTe9U3PE/owj352nttzBoneQBz8yMSjcJcYF1AyiqkgcgnCisVRbGvr\nMyuFQTZ5U8zZMuMmjlFSlKOzDOk595nWi1FZhHl6ecPu0smD/wiOuG+iEnSXx2Jg\nVjJwhzF4NQK/5TevxgzwgmXJZbPe1XTUZTxhAoi3OdS5UsRwsT9pHcXCZQkrDHBI\n850iSeQbvJvzw4QGD6V0ac+RyqKB9FknJVh38zZ/MixGwAhGS4LCjSmaAt5bm6V6\nOtnV8deflTOSCGIu8p9SIU8KokU0gqiVHljBuBpXcwA7Szr6BM2dmlxC3dVn4t8C\nipcQIT0eD9GdbweTC3UQkifwK7JWWJ4i2FqfWyMcVID7cZDBH7Ep7F1Z89Wzi1oh\np/mHaeCT4r26SeJ2ls0t\n=9LC4\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-24T10:29:58Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cps-test-lab/robovast/commit/59572c05daa80c9a63c696e20b36a515ea567456","node_id":"C_kwDOPVaL7doAKDU5NTcyYzA1ZGFhODBjOWE2M2M2OTZlMjBiMzZhNTE1ZWE1Njc0NTY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cps-test-lab/robovast/commit/ab38ca0a7e7fbcef8dbdfd39d3d21787b05b3f4c","sha":"ab38ca0a7e7fbcef8dbdfd39d3d21787b05b3f4c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/commits/ab38ca0a7e7fbcef8dbdfd39d3d21787b05b3f4c"}],"sha":"59572c05daa80c9a63c696e20b36a515ea567456","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/commits/59572c05daa80c9a63c696e20b36a515ea567456"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83823539?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fred-labs","id":83823539,"login":"fred-labs","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzODIzNTM5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/commits/ab38ca0a7e7fbcef8dbdfd39d3d21787b05b3f4c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-24T10:29:29Z","email":"fred-labs@mailbox.org","name":"fred-labs"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-24T10:29:29Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"One fetch per image, not one per caller (#688)\n\nA catalog fetch costs a container and a whole catalog over the wire, and the cache is\nconsulted before it and written after, so nothing stops two callers who miss together from\neach starting their own. The miss that matters is the one at startup: a server warms the\ndocumentation corpus as it is constructed, and a question arriving while that runs fetched\nthe same corpus a second time -- two containers, at the moment the server has least to spare,\nfor an answer already on its way.\n\nCallers that miss the same image and catalog now queue on one lock, and the one that waited\nfinds the cache filled and is told it hit: no container ran for it, which is what the field\nis read for. One lock per key rather than one for all, because two images have nothing to\nwait for from each other and a fetch is seconds long, and it is held across the fetch, so a\nfetch that fails releases it and the next caller is free to try.","tree":{"sha":"001c5470e7218444c8bfe82bf8d5539f2011fdff","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/git/trees/001c5470e7218444c8bfe82bf8d5539f2011fdff"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/git/commits/ab38ca0a7e7fbcef8dbdfd39d3d21787b05b3f4c","verification":{"payload":"tree 001c5470e7218444c8bfe82bf8d5539f2011fdff\nparent 5f00f7af7cae8ee257d2a34625098cbea3b40bad\nauthor fred-labs <fred-labs@mailbox.org> 1790245769 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790245769 +0200\n\nOne fetch per image, not one per caller (#688)\n\nA catalog fetch costs a container and a whole catalog over the wire, and the cache is\nconsulted before it and written after, so nothing stops two callers who miss together from\neach starting their own. The miss that matters is the one at startup: a server warms the\ndocumentation corpus as it is constructed, and a question arriving while that runs fetched\nthe same corpus a second time -- two containers, at the moment the server has least to spare,\nfor an answer already on its way.\n\nCallers that miss the same image and catalog now queue on one lock, and the one that waited\nfinds the cache filled and is told it hit: no container ran for it, which is what the field\nis read for. One lock per key rather than one for all, because two images have nothing to\nwait for from each other and a fetch is seconds long, and it is held across the fetch, so a\nfetch that fails releases it and the next caller is free to try.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqtPuJCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAQe8QAFwXyk4mwc5hJ8SABSnjJvBH\n/Z8kGYAKjqpmHSIszuVCFnWJDig0ZneqwzJBRULLEbugM8Er0pnMCNurwuVeBX/N\n1E+heIt92+8uqHLRzyNK0AImVCNMLR+dYG1+dwxy1WuBe0BO1y8hZjFhxYRxo44X\nVdaYExkQuFr2MPGspl0crLeXkCj1jholD490bWtJj0JgXdaO5gHuacQtIdLCGZVz\n3npbOTn9wXVoc+/jwpoZE+nXfmONxvRcENXuGG+dn4rpxgeyV1z5vf2lW4ahwknX\nOhUMZvNiRWIlmxCgNEJ7c+3mOSkqHJF8qwPHsxvTI9IkFJUPuz9Bmx9gYkS1rmhy\nxyQJwDdTlmP9CdIPujE/5u6Xkh8p/95UvRpwMtt7XMXW5iczzHrAjn3oDKg1L066\nHXEPn5Rs70bcMSSL5VogB6+9rwQkhkHqfUArqgBmXmeRjSgVpjbZZAxXzh83gF8d\nlm6bh0v/OMsl1ABCoXZduD6Kvnm15OMteN3sVnd5qA+0YGZvITe2gyQPoMSNUnRz\n0TFzBwCB2PZfnbxvsX0P+7xHLPBvqlflOAHmIAsZY+KID+F737y8XRyE5Tvf0mTF\nnl+2xEkwpbPDWHlSGEbu2++xcExcKNOINBd1lOpoog0ZcKTlbAhvRkic6dQ6UDjx\nBcCoSTFlOHgjpqY0h2e6\n=XiVA\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-24T10:29:29Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}",