an before, and the check added beside it turns\nforgetting into a CI failure rather than a quiet divergence.\n\n`--set NAME_REF=<sha|branch|tag>` writes that pin wherever it appears and leaves every other\npin alone. A sha is taken as given; a branch or tag is resolved once against the repo the\npin names, so the same commit lands in every copy. `make source-pin PIN=ROQSIM_REF=main`.\n\nThe copies exist because each Dockerfile has to build on its own and Dockerfile.roqsim is\nbuilt with an empty context. That is the build''s business; it should not be the editor''s.\n\n* Read the simulator''s documentation out of the image that runs it\n\n`search_docs` served RoboVAST''s pages alone, so a search for a world''s `components:` list or\nthe scenario DSL returned nothing -- which reads as \"no such thing\" rather than \"not indexed\nhere\". With `address=/sources/<workspace_id>/<path>` it also serves the pages of the image\nthat `.vast` runs, under a `roqsim-` prefix.\n\nThe image already carries them: the simulator image copies roqsim''s source tree to\n/opt/roqsim, so its `docs/` is there to be read. `docs` joins the catalog commands, so the\nexec, the held container and the per-image cache are the ones the catalogs already use, and\nthe answer comes from the simulator THAT campaign pins rather than whichever version sits\nbeside the service. Nothing is added to an image and no commit is pinned twice.\n\nWithout an address nothing is fetched and the search costs what it did. A miss then names\nthe argument that reaches the rest, so zero results stop reading as \"there is no such thing\".\n\n`docs` is not in the tool''s catalog vocabulary: it is a command this reads, not a listing\nanyone asks for.\n\n* Name the address when a page of the image is read without it\n\nA search with an address returns names like `roqsim-interfaces`; reading one without the\naddress listed RoboVAST''s own pages and called it unknown, which is the answer this whole\nchange exists to remove.\n\n* Rank the corpus, and name the pages when excerpts would be a sample\n\nA search matched by substring and returned pages in name order, so the first result was\nthe first alphabetically and a common term answered with five excerpts from each of\ntwenty-seven pages -- about 15,000 tokens of arbitrary sample, with a note at the end\nsaying it was one.\n\nFTS5 with bm25() picks the pages and orders them; sqlite ships it, so this costs no\ndependency. A query becomes quoted prefix terms, ANDed, because a word may carry\npunctuation an operator would claim and a caller was never offered a query language.\n\nAbove a measured reply budget the excerpts go and the pages are named instead, best first,\nwith the call that reads one. `campaign` goes from ~15,700 tokens to ~297; `components`, at\nnine pages, still returns its excerpts.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqtNhmCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAhN0QAK3eLQk3PQIXN03bu7apFxJv\nMJ7oMe0Xf8G3cr/SoD4smvcdQ3RDDrSqoXbjPhHBqnncc3HPbevPNKsuKn93393q\noA3DemlM4H1gZ3inkTXERR/yGLDItUgLXhVbSqcGLyPCLiRVsSqrTOk3oS3WfaFM\n3zA7Qz3qnaou6Yp+n3iHgRqxrKdsaLdG+KFTPQLZetPuX9tbQwGrLX2MKj8RTDLa\nwGC5PDyWw+mc6yD/MpRburjH13Bp5fLnOX0dUff+NwGrZAhE9EjpKqtRzniB2rA3\n/qmmLmYDDOIkDU/1/dPwOHQqGUzShckwSEcaUhVohLkDHeLzP6VODIZ+XhX51HVu\n+lN2Gc32KEBO10eI4RaYLEnLSKHM5D+8tKc3PtRVukVpNhfadfQa4HdVC8nVXx+Z\n6TpIGpsXKpIpk0x7wGsNaj0R2GjIrlKaQHwYKF2n47c97nKaPpuuLXAkGFovmk+4\nZ5L5ntDRwrJdM1JhuUzNlqdhzg+qQOm43gHvTOxzmtB4waCUJGiYRkVL+YkMqRrj\nKxKGzeayoa7gAbebdO/YC3z4X7jVvmmhvb1/2mGOzaGFjY36wjNy1SW/KPTmKeMF\nBs/hWEI4fY366wuJxBiH+nHnNIilGrE3CbCwKERqwEMRKu1Dn/07vftl/BUzvISX\nX7c+K6GvCAk+X8nH0q0l\n=pFLj\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-24T07:59:35Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cps-test-lab/robovast/commit/3fab72ca798c0b56cf270870bcbbddfeeb254aba","node_id":"C_kwDOPVaL7doAKDNmYWI3MmNhNzk4YzBiNTZjZjI3MDg3MGJjYmJkZGZlZWIyNTRhYmE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cps-test-lab/robovast/commit/ea7b7678a8722ad41ab4c5fa87dea95118f7e55e","sha":"ea7b7678a8722ad41ab4c5fa87dea95118f7e55e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/commits/ea7b7678a8722ad41ab4c5fa87dea95118f7e55e"}],"sha":"3fab72ca798c0b56cf270870bcbbddfeeb254aba","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/commits/3fab72ca798c0b56cf270870bcbbddfeeb254aba"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83823539?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fred-labs","id":83823539,"login":"fred-labs","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzODIzNTM5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/commits/ea7b7678a8722ad41ab4c5fa87dea95118f7e55e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-24T06:25:35Z","email":"fred-labs@mailbox.org","name":"fred-labs"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-24T06:25:35Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Serve what an image can spawn, not only what it can configure (#526)\n\nA campaign names a robot and a world before it names anything else, and neither had a tool.\nThe plugin catalog says what a component accepts; nothing said which components exist to\nspawn, so a ref could only be learned by reading the simulator''s source -- and an agent\ndriving the documented path could not learn one at all.\n\nThe simulator already answers both (`roqsim catalog models` / `worlds`). They join the pair\nas two more `catalog` values rather than arriving as tools of their own: the question is the\nsame one, and four more tools would cost several hundred tokens where this costs sixteen.\n\nA listing is read to CHOOSE, so its fields are the ones a choice turns on, and those differ\nby catalog. A model''s `components` is the capability answer -- a turtlebot4 carries\ndiff_drive, lidar and oakd_camera; a piracer carries ackermann_drive and no lidar -- and its\n`ref` is what a world writes. Projected onto the introspection shape a model would have come\nback as a name and two nulls.\n\nA model ref carries a provider (`roqsim_mobile:turtlebot4`), which an entry-point name never\ndoes, so it gets its own pattern rather than a widened one. Widening the shared check would\nalso admit `task.py:Task` -- a plugin the campaign itself carries, which the world-key check\nasks no image about.","tree":{"sha":"93e1ddbf9707fe5f24c51aea11ebe3f9f1047f94","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/git/trees/93e1ddbf9707fe5f24c51aea11ebe3f9f1047f94"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/git/commits/ea7b7678a8722ad41ab4c5fa87dea95118f7e55e","verification":{"payload":"tree 93e1ddbf9707fe5f24c51aea11ebe3f9f1047f94\nparent d2cb95cf37597cd64c7a746225032084a5c29da0\nauthor fred-labs <fred-labs@mailbox.org> 1790231135 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790231135 +0200\n\nServe what an image can spawn, not only what it can configure (#526)\n\nA campaign names a robot and a world before it names anything else, and neither had a tool.\nThe plugin catalog says what a component accepts; nothing said which components exist to\nspawn, so a ref could only be learned by reading the simulator''s source -- and an agent\ndriving the documented path could not learn one at all.\n\nThe simulator already answers both (`roqsim catalog models` / `worlds`). They join the pair\nas two more `catalog` values rather than arriving as tools of their own: the question is the\nsame one, and four more tools would cost several hundred tokens where this costs sixteen.\n\nA listing is read to CHOOSE, so its fields are the ones a choice turns on, and those differ\nby catalog. A model''s `components` is the capability answer -- a turtlebot4 carries\ndiff_drive, lidar and oakd_camera; a piracer carries ackermann_drive and no lidar -- and its\n`ref` is what a world writes. Projected onto the introspection shape a model would have come\nback as a name and two nulls.\n\nA model ref carries a provider (`roqsim_mobile:turtlebot4`), which an entry-point name never\ndoes, so it gets its own pattern rather than a widened one. Widening the shared check would\nalso admit `task.py:Task` -- a plugin the campaign itself carries, which the world-key check\nasks no image about.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqtMJfCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA