ttps://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fred-labs","id":83823539,"login":"fred-labs","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzODIzNTM5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/commits/b5b1c0eee83492caf1eeff7bcfc8bf4a0c048640/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-23T20:02:18Z","email":"fred-labs@mailbox.org","name":"fred-labs"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-23T20:02:18Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Name a version rather than pin one in the capture sample (#659)\n\nThe sample manifest''s provenance fields -- ``producer_version`` and the three entries of\n``packages`` -- are whatever the image that recorded the run held, so the sample writes them\n``<version>``. A sample that spells out today''s numbers has to be edited whenever one of them\nmoves, and reads as a requirement until someone does. The paragraph that describes those\nfields says so, and says that ``version`` at the top is not one of them: that is the format''s\nown number, which a reader refuses when it does not know it.\n\nThe structure the sample exists to show is unchanged.","tree":{"sha":"e63299db275bebc8aaf7b8e7ab5d83000ca0ad4c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/git/trees/e63299db275bebc8aaf7b8e7ab5d83000ca0ad4c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/git/commits/b5b1c0eee83492caf1eeff7bcfc8bf4a0c048640","verification":{"payload":"tree e63299db275bebc8aaf7b8e7ab5d83000ca0ad4c\nparent 3ed7988746c7a9a3d121cce8174603e495847a0f\nauthor fred-labs <fred-labs@mailbox.org> 1790193738 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790193738 +0200\n\nName a version rather than pin one in the capture sample (#659)\n\nThe sample manifest''s provenance fields -- ``producer_version`` and the three entries of\n``packages`` -- are whatever the image that recorded the run held, so the sample writes them\n``<version>``. A sample that spells out today''s numbers has to be edited whenever one of them\nmoves, and reads as a requirement until someone does. The paragraph that describes those\nfields says so, and says that ``version`` at the top is not one of them: that is the format''s\nown number, which a reader refuses when it does not know it.\n\nThe structure the sample exists to show is unchanged.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqtDBKCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAZMQQABgtEbgyC6LBUIBCRt/KAtvJ\nvC3gtlqNBOrzomuRsB1KDtqLwDQKd4jLD7zQK0514yUV3RUcLknrap4+6cjUmePL\nRRTp9TMxScAeo/zX0XDGOBF7x5/b1GVVSERmhijZay5WTjbKFnM1upXkB/rHTT/3\nQjYxmEeNOAIDVes1oWME8Ztzp5gZaNOWIAUlaaxPPCT8mqaFrsP70mXyRLuYUoFC\nJuWztYBtLZsl7/uBXyAkk1GkHaja5ZP+iPv9cP6AaEb+BlhlqMIIeJ2k+0D43oBr\nSa0oHj4ktqBqF2Z4UqjP0uz03/lnwfAcWlHygMhW5JXxLSr/tleKvQan0HqQnWiY\n+I4EHXsbLUXqTrbW1oKyhvte5qXSkeJv0HBH8QsRifIofYVZEhtNKEOKQTzXkjBV\nO95i/+r72c/i3ESrc1BqRb0OSUPpYbkrWLppLe0Qj/0m3tCkzxgoS0xcGTSKUJaQ\nLViYsFTp+AXABHWWZTgFmI+5tNanW/R+8tz5+qO9qgoAeiKFgj11TuY04Z5R1R0Y\nfhYRiZLsjTbtbwtgG83BU70qYAJAWyDIk73q0I8DOdZP1dX6Mc4LgeAoh1rhQs3V\nA6xhV+NxcsZOhDAGN6n0Z9OVqjk3aziM5OjILWSC9sYNMDpEhvlmrSZkZ1htCjqt\nzjLWL2KNoiDRsCh3EZ3i\n=i7/n\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-23T20:02:18Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cps-test-lab/robovast/commit/b5b1c0eee83492caf1eeff7bcfc8bf4a0c048640","node_id":"C_kwDOPVaL7doAKGI1YjFjMGVlZTgzNDkyY2FmMWVlZmY3YmNmYzhiZjRhMGMwNDg2NDA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cps-test-lab/robovast/commit/3ed7988746c7a9a3d121cce8174603e495847a0f","sha":"3ed7988746c7a9a3d121cce8174603e495847a0f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/commits/3ed7988746c7a9a3d121cce8174603e495847a0f"}],"sha":"b5b1c0eee83492caf1eeff7bcfc8bf4a0c048640","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/commits/b5b1c0eee83492caf1eeff7bcfc8bf4a0c048640"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83823539?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fred-labs","id":83823539,"login":"fred-labs","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzODIzNTM5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/commits/3ed7988746c7a9a3d121cce8174603e495847a0f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-23T15:54:58Z","email":"fred-labs@mailbox.org","name":"fred-labs"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-23T15:54:58Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Ingest session settings: no synchronous commit, ANALYZE at the end, widening under the DDL lock (#647)\n\nThree things an ingest does to the index, all for its speed. None of them changes the rows\nor the types it produces.\n\nThe rows it writes commit without waiting for their WAL flush, because the index is\nderived: every row is rebuilt by ingesting the campaign''s files again. The registry row\nthat ends the ingest is the exception and commits durably, so the rows above it are on disk\nbefore anything reads the campaign as ingested -- the marker postprocessing writes\nafterwards rests on that row. One flush per ingest.\n\nAn ingest ends by analysing the tables it cleared and wrote, so the first query over them is\nnot planned on the statistics from before the campaign, or on none at all for a table just\ncreated. The cost is the table''s rather than the ingest''s, and only the tables it wrote are\nnamed. Reported rather than raised: everything the ingest owes is committed and flushed by\nthen, so failing it over statistics would report a complete ingest as a failed one and send\nthe caller round to redo the work.\n\nensure_table decides the DDL from verdicts read under the DDL lock, and creates or widens\nfrom those. A decision taken from a read outside the lock can land on a table another writer\nchanged in between: a column retyped back to the narrower verdict its reader saw, or a\ncreate whose narrower verdicts settle over a table another writer has just built. The common\ncase -- a table that already fits -- is answered from one read and takes no lock at all,\nwhich cannot go stale because a verdict only widens and a column is never dropped; and a\nbatch too wide for the table is refused before it queues, because a table only gains columns.","tree":{"sha":"c5abecf9513561e57cc36f524b213f06721d557b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/git/trees/c5abecf9513561e57cc36f524b213f06721d557b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/git/commits/3ed7988746c7a9a3d121cce8174603e495847a0f","verification":{"payload":"tree c5abecf9513561e57cc36f524b213f06721d557b\nparent a3f550b78903360ce68f6813e6639010f85a8f30\nauthor fred-labs <fred-labs@mailbox.org> 1790178898 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790178898 +0200\n\nIngest session settings: no synchronous commit, ANALYZE at the end, widening under the DDL lock (#647)\n\nThree things an ingest does to the index, all for its speed. None of them changes the rows\nor the types it produces.\n\nThe rows it writes commit without waiting for their WAL flush, because the index is\nderived: every row is rebuilt by ingesting the campaign''s files again. The registry row\nthat ends the ingest is the exception and commits durably, so the rows above it are on disk\nbefore anything reads the campaign as ingested -- the marker postprocessing writes\nafterwards rests on that row. One flush per ingest.\n\nAn ingest ends by analysing the tables it cleared and wrote, so the first query over them is\nnot planned on the statistics from before the campaign, or on none at all for a table just\ncreated. The cost is the table''s rather than the ingest''s, and only the tables it wrote are\nnamed. Reported rather than raised: everything the ingest owes is committed and flushed by\nthen, so failing it over statistics would report a complete ingest as a failed one and send\nthe caller round to redo the work.\n\nensure_table decides the DDL from verdicts read under the DDL lock, and creates or widens\nfrom those. A decision taken from a read outside the lock can land on a table another writer\nchanged in between: a column retyped back to the narrower verdict its reader saw, or a\ncreate whose narrower verdicts settle over a table another writer has just built. The common\ncase -- a table that already fits -- is answered from one read and takes no lock at all,\nwhich cannot go stale because a verdict only widens and a column is never dropped; and a\nbatch too wide for the table is refused before it queues, because a table only gains columns.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqs/ZSCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA5d4QAAuDkQA3FXSsFPQ4b2wpD1vB\nhmkw2FP5hfaNhqVu3YTd3cGMW712eFMIsmFIJ9XH8A5a/GtJ5dRaArNZfLhXewn7\novOZPuAX0pASjSYpcZnk3jYs498Nc1damLOYSkt+NYUleJtEwHTYoYkwNKWisdMV\nNwPSGr5ouaTWbkfq4FhWWOV4yNl5shWp45HfBPmXYKbpEg79fqA+8FtsNKGNkeOP\nnKv6Oyuai2hj9SUwhaFxq00FwgONNGyV8huO6r1FiLgVeNsbOiXYH3cOuiBqzUUq\nkKhxYZzfr0MfFiTLHB6T+J20hJemeW4c4PtH2Lj9zAbOtoU5kzAlCfxGGzPHQzmr\n4j2/xdQVmPtsQemrSwLHGnI4ZYg8KFK3WqZu/Wjh4rbeh0sjR7ybaBVrrgcj6fYz\nik5BRYOhnxnixfolQgYZ8iUsgtnvGqCzO/kvDzUAElarK4ZUCCthkVJ0SuYiU1l8\nyw7jAuEH7TbSP1ehpO7sHePru6edNpGue0pCQXDDceqG8d4m1CkuRJQnAHoIdvbY\nne15K6KNkm9uZSe775CImDHEfIbkbOS/kmavPhuQl6X52p6oi/oL4v+txM3YUwCQ\ncHje/lSNAA8budavLHPckxzTihYzveYwuvmZX5xcdb3bgvV+7s4kH0I2rNph/vz0\n+vA+OmeoH20clI/UomD1\n=BuyX\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-23T15:54:59Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gi