ubscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/commits/a3f550b78903360ce68f6813e6639010f85a8f30/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-23T15:49:25Z","email":"fred-labs@mailbox.org","name":"fred-labs"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-23T15:49:25Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Campaigns: a Run-view button on the card (#643)\n\nReplaying a run is what a reader most often opens a campaign for, so the card carries a\nRun-view icon button first among its controls, under the same canReplay gate as the menu\nentry: recorded runs, or a preview of a running campaign, which the label says. One label\nserves the button and the entry, so the two cannot promise different things. The entry\nstays, because the menu is what lists everything a campaign can be opened in.\n\nLeftmost, so the controls every card shares -- the menu and the fold -- and a live card''s\nStop keep their places whether or not a card has the shortcut.\n\nThe controls column is reserved at the width of its widest set, which with the shortcut is\nfour icon buttons and the three gaps between them: a running campaign that can be\npreviewed. CONTROLS_COLUMN grows by one button and one gap, so a folded row''s meter and age\nstay in line with every other row''s.\n\nThe web UI docs name the button, its condition and where it sits, beside the rule that\neverything else is a named line in the menu.","tree":{"sha":"da0979e7f286f659929f15705a410fb2d171d020","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/git/trees/da0979e7f286f659929f15705a410fb2d171d020"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/git/commits/a3f550b78903360ce68f6813e6639010f85a8f30","verification":{"payload":"tree da0979e7f286f659929f15705a410fb2d171d020\nparent 514d9f4c1dc46d21a854d7bd475973b00eb56784\nauthor fred-labs <fred-labs@mailbox.org> 1790178565 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790178565 +0200\n\nCampaigns: a Run-view button on the card (#643)\n\nReplaying a run is what a reader most often opens a campaign for, so the card carries a\nRun-view icon button first among its controls, under the same canReplay gate as the menu\nentry: recorded runs, or a preview of a running campaign, which the label says. One label\nserves the button and the entry, so the two cannot promise different things. The entry\nstays, because the menu is what lists everything a campaign can be opened in.\n\nLeftmost, so the controls every card shares -- the menu and the fold -- and a live card''s\nStop keep their places whether or not a card has the shortcut.\n\nThe controls column is reserved at the width of its widest set, which with the shortcut is\nfour icon buttons and the three gaps between them: a running campaign that can be\npreviewed. CONTROLS_COLUMN grows by one button and one gap, so a folded row''s meter and age\nstay in line with every other row''s.\n\nThe web UI docs name the button, its condition and where it sits, beside the rule that\neverything else is a named line in the menu.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqs/UFCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAwyUQADe2Mjlw4eTdy6dvdmC+Ef1R\nwTq+Jjh6SzHps9Kj0UO211j636ZJAdvqh2qF9G80HXWUh4AD2jkMmHBnIXgtO94g\nnphm4U0rAhA4j2VepRm7nI8ueKKQHC66NIisDVrb+ex6LJuTzvmSbSXFIlZnZi5B\nJFsq8v4CPFXfG/Huus8rlwjieQtR7csccmyLyO/uBoBDpfa4T98nnTpHY33vOcII\n3tpidvrQwFdWTMFHvARbo/dwgsqgPWrTcbhjsV2dteTcLqNuOWI8dkX8oNbt3Rls\njR/xtPAIY1VR4E086F2kUMVKmyDQ9Ibn+12Th3PHlhlKOghzKD91gZhGwYeh5EYd\neCvvH83I+lDm6g22mXvhPAZKSdivcpCkSE0Rv7Df8tbGM6Z0uUZAdRGoTmZQrXEB\n55RsLJb6S1W+D2j8QEwf56hJj9011L9L1R/9BBHxbKSJRHexL5B2PnenfBhlq0aA\ns+QYOBpZ4CnHIFThMQR+31TI+svEDhSSN917PRqgKbIe9oUUBtfhe6Dmp2VnkTbE\nNWGAXqJcxdByT6If9/vm3G51XB6qB/2v8v0ZIQkQIJj5cLFi/Rsmp93ExR+riIiv\nF5/2mLRp4wbzVNaK5q2oj5DlVhReUoWL4nOhTNYEPYMZMuaLFk9RNcYvasYV683/\n