thub.com/users/fred-labs/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fred-labs","id":83823539,"login":"fred-labs","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzODIzNTM5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/commits/514d9f4c1dc46d21a854d7bd475973b00eb56784/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-23T15:24:02Z","email":"fred-labs@mailbox.org","name":"fred-labs"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-23T15:24:02Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Run view: fast-forward starts a paused playback (#642)\n\nThe fast-forward button asks to watch the run faster, so on a paused clock it advances the\nspeed and starts playback; on a playing one it only cycles 1x, 2x, 4x, 8x and back. The\nbutton never pauses -- that is play/pause''s, and the transport bar has one control for it.\n\nThe behaviour lives in a small module beside the panel, so it is tested against a real\nPlaybackClock rather than through a DOM, and stays out of the shared panel-kit clock\ncontract. Pressed at the end of the timeline it replays from the start, as the play button\ndoes.\n\nThe tooltip and the button''s accessible name both say what the press will do, which while\npaused is two things: \"Play at Nx\" rather than the speed in hand.\n\nThe Playback docs state the speed cycle, the start-on-press and that the button has no\npause in it.","tree":{"sha":"c4ca9963e32a73e66e8808001e270efbdeb5b2c5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/git/trees/c4ca9963e32a73e66e8808001e270efbdeb5b2c5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/git/commits/514d9f4c1dc46d21a854d7bd475973b00eb56784","verification":{"payload":"tree c4ca9963e32a73e66e8808001e270efbdeb5b2c5\nparent 173bbf7617591fb33ae92d50ef4332b896312fde\nauthor fred-labs <fred-labs@mailbox.org> 1790177042 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790177042 +0200\n\nRun view: fast-forward starts a paused playback (#642)\n\nThe fast-forward button asks to watch the run faster, so on a paused clock it advances the\nspeed and starts playback; on a playing one it only cycles 1x, 2x, 4x, 8x and back. The\nbutton never pauses -- that is play/pause''s, and the transport bar has one control for it.\n\nThe behaviour lives in a small module beside the panel, so it is tested against a real\nPlaybackClock rather than through a DOM, and stays out of the shared panel-kit clock\ncontract. Pressed at the end of the timeline it replays from the start, as the play button\ndoes.\n\nThe tooltip and the button''s accessible name both say what the press will do, which while\npaused is two things: \"Play at Nx\" rather than the speed in hand.\n\nThe Playback docs state the speed cycle, the start-on-press and that the button has no\npause in it.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqs+8SCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA6ZsQAKDPujwleeZUVnb6fc6+YKmU\nW3BoffdK8haRYhQ38CW+vDI39iv++mJz/MONrPXFQixlJsH7lyYRPL11acOL+UPq\nDh0atRk3eSPgu9X02F7YcMm7HTcp433VD61GYWg53kLG1gB3k4+5WnTEUWbHf8yi\nHlNEsNuised8pmX82tgpMI8FUs2CICz0hadR//+rq/rwKlKQzofhIuD4dI8510qB\nMPG1SQGOgDi2F7/N+0XX8fF7FhoGBTymaScsGRV7naDogyAW1SfC/FInGYp2GFJs\n7pwQ7MQUUstXD241chsLWNRoUDEr/bXG+nTQuRVUaQpknJnX8vxhiJuEAWowBXCS\nN3MFTu0D8OCf+BBO96FlUVtxvUUqY1ZbSBm9bCVdMDkw+abNVUyfT9SDmbSSQJYh\n3aFx+OtT4pFeQQCiUuXEB2eZ7BD/79rEUrahewPNOpw5omZUNb0egn//Gj+b1zY4\nU1HbZGRMhhQMMyJl5IVPyhrs4ymE72otTFvh6cT7x/Hr2sNeYzLgOhbQ9oZKZcig\nnXFRv+xRtj15g3HTfS30ue70iUg/dga+6Fu7uRjtsVS5pms1RYrfJjlaJ7W+4p7X\n9eVnFfqVI36fzi38dP3pDnAhTh0JX0r