mmit/173bbf7617591fb33ae92d50ef4332b896312fde","node_id":"C_kwDOPVaL7doAKDE3M2JiZjc2MTc1OTFmYjMzYWU5MmQ1MGVmNDMzMmI4OTYzMTJmZGU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cps-test-lab/robovast/commit/c4ea4e77b38e21330268e74ee40f839e13ae2bd0","sha":"c4ea4e77b38e21330268e74ee40f839e13ae2bd0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/commits/c4ea4e77b38e21330268e74ee40f839e13ae2bd0"}],"sha":"173bbf7617591fb33ae92d50ef4332b896312fde","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/commits/173bbf7617591fb33ae92d50ef4332b896312fde"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83823539?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fred-labs","id":83823539,"login":"fred-labs","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzODIzNTM5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/commits/c4ea4e77b38e21330268e74ee40f839e13ae2bd0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-23T15:00:08Z","email":"fred-labs@mailbox.org","name":"fred-labs"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-23T15:00:08Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Read only the topics a rosbag handler converts (#644)\n\nThe worker builds a topic -> handlers map from the handlers'' topics(), and the bag reader\nis filtered to exactly those topics with rosbag2_py.StorageFilter, so the storage plugin\nskips every other topic''s records instead of handing them to Python to be dropped after\nthe read. Camera, laser-scan and odometry streams are usually most of a bag, and no\nhandler asks for them.\n\nOne decision governs the read, because an empty subscription is not an empty filter:\nrosbag2 reads every topic when the filter is empty, so a bag holding nothing any handler\nasked for is not opened for reading at all. The dispatch still tests each topic -- the\nfilter is the storage plugin''s promise, and a plugin that does not keep it has to skip a\nrecord rather than fail on a type nothing cached.\n\nEvery handler''s topics() is checked against the topics its on_message consumes: tf_to_csv\ndeclares /tf and /tf_static, nav2_bt_to_csv /behavior_tree_log, and the action, rosout,\nclock, costmap, to_csv and webm handlers their own. RosbagHandler.topics() states the\ncontract the filter rests on: a handler lists every topic it reads.\n\nThe converter imports nothing from robovast.\n\nTests (need rosbag2_py, skipped without ROS like the converter''s other tests): an\nundeclared topic is never handed out by the reader; the output for the declared topics is\nbyte-identical to a read that ignored the filter, including tf_to_csv''s poses resolved\nthrough a static map -> odom; a bag with none of the declared topics is not read; and a\ntable pins each registered handler''s declared topics, so a new handler fails until it has\na row.","tree":{"sha":"c88c93a265fc17b691c9a5924d9293bcafa72317","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/git/trees/c88c93a265fc17b691c9a5924d9293bcafa72317"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/git/commits/c4ea4e77b38e21330268e74ee40f839e13ae2bd0","verification":{"payload":"tree c88c93a265fc17b691c9a5924d9293bcafa72317\nparent 49e2e677b7f7fd7986a7197476cfcadaf9417998\nauthor fred-labs <fred-labs@mailbox.org> 1790175608 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790175608 +0200\n\nRead only the topics a rosbag handler converts (#644)\n\nThe worker builds a topic -> handlers map from the handlers'' topics(), and the bag reader\nis filtered to exactly those topics with rosbag2_py.StorageFilter, so the storage plugin\nskips every other topic''s records instead of handing them to Python to be dropped after\nthe read. Camera, laser-scan and odometry streams are usually most of a bag, and no\nhandler asks for them.\n\nOne decision governs the read, because an empty subscription is not an empty filter:\nrosbag2 reads every topic when the filter is empty, so a bag holding nothing any handler\nasked for is not opened for reading at all. The dispatch still tests each topic -- the\nfilter is the storage plugin''s promise, and a plugin that does not keep it has to skip a\nrecord rather than fail on a type nothing cached.\n\nEvery handler''s topics() is checked against the topics its on_message consumes: tf_to_csv\ndeclares /tf and /tf_static, nav2_bt_to_csv /behavior_tree_log, and the action, rosout,\nclock, costmap, to_csv and webm handlers their own. RosbagHandler.topics() states the\ncontract the filter rests on: a handler lists every topic it reads.\n\nThe converter imports nothing from robovast.\n\nTests (need rosbag2_py, skipped without ROS like the converter''s other tests): an\nundeclared topic is never handed out by the reader; the output for the declared topics is\nbyte-identical to a read that ignored the filter, including tf_to_csv''s poses resolved\nthrough a static map -> odom; a bag with none of the declared topics is not read; and a\ntable pins each registered handler''s declared topics, so a new handler fails until it has\na row.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqs+l4CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAiRoQAFfi1V54we2NxNOkuFOBXF8D\nLqojg5JMnY9qS2DhbxMo+swAOe6WdepQdPhdWqJc4DdOBhdmTSI2P6ZH5dHGMvZ9\nujHRI8nVpLpvIsRJRr93U7VfoCT+znEWQ5WoZIKC4d+6eNf