lab/robovast/commits/49e2e677b7f7fd7986a7197476cfcadaf9417998"}],"sha":"c4ea4e77b38e21330268e74ee40f839e13ae2bd0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/commits/c4ea4e77b38e21330268e74ee40f839e13ae2bd0"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83823539?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fred-labs","id":83823539,"login":"fred-labs","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzODIzNTM5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/commits/49e2e677b7f7fd7986a7197476cfcadaf9417998/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-23T14:50:59Z","email":"fred-labs@mailbox.org","name":"fred-labs"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-23T14:50:59Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Check the world a search''s draws run, not the default none of them opens (#637)\n\nA search has no configuration: block; every draw is composed from search.parameters, so\nthat template is where a search names the world its runs load. The world check reads it as\none configuration, and the campaign default is skipped when the template replaces it --\nthe same rule that already applies when every configuration overrides the default. The two\nblocks are mutually exclusive in the schema, so a campaign has one or the other.\n\nA sim: value taken from the search space as $name has no value until a draw is composed.\nThat world is reported unchecked, naming the variables it waits on and preview_configurations\nas the step that settles them, rather than described with the marker in place, where the\nsimulator''s refusal of a literal $name would read as the campaign''s own error.\n\nThat reading belongs to the search template alone. A $name is a search variable and only a\nsearch declares any, so the same string in an authored block is a literal the simulator is\nmeant to receive -- and describing the world is how a wrong one is found. The marker check\nis asked of the one block a search composes from, never of a world somebody wrote a dollar\nsign into.\n\nThe markers are collected by config.collect_var_refs, the walk the search schema already\nvalidates its own references with, so one function answers \"which search variables does\nthis data still name\".","tree":{"sha":"11e180f447d2c741f396cd86ec9d9d626bf7d798","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/git/trees/11e180f447d2c741f396cd86ec9d9d626bf7d798"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/git/commits/49e2e677b7f7fd7986a7197476cfcadaf9417998","verification":{"payload":"tree 11e180f447d2c741f396cd86ec9d9d626bf7d798\nparent d6d0d6ae2f07d7d1555feebaeae2f918a8d1ed85\nauthor fred-labs <fred-labs@mailbox.org> 1790175059 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790175059 +0200\n\nCheck the world a search''s draws run, not the default none of them opens (#637)\n\nA search has no configuration: block; every draw is composed from search.parameters, so\nthat template is where a search names the world its runs load. The world check reads it as\none configuration, and the campaign default is skipped when the template replaces it --\nthe same rule that already applies when every configuration overrides the default. The two\nblocks are mutually exclusive in the schema, so a campaign has one or the other.\n\nA sim: value taken from the search space as $name has no value until a draw is composed.\nThat world is reported unchecked, naming the variables it waits on and preview_configurations\nas the step that settles them, rather than described with the marker in place, where the\nsimulator''s refusal of a literal $name would read as the campaign''s own error.\n\nThat reading belongs to the search template alone. A $name is a search variable and only a\nsearch declares any, so the same string in an authored block is a literal the simulator is\nmeant to receive -- and describing the world is how a wrong one is found. The marker check\nis asked of the one block a search composes from, never of a world somebody wrote a dollar\nsign into.\n\nThe markers are collected by config.collect_var_refs, the walk the search schema already\nvalidates its own references with, so one function answers \"which search variables does\nthis data still name\".","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqs+dTCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAaAsQAJWA1tC5HBkjxA9/NxMgGbhg\nF0kT9aqWlwFFkw3fCD1YsEsIeVZVIjg6P5sCIQugsSlNJlPYDxDr5x4W+KswErTl\nSTuqS6MdC5MVr5fnvyJT/t/LY6ch25WcMqJa6LORK7fCQ2A0KHNCHj//KCNr+K9+\nZ8wvUtz/BZyWn3XGooXq41AYdgYYvSgCRtTNacE1rU+fAovx+KLC+aS+Y8Du5c3W\n4x8MNCQKgbEHVJ6viPJ2Cj/4kwil3x6pq/NaQX4WYF+NkDCTThR06/SgRwCuXjeo\nPWx/gM7M5U5d8AWZg2H7WuoAfSbOeY1nf7t9BAn/EiG9rk0qtEPGlVzhD58aXICH\nJxbGBlWcfcwz+44vYs5rTh359gnYSkPqjsUmQFRLelVX0zGDYnePPHXdVi3+wKYM\nRT8Y3KtcHG3srpy/UGppjLTQkL8gOGp6CwSq/+bw0Hh6VD/H+U932kRUzTaXYdru\nX6cG9Nvfch6ObuJ8MEHVXg1cbkIPIWmgiFO2sykIm/+BZ7KkTuKNlOd3JcpSm63e\nFIRh3kHC94yEgS84yBCv6O/Yh8kY4//TUv+g+33yrVKKNpNIgaitiTYPP0exq1/g\nmFrsWajMpNeTGN4QgVZxWmxsX3aqDyQDbNqLNQXLz0QOASnURdhr46QRtlmWYAE6\ndZjYkiPgG5VJZFA869mv\n=u+lK\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-23T14:51:00Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cps-test-lab/robovast/commit/49e2e677b7f7fd7986a7197476cfcadaf9417998","node_id":"C_kwDOPVaL7doAKDQ5ZTJlNjc3YjdmN2ZkNzk4NmE3MTk3NDc2Y2ZjYWRhZjk0MTc5OTg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cps-test-lab/robovast/commit/d6d0d6ae2f07d7d1555feebaeae2f918a8d1ed85","sha":"d6d0d6ae2f07d7d1555feebaeae2f918a8d1ed85","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/commits/d6d0d6ae2f07d7d1555feebaeae2f918a8d1ed85"}],"sha":"49e2e677b7f7fd7986a7197476cfcadaf9417998","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/commits/49e2e677b7f7fd7986a7197476cfcadaf9417998"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83823539?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fred-labs","id":83823539,"login":"fred-labs","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzODIzNTM5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/commits/d6d0d6ae2f07d7d1555feebaeae2f918a8d1ed85/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-23T14:03:39Z","email":"fred-labs@mailbox.org","name":"fred-labs"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-23T14:03:39Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Sort the campaign list by recency or size, in either direction (#646)\n\nListCampaignsRequest gains sort (\"recent\" | \"size\", default \"recent\") and order (\"desc\" |\n\"asc\", default \"desc\"); any other value is refused. The service applies them before\nlimit/offset cut the page, so every surface hands them through: the HTTP route and the SSE\nstream take them as query parameters (422 otherwise), the HTTP client sends them, `vast\ncampaign list` has --sort and --desc/--asc and a size column, and the MCP list_campaigns\ntool takes sort/order and reports results_bytes.\n\nLive campaigns lead under every order. A campaign with no value for the key (no recorded\nsize, no recorded start) comes last in both directions, and ties keep the default recency\norder, by sorting stably on the key and then on the group.\n\nThe size key is read without building a summary per campaign: _results_bytes_for answers\nfrom a tracked entry''s snapshot or from outcome.json, the same source as the row''s figure,\nand memoises the answer, None included, once the record is terminal. The default order\nreads no size at all. A reactivated campaign''s entry carries the recorded size forward, so\na campaign that a re-triggered share or postprocessing is answering for lists at its own\nsize rather than as unmeasured.\n\nThe web UI has an order selector beside the search, kept in the hash\n(#/execution?sort=size&order=desc) and carried across navigation, and the folded row shows\nthe results size. The app-wide stream stays in the default order because the start/end\nnotices read it; the campaign view opens a second, ordered stream for any other order, and\ntakes \"newest\" from the app-wide one. That second stream is open only while the campaign\npage is the one on screen, which is the rule every reading in a kept-alive page follows.","tree":{"sha":"8d935a2c6d21e6209a2cca1bcfe8fbb395a4b788","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/git/trees/8d935a2c6d21e6209a2cca1bcfe8fbb395a4b788"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/git/commits/d6d0d6ae2f07d7d1555feebaeae2f918a8d1ed85","verification":{"payload":"tree 8d935a2c6d21e6209a2cca1bcfe8fbb395a4b788\nparent efc61bd040bc5877fa3ed29ea49f5ebb0a55c156\nauthor fred-labs <fred-labs@mailbox.org> 1790172219 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790172219 +0200\n\nSort the campaign list by recency or size, in either direction (#646)\n\nListCampaignsRequest gains sort (\"recent\" | \"size\", default \"recent\") and order (\"desc\" |\n\"asc\", default \"desc\"); any other value is refused. The service applies them before\nlimit/offset cut the page, so every surface hands them through: the HTTP route and the SSE\nstream take them as query parameters (422 otherwise), the HTTP client sends them, `vast\ncampaign list` has --sort and --desc/--asc and a size column, and the MCP list_campaigns\ntool takes sort/order and reports results_bytes.\n\nLive campaigns lead under every order. A campaign with no value for the key (no recorded\nsize, no recorded start) comes last in both directions, and ties keep the default recency\norder, by sorting stably on the key and then on the group.\n\nThe size key is read without building a summary per campaign: _results_bytes_for answers\nfrom a tracked entry''s snapshot or from outcome.json, the same source as the row''s figure,\nand memoises the answer, None included, once the record is terminal. The default order\nreads no size at all. A reactivated campaign''s entry carries the recorded size forward, so\na campaign that a re-triggered share or postprocessing is answering for lists at its own\nsize rather than as unmeasured.\n\nThe web UI has an order selector beside the search, kept in the hash\n(#/execution?sort=size&order=desc) and carried across navigation, and the folded row shows\nthe results size. The app-wide stream stays in the default order because the start/end\nnotices read it; the campaign view opens a second, ordered stream for any other order, and\ntakes \"newest\" from the app-wide one. That second stream is open only while the campaign\npage is the one on screen, which is the rule every reading in a kept-alive page follows.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqs9w7CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAt6AQADhzEXBNAEEDhjo6G6gDgXmo\njtUJfirkZeZO9w7o41XsFfGeWqtSz6iHU6Q8YDkBwCV/RIEwJXM4hCb3pxP/2/GM\nW5IWIZGdmmWvvyFZtRjQoDx85pJ1Gb4z1RBF+KF54uhEFg8MocPTVMbqiqFk/pFg\n1GkHWaDj7Rtxiu8b2gsSr5HYcrcNGZ0qrPQVPJOI/WcXnbmgNSh0PaergbS8omKZ\n4ZCLPjIDEg32iVM1aSOQlgTnAA1FD0gqbXCF6K7uDEkUMUJXg/KHJqnivMHNSiY0\nTFaFkDudevxkN3hdFrjC1nkAwzBlSoJTKwRuAbBYkDSN+jM0GtXvQj2padTGcMbE\nXev/0VpUyXKn6FLBYiEkZYkpd8xzb5MbBe/qzIsIBQWgTyefg8rA7hUbVN5hsU/r\nIPp9C8lQjTX+bo7nH/8az4WTJrWsA3Bs+JbeduG3bha56l/CWe6D+ER0wujo4Cew\ny5MQx3+SqjcesxiZNXWLvHMTwEj4XJWxoyij0YJm4qpbMdgu8me5nJgQxrCRvadb\nZjI1VFE7p63os8y1ydT6xKW8hW227eaij/OtKxtX+yfu4uaf03Scr4YnZuKKo32d\nCW3YrIIj+XV+b3/aj1s5JJTYzdDjY+KRKaA6agaPhStxw+FRumLL7Rh7p3yQ/UyT\nnWSKHFA0vMhPn4B+ftNa\n=kwlo\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-23T14:03:39Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cps-test-lab/robovast/commit/d6d0d6ae2f07d7d1555feebaeae2f918a8d1ed85","node_id":"C_kwDOPVaL7doAKGQ2ZDBkNmFlMmYwN2Q3ZDE1NTVmZWViYWVhZTJmOTE4YThkMWVkODU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cps-test-lab/robovast/commit/efc61bd040bc5877fa3ed29ea49f5ebb0a55c156","sha":"efc61bd040bc5877fa3ed29ea49f5ebb0a55c156","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/commits/efc61bd040bc5877fa3ed29ea49f5ebb0a55c156"}],"sha":"d6d0d6ae2f07d7d1555feebaeae2f918a8d1ed85","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/commits/d6d0d6ae2f07d7d1555feebaeae2f918a8d1ed85"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83823539?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fred-labs","id":83823539,"login":"fred-labs","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzODIzNTM5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/commits/efc61bd040bc5877fa3ed29ea49f5ebb0a55c156/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-23T13:45:34Z","email":"fred-labs@mailbox.org","name":"fred-labs"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-23T13:45:34Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Show a campaign''s queue priority and hold where it is looked for (#645)\n\n* Show a campaign''s queue priority and hold where it is looked for\n\nThe web UI''s priority and paused chips render on a folded card as well as an open one,\nwhich is how a card starts, so a rank set from the actions menu is visible where it was\nset. Both show only when the value is not the default and only while the campaign is\nlive: the service reports them from the admission queue, which drops a campaign once it\nends, so the launch record is never consulted.\n\nSetting a priority or a hold confirms with the service''s own answer -- the rank the\ncampaign now has, and that the runs already started are left alone. The priority prompt\nstarts at the current rank and refuses anything that is not a whole number in the dialog,\nwhich keeps the typed text. A refusal is a refusal whatever the answer''s shape: an\nunsuccessful result is the warning, and only a successful one is confirmed.\n\n`vast campaign list` carries the same standing after the phase (\"[prio -1]\", \"[paused]\",\n\"[prio -1, paused]\"), matching the MCP listing. The label and the input rule live in\n`frontend/ui/src/lib/queueStanding.ts`, where a test can pin them.\n\n* Offer queue priority and pause only on a lane that has a queue\n\nVersionInfo carries can_schedule, set from the same _SUPPORTS_SCHEDULING flag the service\nrefuses a rank or a hold on, so what a client is offered and what the service accepts\ncannot disagree. The local lane reports false and the cluster lane, inheriting version(),\nreports true. None means the service did not say, as for can_build_images, and a consumer\nreads that as no verdict rather than as false.\n\nThe web UI''s running campaign card offers \"Set queue priority...\" and pause/resume only\non a true verdict: an entry that can only be refused advertises a capability the caller\ndoes not have. `vast service info` prints it as a queue line and the MCP get_service_info\nrelays it, each only when the service gave a verdict.","tree":{"sha":"9bc7b1ddbdf0c097edc8ae62cb2fee4ab7526c50","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/git/trees/9bc7b1ddbdf0c097edc8ae62cb2fee4ab7526c50"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/git/commits/efc61bd040bc5877fa3ed29ea49f5ebb0a55c156","verification":{"payload":"tree 9bc7b1ddbdf0c097edc8ae62cb2fee4ab7526c50\nparent 3027d40f6ffbe765b64228ff85ce1a3e6f8c5af4\nauthor fred-labs <fred-labs@mailbox.org> 1790171134 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790171134 +0200\n\nShow a campaign''s queue priority and hold where it is looked for (#645)\n\n* Show a campaign''s queue priority and hold where it is looked for\n\nThe web UI''s priority and paused chips render on a folded card as well as an open one,\nwhich is how a card starts, so a rank set from the actions menu is visible where it was\nset. Both show only when the value is not the default and only while the campaign is\nlive: the service reports them from the admission queue, which drops a campaign once it\nends, so the launch record is never consulted.\n\nSetting a priority or a hold confirms with the service''s own answer -- the rank the\ncampaign now has, and that the runs already started are left alone. The priority prompt\nstarts at the current rank and refuses anything that is not a whole number in the dialog,\nwhich keeps the typed text. A refusal is a refusal whatever the answer''s shape: an\nunsuccessful result is the warning, and only a successful one is confirmed.\n\n`vast campaign list` carries the same standing after the phase (\"[prio -1]\", \"[paused]\",\n\"[prio -1, paused]\"), matching the MCP listing. The label and the input rule live in\n`frontend/ui/src/lib/queueStanding.ts`, where a test can pin them.\n\n* Offer queue priority and pause only on a lane that has a queue\n\nVersionInfo carries can_schedule, set from the same _SUPPORTS_SCHEDULING flag the service\nrefuses a rank or a hold on, so what a client is offered and what the service accepts\ncannot disagree. The local lane reports false and the cluster lane, inheriting version(),\nreports true. None means the service did not say, as for can_build_images, and a consumer\nreads that as no verdict rather than as false.\n\nThe web UI''s running campaign card offers \"Set queue priority...\" and pause/resume only\non a true verdict: an entry that can only be refused advertises a capability the caller\ndoes not have. `vast service info` prints it as a queue line and the MCP get_service_info\nrelays it, each only when the service gave a verdict.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqs9f+CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAu74QAA2FowHd0+HESciwv0asuil8\nbPyAD27GO/ZYrwH9NylT/ykTHkLuXsb2GjEiX4Pl7nrVkDbhla2+jYGgAYaHBLhU\n5inA7eEubWtSkYrm0zM9UUdQKdOxsRnpuax1qKiYGnUI3eB9gg/nNw/aNYd7ABqW\nF/T6YMKkkicmRRonm9b8C3MhssIGnn/HqWCWEtyPAfXQULDBBNaHZSX6B4Aj7mkD\nGzcAskQLOCs++/8qZu/Ap+8EuNMqZx+950PyQ2z7w/WZaacbR8SPvH73noGorW+k\nHDVC00vqf+Dzj8/dS3jj6CbhbX2d/JXtUZrCZC3B0jhp687J2XvWF3DTJXnyaTz6\nezgnMl6P9AzA1UYq6EN5gLeBGCEfz/yzOaguP0iuYkR5uQDjnH8+NywUxj5PyEsR\nY+RJF861eDm/TTIX25k2sBcHK3oEbwfMt0Gk7ewLZp6kG/wkOJrEXo6/LzhJLWgL\ncXKRtMeWb32E62m3b6vSteWqJmQgTF09NuyQ2VwbpLEGY2M03LcVUzQRTVVLTmrk\n3nMSBOE+/ng4oLVA+VC39Vn3tMAbFKTA5wUMGlZVdnbU57G1M8icqJ3Mbl5A7BSc\n013ailSR7xapubD+HwPXDFUg5zSN+E9bidfP/70QUB7a54m1cTcp65EyEKkTrPrt\neFZIZEJq8yTwGl0q4LFZ\n=AObv\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-23T13:45:35Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cps-test-lab/robovast/commit/efc61bd040bc5877fa3ed29ea49f5ebb0a55c156","node_id":"C_kwDOPVaL7doAKGVmYzYxYmQwNDBiYzU4NzdmYTNlZDI5ZWE0OWY1ZWJiMGE1NWMxNTY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cps-test-lab/robovast/commit/3027d40f6ffbe765b64228ff85ce1a3e6f8c5af4","sha":"3027d40f6ffbe765b64228ff85ce1a3e6f8c5af4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/commits/3027d40f6ffbe765b64228ff85ce1a3e6f8c5af4"}],"sha":"efc61bd040bc5877fa3ed29ea49f5ebb0a55c156","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/commits/efc61bd040bc5877fa3ed29ea49f5ebb0a55c156"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83823539?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fred-labs","id":83823539,"login":"fred-labs","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzODIzNTM5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/commits/3027d40f6ffbe765b64228ff85ce1a3e6f8c5af4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-23T13:27:59Z","email":"fred-labs@mailbox.org","name":"fred-labs"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-23T13:27:59Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Delete several campaigns in one operation (#648)\n\nA new interface operation, delete_campaigns(ids), answers one CampaignDeletion per id\n(deleted, not_found, partial, running, invalid) instead of one verdict for the call. It is\nnot all-or-nothing: a running campaign or an id that is not a campaign id is that id''s\noutcome and leaves it untouched, and the rest are deleted. Served as POST /campaigns/delete\nwith the ids in the body, since a list of ids is not a path and a body on DELETE is what\nproxies drop.\n\nBoth deletes share one removal path. LocalTransport._delete_deletable removes a campaign the\nguard has passed and reports a structured outcome; delete_campaign raises the guard''s\nrefusals (400/409 over HTTP) and wraps the outcome, delete_campaigns turns them into\noutcomes. The cluster lane''s Job reap and token-Secret removal move onto that hook, so they\nrun for every id of a batch too.\n\nSurfaces:\n- CLI: vast campaign delete A B C, one line per id, non-zero exit if any was not fully\n  deleted; a single id goes through the same call.\n- MCP: delete_campaign takes one id or a list and returns the per-id results. No new tool;\n  the description is shorter than before, so the tool surface shrinks slightly.\n- Web UI: a selection mode on the campaign list (running campaigns not selectable), a\n  \"Delete N selected\" action, and one dialog that lists the ids and then shows each\n  outcome in place. openapi.json and api.generated.ts regenerated.\n\nDocs: web_ui, client, mcp and http_api describe the operation and its per-id answer.","tree":{"sha":"b905672ba8f2f0016bbd088676b68dc25285230f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/git/trees/b905672ba8f2f0016bbd088676b68dc25285230f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/git/commits/3027d40f6ffbe765b64228ff85ce1a3e6f8c5af4","verification":{"payload":"tree b905672ba8f2f0016bbd088676b68dc25285230f\nparent 9488c12778dd38c8a40208baa1c400210d212bb7\nauthor fred-labs <fred-labs@mailbox.org> 1790170079 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790170079 +0200\n\nDelete several campaigns in one operation (#648)\n\nA new interface operation, delete_campaigns(ids), answers one CampaignDeletion per id\n(deleted, not_found, partial, running, invalid) instead of one verdict for the call. It is\nnot all-or-nothing: a running campaign or an id that is not a campaign id is that id''s\noutcome and leaves it untouched, and the rest are deleted. Served as POST /campaigns/delete\nwith the ids in the body, since a list of ids is not a path and a body on DELETE is what\nproxies drop.\n\nBoth deletes share one removal path. LocalTransport._delete_deletable removes a campaign the\nguard has passed and reports a structured outcome; delete_campaign raises the guard''s\nrefusals (400/409 over HTTP) and wraps the outcome, delete_campaigns turns them into\noutcomes. The cluster lane''s Job reap and token-Secret removal move onto that hook, so they\nrun for every id of a batch too.\n\nSurfaces:\n- CLI: vast campaign delete A B C, one line per id, non-zero exit if any was not fully\n  deleted; a single id goes through the same call.\n- MCP: delete_campaign takes one id or a list and returns the per-id results. No new tool;\n  the description is shorter than before, so the tool surface shrinks slightly.\n- Web UI: a selection mode on the campaign list (running campaigns not selectable), a\n  \"Delete N selected\" action, and one dialog that lists the ids and then shows each\n  outcome in place. openapi.json and api.generated.ts regenerated.\n\nDocs: web_ui, client, mcp and http_api describe the operation and its per-id answer.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqs9PfCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAALdkQABcQdyPD59vl7DUmsplj0pfX\n/sAt8X48ufsq5JRPKBz2psA3GSzUD+w2OCEAlmpygMdW08RMIB7mzJkCsK7ffxVY\nS72xg6eHNdYUiRoDYydAwptszeb4HGYg1OmuIyKfSuOmaD4QZTBIM200+92+NdJ7\nehNSaOxRwefjcorWXvdFQOtUuD0yi8bsnSKsThZEE3q6vRmXeOAZ2gu5J3DPwHMb\nbP/+XV+aBA02iivHI+TPgQG9VHh3ycGOBH3PFdVthp04ax2iDz5UnV0LetVYFcva\nNG496cwO9H8W3Pgn+KIm87cQeax6m4iQhHgLcFwMZUcoqtSDgDUjoPvX+N3lL+Nk\nkdgIUbNVwuYxKHbNUiAOPR02LnUBn8oZ58qKPf6VATby33hQeOFkalT7OcaU3iun\nL+H/orWHXMHl4bxxPTDJ2QAW9/UYoH05Ch+p16W3eRpJ6EcLaMhl3ClgWR8P7uCd\nbaXx/o3IfePNyDhIvV3AhJy2lhwZmmmSheh62NYWTx04NF9t2GsgSdP2/MSXP3F8\n5foGV4oKJ7DKCa/xM3Cfp7YgwJZSHzhbp680ompvjobw0iVd1tyATJt77x9qMHtS\nyfBvmvn342JjeL3nxFF50YxQSUxwmAdzOmUWYMwY9tI+L3jKc8DlLXocPYv3ZWb0\n8k2B+gjQkfwFOp/Mb99l\n=O4q1\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-23T13:27:59Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cps-test-lab/robovast/commit/3027d40f6ffbe765b64228ff85ce1a3e6f8c5af4","node_id":"C_kwDOPVaL7doAKDMwMjdkNDBmNmZmYmU3NjViNjQyMjhmZjg1Y2UxYTNlNmY4YzVhZjQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cps-test-lab/robovast/commit/9488c12778dd38c8a40208baa1c400210d212bb7","sha":"9488c12778dd38c8a40208baa1c400210d212bb7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/commits/9488c12778dd38c8a40208baa1c400210d212bb7"}],"sha":"3027d40f6ffbe765b64228ff85ce1a3e6f8c5af4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/commits/3027d40f6ffbe765b64228ff85ce1a3e6f8c5af4"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83823539?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fred-labs","id":83823539,"login":"fred-labs","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzODIzNTM5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/commits/9488c12778dd38c8a40208baa1c400210d212bb7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-23T13:27:15Z","email":"fred-labs@mailbox.org","name":"fred-labs"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-23T13:27:15Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Name a module alias and a late import as the linter reads them (#662)\n\nThe shared pylint configuration is what CI''s Scan job runs, so a test that is fine under\nthe project''s own run can still fail it. Three tests did: a module bound to a local name\nin upper case, and two imports that follow an ``importorskip`` guard and so cannot sit at\nthe top of the module. The guarded imports carry the pragma the rest of the tree uses for\nthem, and the one duplicate import of an already-imported module goes.","tree":{"sha":"e0aaf289e504f574f491a3fc5085668da6d9bbbb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/git/trees/e0aaf289e504f574f491a3fc5085668da6d9bbbb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/git/commits/9488c12778dd38c8a40208baa1c400210d212bb7","verification":{"payload":"tree e0aaf289e504f574f491a3fc5085668da6d9bbbb\nparent 14da1214a2ec72ea0c734c158e39e0698acb67a0\nauthor fred-labs <fred-labs@mailbox.org> 1790170035 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790170035 +0200\n\nName a module alias and a late import as the linter reads them (#662)\n\nThe shared pylint configuration is what CI''s Scan job runs, so a test that is fine under\nthe project''s own run can still fail it. Three tests did: a module bound to a local name\nin upper case, and two imports that follow an ``importorskip`` guard and so cannot sit at\nthe top of the module. The guarded imports carry the pragma the rest of the tree uses for\nthem, and the one duplicate import of an already-imported module goes.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqs9OzCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAADo0QAHCpDQOkjg2rSewyDxxbpGwi\nIUJEhutU9k3junblEbLnbTIOimOtgOABsCws1uIbIZlrF/wpTwflXlT2juW1GguK\nh/7xoOs7V5lYHfZZcdCx7cBJMi7rX8tw2qFQ+AF91Ke6oJ33yDo4OYW3LpwB6fo6\n6YTLNRzcjvx8YjtmaHfdn5B3DwX9lGZraxhkvBs3UaeHD3FgJRvC6740nKp7P/Xq\nFd5ny027tM9HqSb+nCLvo18B7l6QkxNn8j6Edv6dZlKC+Gwzk6idXNON+HnSx1/h\nXaKnF8uR6xuHQZo9ZJQbrF3hDUT5KI8kqEAUTSN7hc26KVAGyW48hINAsbiQdiIm\n6Ezfxr3T4LwqSxL1F2qCljd57OoGpLQpv1P9h5n47uNHkeEodGLX/OL0SKduPMrV\nmQcb8KI2yVkmPj287oDzz2wX8AEVdGlck31qmr1hHkA95iZwxoXdSOaqqmKGiOjR\nZMAZU+topNaH3LL+5JNE5M54wy9OOgjZaF84ja16bNfJWM+/nTiU4ccSIXn7++s4\nRhIlwW15VqLnz/6Ux7XY3khETaf3KF741JP4DKUneO2I53ttSP9o2BuoTF26cpFy\nzC720D5jfVNwBdZJli4CuYIbMzuOWgpz1+we+LKOGKMejtGgWx/6LfVDGW4cHVzX\n40SV7RUQdJMmmVVsurm1\n=xH3r\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-23T13:27:16Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cps-test-lab/robovast/commit/9488c12778dd38c8a40208baa1c400210d212bb7","node_id":"C_kwDOPVaL7doAKDk0ODhjMTI3NzhkZDM4YzhhNDAyMDhiYWExYzQwMDIxMGQyMTJiYjc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cps-test-lab/robovast/commit/14da1214a2ec72ea0c734c158e39e0698acb67a0","sha":"14da1214a2ec72ea0c734c158e39e0698acb67a0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/commits/14da1214a2ec72ea0c734c158e39e0698acb67a0"}],"sha":"9488c12778dd38c8a40208baa1c400210d212bb7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/commits/9488c12778dd38c8a40208baa1c400210d212bb7"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83823539?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fred-labs","id":83823539,"login":"fred-labs","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzODIzNTM5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/commits/14da1214a2ec72ea0c734c158e39e0698acb67a0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-22T21:29:50Z","email":"fred-labs@mailbox.org","name":"fred-labs"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-22T21:29:50Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Retire robovast_nav''s MCP plugin: its reads are answered by core for any robot type (#640)\n\nRemove robovast_nav/mcp_plugin.py and its robovast.mcp_plugins entry.\nEach tool''s question is answered by core: a track''s length, duration and\nspeeds by pose_track_view; an action''s feedback by its table through\nSQL; deviation from the planned path by get_track_deviation; obstacles\nand the planned path by get_config_contribution; the map with a run''s\ntrack by draw_config. The retired names are listed with their\nreplacements, and the core instructions route ''where a robot went'' to\nthe view and tools, which exist wherever robovast does.\n\nget_track_deviation and draw_config take the measurement clock from\ncampaign_ingest.pose_clock, the rule pose_track_view and the column\nnotes use. The developer guide''s MCP plugin section says what a domain\npackage contributes instead of read tools.","tree":{"sha":"6e1039e626b652e76068dca868c1c78560f47d7d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/git/trees/6e1039e626b652e76068dca868c1c78560f47d7d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/git/commits/14da1214a2ec72ea0c734c158e39e0698acb67a0","verification":{"payload":"tree 6e1039e626b652e76068dca868c1c78560f47d7d\nparent 6b4a13dde5052ac1048418d02239dcaae2ca7371\nauthor fred-labs <fred-labs@mailbox.org> 1790112590 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790112590 +0200\n\nRetire robovast_nav''s MCP plugin: its reads are answered by core for any robot type (#640)\n\nRemove robovast_nav/mcp_plugin.py and its robovast.mcp_plugins entry.\nEach tool''s question is answered by core: a track''s length, duration and\nspeeds by pose_track_view; an action''s feedback by its table through\nSQL; deviation from the planned path by get_track_deviation; obstacles\nand the planned path by get_config_contribution; the map with a run''s\ntrack by draw_config. The retired names are listed with their\nreplacements, and the core instructions route ''where a robot went'' to\nthe view and tools, which exist wherever robovast does.\n\nget_track_deviation and draw_config take the measurement clock from\ncampaign_ingest.pose_c