pe":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cps-test-lab/robovast/commit/14da1214a2ec72ea0c734c158e39e0698acb67a0","node_id":"C_kwDOPVaL7doAKDE0ZGExMjE0YTJlYzcyZWEwYzczNGMxNThlMzllMDY5OGFjYjY3YTA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cps-test-lab/robovast/commit/6b4a13dde5052ac1048418d02239dcaae2ca7371","sha":"6b4a13dde5052ac1048418d02239dcaae2ca7371","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/commits/6b4a13dde5052ac1048418d02239dcaae2ca7371"}],"sha":"14da1214a2ec72ea0c734c158e39e0698acb67a0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/commits/14da1214a2ec72ea0c734c158e39e0698acb67a0"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83823539?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fred-labs","id":83823539,"login":"fred-labs","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzODIzNTM5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/commits/6b4a13dde5052ac1048418d02239dcaae2ca7371/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-22T21:26:06Z","email":"fred-labs@mailbox.org","name":"fred-labs"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-22T21:26:06Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Summarise every recorded track in one view, on its measurement clock (#635)\n\n`pose_track_view` gives one row per track -- one frame of one run as one\npose-contract table recorded it -- with its point count, 3D length,\nduration, average and maximum speed, largest single step, start and end\npose, and bounding box, computed over every recorded pose.\n\nThe view is generated over whichever tables follow the pose contract, so\n`poses` (from a bag) and `sim_poses` (from the simulator) both appear,\nand a new producer''s table does on the next ingest without registration.\nEach contributes on its own measurement clock: `stamp` where the table\nhas one, else `timestamp`. That choice now lives in one helper,\n`campaign_ingest.pose_clock`, which the column notes use too, so the\nnotes and the view cannot name different clocks. A sample with no\nmeasurement time (a latched /tf_static transform) is not a point on a\ntrack.\n\nThe window partitions by the whole track key, so a `WHERE campaign_id`\non the view reaches each table underneath instead of being applied after\nthe corpus has been windowed; a test reads the plan to pin that.\n\nA reposition counts as travel: a body spawned at the origin and then\nplaced at its start pose adds that jump to the length. The view does not\nguess a threshold to drop it; `max_step_m` makes it visible, and the\ndescription says how to read it.","tree":{"sha":"c0d93578d26624952448c84044453155e060ed11","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/git/trees/c0d93578d26624952448c84044453155e060ed11"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/git/commits/6b4a13dde5052ac1048418d02239dcaae2ca7371","verification":{"payload":"tree c0d93578d26624952448c84044453155e060ed11\nparent d963eca6972c464c565ddcc8afb42232c00095d0\nauthor fred-labs <fred-labs@mailbox.org> 1790112366 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790112366 +0200\n\nSummarise every recorded track in one view, on its measurement clock (#635)\n\n`pose_track_view` gives one row per track -- one frame of one run as one\npose-contract table recorded it -- with its point count, 3D length,\nduration, average and maximum speed, largest single step, start and end\npose, and bounding box, computed over every recorded pose.\n\nThe view is generated over whichever tables follow the pose contract, so\n`poses` (from a bag) and `sim_poses` (from the simulator) both appear,\nand a new producer''s table does on the next ingest without registration.\nEach contributes on its own measurement clock: `stamp` where the table\nhas one, else `timestamp`. That choice now lives in one helper,\n`campaign_ingest.pose_clock`, which the column notes use too, so the\nnotes and the view cannot name different clocks. A sample with no\nmeasurement time (a latched /tf_static transform) is not a point on a\ntrack.\n\nThe window partitions by the whole track key, so a `WHERE campaign_id`\non the view reaches each table underneath instead of being applied after\nthe corpus has been windowed; a test reads the plan to pin that.\n\nA reposition counts as travel: a body spawned at the origin and then\nplaced at its start pose adds that jump to the length. The view does not\nguess a threshold to drop it; `max_step_m` makes it visible, and the\ndescription says how to read it.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqsvJuCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAVNkQAIdZv8lsPEeYbpQ8z0/Q9yh2\n6ALXuvDp8Nr2np6dErsB8TdHlR0fQQxEpW96iblp0qWzlec8TibhBYpmv4AOLyZb\nR/st1wh6K4kl6l4T520m7MscUAAickdJyKVt1Bw64rPYRuJLNphwuRDT2kJr88bN\nGamBs9npUvko4R6OlGPf+jP4KfUZFQeW+VuVcujuIjGG9CCmhCoPdBbAc2uZsOq8\ndFktcN+VHMKncbf5Z7X8WFLQWFVb+N6SDrII3SA0U9wECIdQrnHxj6RmSKx+TYwB\nqCQOZRQkV1rIv4AOTMm+qVuvx4uZJ94uRxon5lqZ7s0oLUE9IzXxABohKAXhST5C\nb07awE569LqIISiU7VAQjzbtVwvuq6W01Zp/NtvbZNe/cwmiMSKdTxNM3ElxnIrm\n1hG3Z2EUVd4gQdFc2hdjwD8+roF4cquNHzARRVS/ghbOYumdaCaS50IQA1deDSms\nLItvWm/BVCGr9fM3SRsAN2BRJm4txzsbXxlgKczjY3OtZ/7wvQZMrT45Xz6YjA0f\ni4oQNYk6NidyfEoUNsP6e5Y0aqUDI0qyOUOTd8L30klzpN4KxE6ZxZlM7L/7P+FU\n2n1/wBIk7nA6RK5JGAuOX/1byYr/9/BgON5d