ents_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fred-labs","id":83823539,"login":"fred-labs","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzODIzNTM5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/commits/a1d73a25d05c329746abb166d02af5ed30b64628/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-22T21:08:22Z","email":"fred-labs@mailbox.org","name":"fred-labs"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-22T21:08:22Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Serve a campaign configuration''s contribution, and measure a track against its path (#638)\n\nTwo interface operations in core, generic over the pose contract rather than over\nnavigation, threaded through the models, Routes, both transports, the HTTP routes\nand the MCP plugin.\n\nget_config_contribution reports what one configuration''s variations placed -- the\nmarkers its config view draws and the files its panels read -- derived from the\nfrozen .vast and configurations.yaml rather than stored, and shared with the\nworkspace preview through one collector. A variation type that cannot be resolved\nlands in errors instead of an empty view.\n\nget_track_deviation measures every pose of one recorded track against a path\nmarker of its configuration, on a connection scoped to that campaign so no reply\ncap thins the track, and reports the driven length beside the path''s and the\nratio between them. A path that states no height is compared in the plane, and\nboth lengths are then measured there too. With several paths and none named, the\ncall is refused with their labels rather than guessing.\n\nnav_get_obstacles and nav_get_path_deviation are retired. The first answered only\nfor a campaign that happened to name its obstacle parameter `static_objects`, a\nname each campaign binds for itself, and reported an empty list for any other;\nthe contribution reports the same placements from the variation that made them.\nThe second measured its cross-track figures over one capped reply.","tree":{"sha":"782f6c98bb6a278611052157f895e5d1b3955128","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/git/trees/782f6c98bb6a278611052157f895e5d1b3955128"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/git/commits/a1d73a25d05c329746abb166d02af5ed30b64628","verification":{"payload":"tree 782f6c98bb6a278611052157f895e5d1b3955128\nparent ece5d5f708715c55d6429b635c5f914f7a69efba\nauthor fred-labs <fred-labs@mailbox.org> 1790111302 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790111302 +0200\n\nServe a campaign configuration''s contribution, and measure a track against its path (#638)\n\nTwo interface operations in core, generic over the pose contract rather than over\nnavigation, threaded through the models, Routes, both transports, the HTTP routes\nand the MCP plugin.\n\nget_config_contribution reports what one configuration''s variations placed -- the\nmarkers its config view draws and the files its panels read -- derived from the\nfrozen .vast and configurations.yaml rather than stored, and shared with the\nworkspace preview through one collector. A variation type that cannot be resolved\nlands in errors instead of an empty view.\n\nget_track_deviation measures every pose of one recorded track against a path\nmarker of its configuration, on a connection scoped to that campaign so no reply\ncap thins the track, and reports the driven length beside the path''s and the\nratio between them. A path that states no height is compared in the plane, and\nboth lengths are then measured there too. With several paths and none named, the\ncall is refused with their labels rather than guessing.\n\nnav_get_obstacles and nav_get_path_deviation are retired. The first answered only\nfor a campaign that happened to name its obstacle parameter `static_objects`, a\nname each campaign binds for itself, and reported an empty list for any other;\nthe contribution reports the same placements from the variation that made them.\nThe second measured its cross-track figures over one capped reply.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqsu5GCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAd0wQAK/Awh2viQeuRJ9UtivkgZML\nnp5rlDnObiTrlBiFEbN2B2Hn6oxGy+a9EBr0TT1qHJXmCAf7b8k/p3I0vTmPcuFI\nS4RbyAyfYZJlqGFuQ52wzeYYzBpedN7XqDoyTLtT2T2GYkirenceqrIblRfimYZH\n6biQOXc4oA0e5IyaRNM3KREvWLoLSZQxVmCFzuH+D5fNJktFziBgfSI9X/0rCm22\nxDgu0axTp6lBOpAPlzUZyTlnKh2qsS7NnZMloNwSUfEll4bmTnyHIgIJxRgs/kIi\nCS/gwfau/zMfWc3EyVjtYQKm92F3fEvFc5zg0qMezGnzYzLNQoiilZSy4Me0f39B\nAHTsB4P5pt5jYUlM/c2E5hPYSZpoheeGBaohRj6++kBxCA3Pw3S+l+F/EoFjxnmU\noOhkpvI5mKfbLFJWMgVdMA6ZjcUEjQWPwD6bPeiWRnwfhukjKAN3GOur5JpVTH1y\nV5VrIvA58c0kIxuME0rrH/6PMXVeRjahtQGgCxrEBV48bEDhu3nfXBn62b3nHpOz\nS7nec7FTCkZgWj6p/FSm14YyjXJLYgNJDs8gdJogamgdhdnv7fuQfYDRM2WgP5Yw\nyAvSFAXmIWjWx17ruY4yhSBB5JWnux1IWS+/Ej7LyuPSls15nzWEUFqX2WEZI40h\nK7CRLeiCnS1iARbRo2wC\n=v7BX\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-22T21:08:23Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cps-test-lab/robovast/commit/a1d73a25d05c329746abb166d02af5ed30b64628","node_id":"C_kwDOPVaL7doAKGExZDczYTI1ZDA1YzMyOTc0NmFiYjE2NmQwMmFmNWVkMzBiNjQ2Mjg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cps-test-lab/robovast/commit/ece5d5f708715c55d6429b635c5f914f7a69efba","sha":"ece5d5f708715c55d6429b635c5f914f7a69efba","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/commits/ece5d5f708715c55d6429b635c5f914f7a69efba"}],"sha":"a1d73a25d05c329746abb166d02af5ed30b64628","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/commits/a1d73a25d05c329746abb166d02af5ed30b64628"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83823539?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fred-labs","id":83823539,"login":"fred-labs","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzODIzNTM5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/commits/ece5d5f708715c55d6429b635c5f914f7a69efba/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-22T20:50:26Z","email":"fred-labs@mailbox.org","name":"fred-labs"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-22T20:50:26Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Advise on a world key the pinned image''s plugin does not publish (#650)\n\nA campaign runs a pinned image, and a world can be newer than it. A key a later\nplugin reads is, to the image''s older plugin, a key nobody reads, and most plugins\ndo not refuse one: the run starts, the key does nothing, and the result looks\nconfigured.\n\nvalidate_project''s world check now compares, for every component the world\ndocument declares, its top-level config keys against what that image''s own plugin\npublishes (`python3 -m roqsim.introspection describe`: parameters, and schema\nwhere declared). A key missing from it is an advice-level problem naming the image,\nthe plugin, the component and the key; `valid` is unaffected. A plugin whose schema\ndeclares strict_keys has a complete list by its own declaration, and the advice\nsays the image will refuse the key. Otherwise the published list is the plugin''s\ndocumented Config block, which can leave out a key the plugin does read, and the\nwording states what the catalog shows and what follows if it is complete.\n\nNot compared: the keys roqsim accepts on any component (roqsim.schema.INJECTED_KEYS,\nread from the image''s own interpreter since its catalog does not publish them),\ncomponents a model''s manifest adds, plugins that publish no keys, and plugins\nloaded by path. A catalog that cannot be read is itself advice saying the keys\nwere not checked.\n\nThe catalog commands, their parsing and the per-image cache move from the MCP\nimage_catalog plugin into robovast.service.image_catalog, so the MCP tools and the\nworld check share one cache keyed by the resolved image identity; the uncached\nplugins of one world are asked in one exec. The web UI lists advice on a valid\nreport, as the CLI and MCP already do.","tree":{"sha":"a54a53f0051a3c751233552c62a823c674af85b3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/git/trees/a54a53f0051a3c751233552c62a823c674af85b3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/git/commits/ece5d5f708715c55d6429b635c5f914f7a69efba","verification":{"payload":"tree a54a53f0051a3c751233552c62a823c674af85b3\nparent 9e48647822d9d16e25ab0132e1106da0062297bb\nauthor fred-labs <fred-labs@mailbox.org> 1790110226 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790110226 +0200\n\nAdvise on a world key the pinned image''s plugin does not publish (#650)\n\nA campaign runs a pinned image, and a world can be newer than it. A key a later\nplugin reads is, to the image''s older plugin, a key nobody reads, and most plugins\ndo not refuse one: the run starts, the key does nothing, and the result looks\nconfigured.\n\nvalidate_project''s world check now compares, for every component the world\ndocument declares, its top-level config keys against what that image''s own plugin\npublishes (`python3 -m roqsim.introspection describe`: parameters, and schema\nwhere declared). A key missing from it is an advice-level problem naming the image,\nthe plugin, the component and the key; `valid` is unaffected. A plugin whose schema\ndeclares strict_keys has a complete list by its own declaration, and the advice\nsays the image will refuse the key. Otherwise the published list is the plugin''s\ndocumented Config block, which can leave out a key the plugin does read, and the\nwording states what the catalog shows and what follows if it is complete.\n\nNot compared: the keys roqsim accepts on any component (roqsim.schema.INJECTED_KEYS,\nread from the image''s own interpreter since its catalog does not publish them),\ncomponents a model''s manifest adds, plugins that publish no keys, and plugins\nloaded by path. A catalog that cannot be read is itself advice saying the keys\nwere not checked.\n\nThe catalog commands, their parsing and the per-image cache move from the MCP\nimage_catalog plugin into robovast.service.image_catalog, so the MCP tools and the\nworld check share one cache keyed by the resolved image identity; the uncached\nplugins of one world are asked in one exec. The web UI lists advice on a valid\nreport, as the CLI and MCP already do.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqsuoSCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAo1AQAJhOjvzmYfOIgat/xCvBC+5K\nS0WUsqOgzeDeWvwZwN7ynObChYlWvUMzLTVjFK+mPBigfbz7px8P+hB69F2Jtf0u\nGfPPACFfBkckp9kF9GvNFb4oBD3vZ9Kn6b995XptrdYO6wTGzkZOwWP9bMeZjik/\nVUUDj1bjiAdI2JoL0vSBO2xtYkiURD510Q1LZDao8qpDX+Vo5LUnLt121+5BZJbK\nOSfgQBqU8N5N65UUobobm4fDkGx0OfTvYdo1QhuMyUH9knscj/DAuGPAjI7ZrTaQ\n/l2LWyaLSL8IJrEpKlfLfJfRqY5II+HvVN6fqHIwoB7KfI2ja5ZC/OysewgcqyB0\nT7+o84zLIwCyUvMbIVpMKHMzCjb1doKuU9vT8gdqHAtoYfybmY/zBxNVVFKPJYvc\nh6VUFF2t/1OMKbvwIehVLgU5n8/5IESx87zlpzz/yxcExIDXFS37TsJoXiDXoiLt\nNRl61OVaNuFFWgg3VLrHdjfqxLDoqU86FNkwcu4jHFYBSA6gsL1KWZPR+VL34VZx\nGuxh9RcrfDH2SQcib+t93+rndFRKn0bDiAAFtCfK0pWQIFXE88s1ewpRUEDjfW+Z\n6Gy8ZhXqpoeUmncyCexBLpY0IgNqb2HeBuAM4d3fiHMpg2R9LS3M5z6I2cr9YzpZ\nF/E9CmgCeD2kJD2podYP\n=znmU\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-22T20:50:27Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","or