user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/commits/9e48647822d9d16e25ab0132e1106da0062297bb/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-22T20:39:24Z","email":"fred-labs@mailbox.org","name":"fred-labs"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-22T20:39:24Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Classify which simulator a campaign ran (#660)\n\nAn image is built from a resolved roqsim commit and labelled with it, and every\nimage derived from it keeps the label, so a campaign already records which\nsimulator produced its results. Nothing read it: a campaign whose images were\nbuilt from two different roqsim commits classified as reproducible, though its\nruns did not all meet the same simulator -- which no image digest says, since\nimages differ legitimately for other reasons.\n\nThe manifest now names the simulator: a commit is an identification, a moving\nref is not, and two commits across one campaign''s images are opaque. A campaign\nwhose images name no simulator contributes no entry.","tree":{"sha":"71bc90c2395a0946bc72ba99150174e376b53091","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/git/trees/71bc90c2395a0946bc72ba99150174e376b53091"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/git/commits/9e48647822d9d16e25ab0132e1106da0062297bb","verification":{"payload":"tree 71bc90c2395a0946bc72ba99150174e376b53091\nparent 7b3cd0bbf5cc151e16f1d61b7c9adc2a0c9a78ba\nauthor fred-labs <fred-labs@mailbox.org> 1790109564 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790109564 +0200\n\nClassify which simulator a campaign ran (#660)\n\nAn image is built from a resolved roqsim commit and labelled with it, and every\nimage derived from it keeps the label, so a campaign already records which\nsimulator produced its results. Nothing read it: a campaign whose images were\nbuilt from two different roqsim commits classified as reproducible, though its\nruns did not all meet the same simulator -- which no image digest says, since\nimages differ legitimately for other reasons.\n\nThe manifest now names the simulator: a commit is an identification, a moving\nref is not, and two commits across one campaign''s images are opaque. A campaign\nwhose images name no simulator contributes no entry.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqsud8CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAALqcQAGmHeFEBWVfY+Kj1DmCm7+Hj\n8zEu87ynhf+gc2bMf9G0A+Ky1c/8OaW5jN/oZwT1eKhaqnGelEU0+EvuKzhY58RM\nFWNLIFVSa7B2WYaG0NetrpllO57OiH5QzHYbjLUnR9i/SuicAswzaTtcyQZSW4tC\nQxuAjQTz2MiCuq5Bmw7J7zk84pmE7WKeRx2QB5Hfh/QfevoP0YZN0j+gk5nZt+qt\ngvFIIKzd8DBdAlSo4riEtEm9q4ilpcW6VMNrRjXCffFDkyEcQea+zpkFB9+37ilS\nRMCboxO3KGE/1H+Bt4LI2dLBLBPDgZLVwOupqG60QvkT7ZqTmi6iTXaMfA0VG0Hj\nf+F+DM5ix31BCtsVYN//LAoReDp+Jj9CQuHE0Vqx8rjx4uX14YspcNEl5tRCHGqn\nrSudraWGxAT+GnJoYV7P9/StChZYi2IeUk7BUAh7yDtK3vP+OrfTx4EckKWCaBBi\nip21J3gtEpyBXzoSUo/RTEU0/RW/wdzCcmmsaNRwJwCSCiKXdHRqCy7gW6Nupz++\n6u5wNgtYVrd8oYPozqjhGAz/KeUbEhvBUZ4UxrpKk9+k5NCL76luhkBjvmNs/QOv\nVLQzevzLasR6V2UtTEwb4MEcrlP+Vmn5xeUd1a2CrNcbA1DIsYOsEAUWtwMz/d6s\npevKjIsJqSpN1SvaIFN8\n=9jxb\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-22T20:39:25Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cps-test-lab/robovast/commit/9e48647822d9d16e25ab0132e1106da0062297bb","node_id":"C_kwDOPVaL7doAKDllNDg2NDc4MjJkOWQxNmUyNWFiMDEzMmUxMTA2ZGEwMDYyMjk3YmI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cps-test-lab/robovast/commit/7b3cd0bbf5cc151e16f1d61b7c9adc2a0c9a78ba","sha":"7b3cd0bbf5cc151e16f1d61b7c9adc2a0c9a78ba","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/commits/7b3cd0bbf5cc151e16f1d61b7c9adc2a0c9a78ba"}],"sha":"9e48647822d9d16e25ab0132e1106da0062297bb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/commits/9e48647822d9d16e25ab0132e1106da0062297bb"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83823539?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fred-labs","id":83823539,"login":"fred-labs","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzODIzNTM5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/commits/7b3cd0bbf5cc151e16f1d61b7c9adc2a0c9a78ba/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-22T20:27:05Z","email":"fred-labs@mailbox.org","name":"fred-labs"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-22T20:27:05Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Build the images from pushed commits only (#658)\n\nEach image had a second source: --roqsim-src and --scenario-execution-src\nreplaced a Dockerfile''s clone stage with a checkout on disk. An image built that\nway carries a commit no repository records, so a campaign that ran it cannot say\nwhat to rebuild it from, nor which simulator it ran.\n\nThe two flags are gone, with what they cost: the rsync staging that had to strip\nroqsim''s fetched external assets out of a working tree, the release script''s\nmutual-exclusion rule against --roqsim-ref and its checkout validation, and the\nexplanations of which source a build used in two scripts and two doc pages.\n\nROQSIM_REF and SCENARIO_EXECUTION_REF name what is cloned, and that is the one\npath; iterating on unpushed work means pushing a branch. A one-off build from a\ntree on disk is buildx''s own --build-context <stage>=<path>, which replaces a\nclone stage without a flag here, and the simulator image still refuses a source\ntree carrying assets roqsim does not publish however that context was filled.","tree":{"sha":"bc24ac3e8eef442082dcb8de3cb678f79a2f1664","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/git/trees/bc24ac3e8eef442082dcb8de3cb678f79a2f1664"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/git/commits/7b3cd0bbf5cc151e16f1d61b7c9adc2a0c9a78ba","verification":{"payload":"tree bc24ac3e8eef442082dcb8de3cb678f79a2f1664\nparent 8814cdff57f77f9f17313edca32ce1513706cdf6\nauthor fred-labs <fred-labs@mailbox.org> 1790108825 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790108825 +0200\n\nBuild the images from pushed commits only (#658)\n\nEach image had a second source: --roqsim-src and --scenario-execution-src\nreplaced a Dockerfile''s clone stage with a checkout on disk. An image built that\nway carries a commit no repository records, so a campaign that ran it cannot say\nwhat to rebuild it from, nor which simulator it ran.\n\nThe two flags are gone, with what they cost: the rsync staging that had to strip\nroqsim''s fetched external assets out of a working tree, the release script''s\nmutual-exclusion rule against --roqsim-ref and its checkout validation, and the\nexplanations of which source a build used in two scripts and two doc pages.\n\nROQSIM_REF and SCENARIO_EXECUTION_REF name what is cloned, and that is the one\npath; iterating on unpushed work means pushing a branch. A one-off build from a\ntree on disk is buildx''s own --build-context <stage>=<path>, which replaces a\nclone stage without a flag here, and the simulator image still refuses a source\ntree carrying assets roqsim does not publish however that context was filled.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqsuSZCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAXBsQAJYD25Tu9tRK+8rYrETbdNGy\n7FcZjx9HFVe3Y65PhnCpkXhh47d9Jd/alDvOviEBHqE7c131brSpWrW14QkKkWVy\nWFQHU/4aXMg7yHDSb+oiDETFtr2Dbiwd+uGXFqURBe1stAS+jEHBSlNYOVmB7hMJ\ntEuagWk/OS9rM/JJl+AsEG/B2AK/6Ild3l5MAlZjkkO/vIJKypzNluYRmjD90QDc\nK05Jmxs6e7TqfrpkhmThkpRlwJTlVbH6Ywm225xy1EEA9Kh/iWYm5VXVjSQA5LHN\nAHjmf4ChlBzTGu70QtahliYHB/ZsVzNoDu1RomRwF4R05lck3OWAljhCXcCalQTg\n66fPMqiocsitK8XMbOJW/0ctgw7GN0V3JWw5uZBSA9HDL7+BaQtv/kbFYQi59Cq6\nZB+/5M2UW+CBKIwo8803c3WFIwsQkuHu8jG/YJsJq/FcBMlghX9+yaye2a3yxPqD\nChqYUjAoSeDmrPlyOATE0jrILuqvL6yUyCxt2Qi5auF4GlXgQu0y/BHokNh5JPuz\noKDRP0oPNLZMXcn4PAMNty9DHqNhn1pRBB7SlvFMZg+fF8K7nj1gnSO1cOlD1/qr\nVxudu7KdaU0XAuKa4SfNQrh7PitsHZMAwwREAGngK2XtS/4n3+luIjq2D4PoCBnj\nZzz9kKOMRcjo4qd+AhU9\n=2yLo\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-22T20:27:06Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cps-test-lab/robovast/commit/7b3cd0bbf5cc151e16f1d61b7c9adc2a0c9a78ba","node_id":"C_kwDOPVaL7doAKDdiM2NkMGJiZjVjYzE1MWUxNmYxZDYxYjdjOWFkYzJhMGM5YTc4YmE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cps-test-lab/robovast/commit/8814cdff57f77f9f17313edca32ce1513706cdf6","sha":"8814cdff57f77f9f17313edca32ce1513706cdf6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/commits/8814cdff57f77f9f17313edca32ce1513706cdf6"}],"sha":"7b3cd0bbf5cc151e16f1d61b7c9adc2a0c9a78ba","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/commits/7b3cd0bbf5cc151e16f1d61b7c9adc2a0c9a78ba"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83823539?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fred-labs","id":83823539,"login":"fred-labs","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzODIzNTM5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/commits/8814cdff57f77f9f17313edca32ce1513706cdf6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-22T20:11:22Z","email":"fred-labs@mailbox.org","name":"fred-labs"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-22T20:11:22Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Keep a run switch in the run view from reloading what did not change (#649)\n\n* Keep a run switch in the run view from reloading what did not change\n\nSwitching run rebuilt everything behind the view, including what belongs to the\ncampaign or the world rather than the run.\n\n- The parsed scene model is leased from a small client-side cache keyed by the\n  descriptor URL and parked when the panel unmounts, so the next run of the same\n  world is seated in it, reset to rest, with no fetch and no rebuild. The viewport\n  is still one per mount: PanelHost remounts every panel per run, and keeping it\n  would mean every panel handling a changing provider.\n- /describe is read through the query cache under one key per campaign, so the\n  providers of its runs share one answer instead of each asking again.\n- Scene assets are served Cache-Control: private, max-age=31536000, immutable.\n  The key in their path fingerprints everything an entry is compiled from and an\n  entry is never rewritten under its key, so the URL names its bytes. /results\n  files get no such header.\n- The service memoises a run''s scene identity for a campaign at rest, against the\n  rest key plus the stat of the run''s capture. That identity hashes every\n  campaign-file tree a world reads and, for a tag-only campaign, asks Docker.\n\nThe local_file docstring said the cluster lane fetches the object behind an\naddress; both lanes serve from the results root on the service''s own disk.\n\n* The viewport shows a scene root and does not own it\n\nA model outlives the viewport that displayed it: sceneModelCache parks one for\nthe next mount, and React tears the viewport down before the lease is released.\nA viewport that freed the graph it was shown would hand that mount an emptied\nmodel, which renders as a world with nothing in it rather than as an error.\n\ndetachSceneRoot takes the root out of the viewport, and is what both a scene swap\nand dispose do with it. Whoever loaded the model frees it: the cache for a leased\none, the config panel for its own.","tree":{"sha":"84e413f21128713a13c9b4307a05c7253c9bb7e9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/git/trees/84e413f21128713a13c9b4307a05c7253c9bb7e9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/git/commits/8814cdff57f77f9f17313edca32ce1513706cdf6","verification":{"payload":"tree 84e413f21128713a13c9b4307a05c7253c9bb7e9\nparent 0a4e448d422ee1e689e16f63cc4df6950bde098d\nauthor fred-labs <fred-labs@mailbox.org> 1790107882 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790107882 +0200\n\nKeep a run switch in the run view from reloading what did not change (#649)\n\n* Keep a run switch in the run view from reloading what did not change\n\nSwitching run rebuilt everything behind the view, including what belongs to the\ncampaign or the world rather than the run.\n\n- The parsed scene model is leased from a small client-side cache keyed by the\n  descriptor URL and parked when the panel unmounts, so the next run of the same\n  world is seated in it, reset to rest, with no fetch and no rebuild. The viewport\n  is still one per mount: PanelHost remounts every panel per run, and keeping it\n  would mean every panel handling a changing provider.\n- /describe is read through the query cache under one key per campaign, so the\n  providers of its runs share one answer instead of each asking again.\n- Scene assets are served Cache-Control: private, max-age=31536000, immutable.\n  The key in their path fingerprints everything an entry is compiled from and an\n  entry is never rewritten under its key, so the URL names its bytes. /results\n  files get no such header.\n- The service memoises a run''s scene identity for a campaign at rest, against the\n  rest key plus the stat of the run''s capture. That identity hashes every\n  campaign-file tree a world reads and, for a tag-only campaign, asks Docker.\n\nThe local_file docstring said the cluster lane fetches the object behind an\naddress; both lanes serve from the results root on the service''s own disk.\n\n* The viewport shows a scene root and does not own it\n\nA model outlives the viewport that displayed it: sceneModelCache parks one for\nthe next mount, and React tears the viewport down before the lease is released.\nA viewport that freed the graph it was shown would hand that mount an emptied\nmodel, which renders as a world with nothing in it rather than as an error.\n\ndetachSceneRoot takes the root out of the viewport, and is what both a scene swap\nand dispose do with it. Whoever loaded the model frees it: the cache for a leased\none, the config panel for its own.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqsuDqCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAM0IQACjQq5WsyY5yjh0zKi10JxkN\nG2juxeIq3MnpmfyCP+aPeUcLgG3UXVeWuAUuAvWmSGLuiEr/V47g8eJ1ALr0NEOA\n+PaEpRN9XjKzXgOTUs18Yqefh5mgk4qoT6BNvSeOBlX3hIcpB3LqJL319riHgfTR\n2XvRyYAJp+AQJEsnQ3FaNAlwZTx9I0nED0a5eVXFJFX6jvQ8sUXG+o+K/Nkfr9z2\nOiSWrkUGdLIl5H7lcQeb8xQyC3wB29nM48UxEgMVg58fCY7zMebr+R/5upAHYY8D\nskT9X80BxRfNexDkF+do+Bdy4y0fVF/Hu2ThYbbACI/paefUbHp8Wk/B4Am5VC4N\ngiyplE2ZYR5x11KUMO/N2H7Tmu75EcXAh+4EQqH+DtGtZcP+UBag5yujQ49SaVrI\nrSAoVMJoGQcpbVUvR4cskhaDz9tbhKCUyp7k27+GXgSiRvREy+kl/R3aObyD1/aC\n3Lybcie/UBewGwqHSmIW+SviGHmStBYkG3mure9QadbDyPZpoKZxCbpb7TRP0rMO\nvE572H8I1JVHeZmUmIC3bFl1UeI0u3wS85H844OKRCtPvYuM8vuinUgd4qKb/IK3\nQL5Z4W+cGJp2lqCfBi8qzTquAbCVEGc9wErvw8EyLyU2c+J37gvhwOjNFHarC+we\ndfXsM6e9EYSoeoHPp+x6\n=Li6t\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","