:83823539,"login":"fred-labs","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzODIzNTM5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/commits/aa034f994381befc11b5eb466bc92b01b78586fa/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-22T19:48:33Z","email":"fred-labs@mailbox.org","name":"fred-labs"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-22T19:48:33Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"A campaign stopped before any run gets no postprocessing pass (#629)\n\n* A campaign stopped before any run gets no postprocessing pass\n\nThe stopped path runs the analysis a stopped campaign is owed for its finished batches,\nand ran it unconditionally. A campaign stopped before any run existed has none: the pass\nreads run directories and nothing else, so it derived nothing -- and on the cluster lane\nit is a Job of its own, a pod scheduled on a node to read an empty campaign. Since a stop\nlands wherever a campaign is, that is the common shape of an early stop: staging,\ninstalling plugins, waiting for an image, composing, or Jobs still queued.\n\n`campaign_has_runs` answers the one question the pass depends on -- does any configuration\nhave a run directory -- and is false for a campaign directory that does not exist yet,\nwhere a campaign stopped while starting is. The stopped path asks it first and skips a pass\nwith nothing to read, saying so in the campaign log; the campaign still ends `stopped`,\nwith no postprocessing error, since there was nothing to fail at. Run directories rather\nthan any other sign of progress because they are exactly what the pass would read, and on\nthe cluster the stopped path runs after the batch has swept its Jobs, so no delivery can\nstill arrive behind the check.\n\n* An unreadable campaign directory raises instead of reading as no runs\n\n\"No runs\" and \"unreadable\" both skip the postprocessing pass, so a directory\nthat cannot be read must not answer the first: the campaign is then missing its\nderived data with nothing said. Only an absent directory is no runs.","tree":{"sha":"81f68471e01e7e0ec88a8acd83df48e85f88f3b1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/git/trees/81f68471e01e7e0ec88a8acd83df48e85f88f3b1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/git/commits/aa034f994381befc11b5eb466bc92b01b78586fa","verification":{"payload":"tree 81f68471e01e7e0ec88a8acd83df48e85f88f3b1\nparent a6fa623c11523e51cbf3b7f548e03901b8da5cf9\nauthor fred-labs <fred-labs@mailbox.org> 1790106513 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790106513 +0200\n\nA campaign stopped before any run gets no postprocessing pass (#629)\n\n* A campaign stopped before any run gets no postprocessing pass\n\nThe stopped path runs the analysis a stopped campaign is owed for its finished batches,\nand ran it unconditionally. A campaign stopped before any run existed has none: the pass\nreads run directories and nothing else, so it derived nothing -- and on the cluster lane\nit is a Job of its own, a pod scheduled on a node to read an empty campaign. Since a stop\nlands wherever a campaign is, that is the common shape of an early stop: staging,\ninstalling plugins, waiting for an image, composing, or Jobs still queued.\n\n`campaign_has_runs` answers the one question the pass depends on -- does any configuration\nhave a run directory -- and is false for a campaign directory that does not exist yet,\nwhere a campaign stopped while starting is. The stopped path asks it first and skips a pass\nwith nothing to read, saying so in the campaign log; the campaign still ends `stopped`,\nwith no postprocessing error, since there was nothing to fail at. Run directories rather\nthan any other sign of progress because they are exactly what the pass would read, and on\nthe cluster the stopped path runs after the batch has swept its Jobs, so no delivery can\nstill arrive behind the check.\n\n* An unreadable campaign directory raises instead of reading as no runs\n\n\"No runs\" and \"unreadable\" both skip the postprocessing pass, so a directory\nthat cannot be read must not answer the first: the campaign is then missing its\nderived data with nothing said. Only an absent directory is no runs.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqstuRCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAZvoQAK1I6ns0F/Zj8YvDSex3+qjN\nBTX5eOlPfVDSkjTOcHefgzdD7ewdcFrbAsMSSz+LMyset4US7i5D3tcTHy5LKKki\nn/7SMRsykfokMk7FYjwfQKag4xw3eexsCRNW1c2o19+8yUnO0xSMII+YGN1k8JU0\nNkVOYh+KhS026xFVmefaNF3LejVEfMmpWX7jft0QrO2vp5mYs6EUeCHDVvm+BP+C\nm+VuZo0QU4xbamO+OXznso5PNTrQMF3JsXBOVOXuitb131h43ir72/LsWUcmti80\nfEm4SY/l9cFD7a371QOsUJHg/k0mVG5wYXO7R3vV7HYpqX5/NSoaF7iR65JoX9Cr\nc0V+J78pBFvFXRese2WLR4BZLbDUq96KT+ELAJUY2AHHfNOIyLOrP3vr1sRmsh9P\nzse8tztc3GFMOrcZL/mNgfYDWNdpz9MDjFnz5AWK27rLxoi1RKiRFqaqcn5RJLqi\nz5PGu98W1ZnnGXpS2GheR4j23zklNveUoZDaCMz0EVKRqFqU6nDcnuh2qKIxu/n7\ncewvg8/Qzwoa/sr50cg0rKqUoUoPoQpYkzPJ67Wqlf1HGgKHFL+EoE0LQ+iyj7x2\nrekTJHGVrCgf7qYNFbQjib4wkkF9xIFmz4dLXXeWtmeVbOLalfn56JKDqQg6IOIF\n3EMC14Vifo8LXZidkyMR\n=nzA2\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-22T19:48:33Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":198644