e03901b8da5cf9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/commits/a6fa623c11523e51cbf3b7f548e03901b8da5cf9"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83823539?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fred-labs","id":83823539,"login":"fred-labs","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzODIzNTM5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/commits/3a306932e9dc1b3626e6eeb6c591ec37390439cd/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-22T19:35:12Z","email":"fred-labs@mailbox.org","name":"fred-labs"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-22T19:35:12Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Drop the read_only flag nothing sets (#654)\n\nWorkspaceInfo.read_only was always False: a pinned directory is writable, and the\ntwo things it may not take -- a whole-tree sync and a delete -- are refused by\nWorkspaceRegistry.require_syncable and by the delete path. The field is gone,\nwith the UI chips and the disabled delete button that branched on it, and the\narchitecture page says what a pin actually refuses.","tree":{"sha":"d10a1ab63fd7cf7346adc441509f239837845308","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/git/trees/d10a1ab63fd7cf7346adc441509f239837845308"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/git/commits/3a306932e9dc1b3626e6eeb6c591ec37390439cd","verification":{"payload":"tree d10a1ab63fd7cf7346adc441509f239837845308\nparent 5f36465bb46ef3659e0e009feec44e4129b04098\nauthor fred-labs <fred-labs@mailbox.org> 1790105712 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790105712 +0200\n\nDrop the read_only flag nothing sets (#654)\n\nWorkspaceInfo.read_only was always False: a pinned directory is writable, and the\ntwo things it may not take -- a whole-tree sync and a delete -- are refused by\nWorkspaceRegistry.require_syncable and by the delete path. The field is gone,\nwith the UI chips and the disabled delete button that branched on it, and the\narchitecture page says what a pin actually refuses.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqsthwCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAjNYQAGo1wC76nAD2kNKmv0DYu6QI\njlt1vnCh2WKHqWkp67j4xzkhmufclTXl7p8vXLvxlw0jqJ+25qg1uqjCH0Cl9PYS\nHNwK7HWXKSI8n2l8gWcym7Ge8ncFrcvhYroObkLBjef3DbxbEoIGHeMx/2VUVHTv\nIru88CJHDk9Rvsl9JFA3Auaw3CiBDZVFJE71Y2oaAda+ZRym88eUqCJPuSaqOMhi\nRt1kOvGuBZRykdHIGhwUkt1WldzZGe/kPNlgU0WHodF6gOttZoerOshuFOJgoxtG\n7EtZcPDaAnSb6CWqLLDhUG9zIIunFqiWGVsVzn/OmFRppcAat9mZPvayHClrsDxt\nyY+FUP7kPZjHHQWGz/Z4yQXB2qxGg1x55dLnN7NY8n/amwYFffgjdYZzQTGcGKFa\ndKnLqfLZW4dq2peVyDNkuIcELMktQfY8Mm0pK7JL4rAX9PQ2bzHYZZ/dWn+9leXi\njcsrO2V3jeFlOrrrSz0N92HduV2rznb4BwL00ALVY+EZsroeBbuY4U7VxMhIkVQ/\nhdo4ozbbhc2nknDBQSu7VZCEISAqs2zqui34uCDSEmslaBNrgED7NzKsyAO15uy0\n3TszbPZ393qWK2Bggv67z7078yZEV4qWgj6XJhzgILAWKu51HPyFhNN64+o3iFs2\nnovEu7JeQxrU1aqJffCd\n=GF+Y\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-22T19:35:13Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cps-test-lab/robovast/commit/3a306932e9dc1b3626e6eeb6c591ec37390439cd","node_id":"C_kwDOPVaL7doAKDNhMzA2OTMyZTlkYzFiMzYyNmU2ZWViNmM1OTFlYzM3MzkwNDM5Y2Q","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cps-test-lab/robovast/commit/5f36465bb46ef3659e0e009feec44e4129b04098","sha":"5f36465bb46ef3659e0e009feec44e4129b04098","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/commits/5f36465bb46ef3659e0e009feec44e4129b04098"}],"sha":"3a306932e9dc1b3626e6eeb6c591ec37390439cd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/commits/3a306932e9dc1b3626e6eeb6c591ec37390439cd"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83823539?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fred-labs","id":83823539,"login":"fred-labs","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzODIzNTM5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/commits/5f36465bb46ef3659e0e009feec44e4129b04098/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-22T19:31:57Z","email":"fred-labs@mailbox.org","name":"fred-labs"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-22T19:31:57Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Let a workspace change once the batch campaign reading it has staged (#529)\n\nA push into a workspace was refused for as long as any campaign launched from it\nran, on the rule that a campaign reads its project for its whole life. A batch\ncampaign does not: it composes once, resolves what each configuration\nreferences, and stages those files, and from then on reads only its own campaign\ndirectory. The refusal therefore outlived the read by the length of the campaign.\n\nBoth lanes call on_configs_staged once their staging is done, and the controller\nreleases the project there. A search campaign re-composes every generation and is\ndeliberately not released. WorkspaceInfo.preparing_campaigns carries the subset\nstill reading, which is what the refusal now asks; running_campaigns stays the\nnote a push prints about the campaigns it will not reach.\n\nThe callback is the controller''s: a value a caller puts on RunOptions is refused\nrather than replaced, since it would never be called.","tree":{"sha":"28ed7abdcc88482adfdfcdc31c909ffce19b5cb5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/git/trees/28ed7abdcc88482adfdfcdc31c909ffce19b5cb5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/git/commits/5f36465bb46ef3659e0e009feec44e4129b04098","verification":{"payload":"tree 28ed7abdcc88482adfdfcdc31c909ffce19b5cb5\nparent b15e2a54f7ad6f82013a67d304275ad45c6fa08b\nauthor fred-labs <fred-labs@mailbox.org> 1790105517 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790105517 +0200\n\nLet a workspace change once the batch campaign reading it has staged (#529)\n\nA push into a workspace was refused for as long as any campaign launched from it\nran, on the rule that a campaign reads its project for its whole life. A batch\ncampaign does not: it composes once, resolves what each configuration\nreferences, and stages those files, and from then on reads only its own campaign\ndirectory. The refusal therefore outlived the read by the length of the campaign.\n\nBoth lanes call on_configs_staged once their staging is done, and the controller\nreleases the project there. A search campaign re-composes every generation and is\ndeliberately not released. WorkspaceInfo.preparing_campaigns carries the subset\nstill reading, which is what the refusal now asks; running_campaigns stays the\nnote a push prints about the campaigns it will not reach.\n\nThe callback is the controller''s: a value a caller puts on RunOptions is refused\nrather than replaced, since it would never be called.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqstetCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAANzwQAIKVVoKGQyrx/HNjCfhLUkh1\ntlavn0b1gVtCzE4lQXlXSpJhMHeqoup7f7RiHb4WIFhoQTZu9yhL8MwBhFgIa6sM\ninwNFSH7/PKCzZhGUUQ+cWeHBlLDsYvOX0Aha0hrhVQ1INYPJsOiErMCCzXDDr4m\n9kFwsp2NAfkaF992hltyPpuBMwnHTbXKuQbvDQ6Csn2eJFf//LCN+Bja1QpWROfL\nTnAu1jfbUwQNBh9horwH0ph5dZQExMlbvPj5jiKFSzPOfeGd4mcDwYO2XfRxb/AI\nWaqXMo2HamjPx65f0bsAuLewVeJukB3217jfntX+YZ6ISfoGdMbr0b5bSg7aBzW4\nM6P8kfDeoT8GuhchjrgSfu25pPg2tfS8m5PlBM+rxMWaFL1vplQXABEtec3rpZ3L\nWixG7d289woKvgXIQxLYhk6K6xS3KXVkw5WeTug8b2ZYWKaKebAw01PZl4b60BEq\n8wrBxeHF3xv2cLqbBcVCXHdPnFeLCe/8Q6H9mAywPK9ibN65ofUmuiqHtwWeKHYE\nPtMPcFNEwEToTw6SMIXUveS57efoDeZ2jbiy+aNnQBwNEmC+XhIY4NjtOsPWEZSR\n7jn0xTeQQ5BSVS0U1J9qecU9GFGXvVmdJ+HKogkP1pPYKogoITNlpSj34A6KkGIQ\nw/oo93sL/C8hD/nFm1SX\n=06MJ\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-22T19:31:58Z"}},"committer":