d-labs","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzODIzNTM5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/commits/b15e2a54f7ad6f82013a67d304275ad45c6fa08b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-22T19:24:18Z","email":"fred-labs@mailbox.org","name":"fred-labs"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-22T19:24:18Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Ask the simulator once per question, and key a block by itself (#653)\n\nThe block key dropped every non-string leaf, on the rule that only a string names\na file. A boolean or a number that selects a plugin naming files then made two\ndifferent blocks one, and the campaign staged the files of whichever came first.\nIt also added nothing: identical questions already collapse in the query memo,\nwhich keys on the image, command and documents a query carries.\n\nBlocks are keyed by themselves again, and the memo remains what makes a sweep of\nforty numeric levels one container round trip. Its test asks what the surface\ndoes: one question however many blocks ask it, and a second question for a block\nthat names another world.","tree":{"sha":"cb9730b78f229e83a2c9eba5cdc2c9f3f3a9e73a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/git/trees/cb9730b78f229e83a2c9eba5cdc2c9f3f3a9e73a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/git/commits/b15e2a54f7ad6f82013a67d304275ad45c6fa08b","verification":{"payload":"tree cb9730b78f229e83a2c9eba5cdc2c9f3f3a9e73a\nparent 6b075b602882eddedbadf592798dbfaa10590fcc\nauthor fred-labs <fred-labs@mailbox.org> 1790105058 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790105058 +0200\n\nAsk the simulator once per question, and key a block by itself (#653)\n\nThe block key dropped every non-string leaf, on the rule that only a string names\na file. A boolean or a number that selects a plugin naming files then made two\ndifferent blocks one, and the campaign staged the files of whichever came first.\nIt also added nothing: identical questions already collapse in the query memo,\nwhich keys on the image, command and documents a query carries.\n\nBlocks are keyed by themselves again, and the memo remains what makes a sweep of\nforty numeric levels one container round trip. Its test asks what the surface\ndoes: one question however many blocks ask it, and a second question for a block\nthat names another world.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqstXiCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAVlQQAFogGPEhQUycxwzcUCTsEcEw\n0KI2ahualo8PWVxyZWUY2+iqsc79BlV3GOEi2e7tbRlP46C6r8ICYFKtexioaqdD\nJ84KBtJI9VdK8xWsAAmXfl52uYlkwJoa4NG+16FoNpRciwATANZ7Ruk4QScwZDgL\ngwboc7ibthY02JKPY/O5sTBASzlKQHdslEV+HeyicdWJc0TQLaiOspjxn+4YqHRF\ns3eJm3Gi12IecfAsfr/Rt/CSVW8y/RwFCTtFNQUJvbbA2FG9SNQLRYoSybUuZVpP\nNXWTm3GFwGGBkrPQ6LQFP6wALHo9WP+C4oEytOlvA2sCt6LJRigF/wE+uK13761O\nIKO1fLDmeL9sqAxFpAtvaH2VG2q1C5Eb1Rf22PauNfZYt9g5iZFXqLSLyKqmNkvv\nh4H/xhkqiuYUniLdvVLeIRy4/R3JJZlezXqQs+gxTtK8Wyxdddls1+4GI5hNYh+a\nDlli9Y5mI9AFFCDQeuZ7EAXMj7xCNx5Dd4td46M/hZWq4AqnTgrms3TQ8EufSFlU\nafJGtFg/3XH2sFXZ7YwC+4DN8RDgv1WfXpghEOtRQau3XYt4FAst7xIVKBBBjZ18\nbA5vi57kPCSE/HBIRAQzsHdgfUY25F7Y9pIkHVnO85zZCHucq/5ZHic7qnOrmbfu\nNjp0zXUaoGKhavFmqr79\n=bUq2\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-22T19:24:18Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cps-test-lab/robovast/commit/b15e2a54f7ad6f82013a67d304275ad45c6fa08b","node_id":"C_kwDOPVaL7doAKGIxNWUyYTU0ZjdhZDZmODIwMTNhNjdkMzA0Mjc1YWQ0NWM2ZmEwOGI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cps-test-lab/robovast/commit/6b075b602882eddedbadf592798dbfaa10590fcc","sha":"6b075b602882eddedbadf592798dbfaa10590fcc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/commits/6b075b602882eddedbadf592798dbfaa10590fcc"}],"sha":"b15e2a54f7ad6f82013a67d304275ad45c6fa08b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/commits/b15e2a54f7ad6f82013a67d304275ad45c6fa08b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83823539?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fred-labs","id":83823539,"login":"fred-labs","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzODIzNTM5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/commits/6b075b602882eddedbadf592798dbfaa10590fcc/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-22T19:18:31Z","email":"fred-labs@mailbox.org","name":"fred-labs"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-22T19:18:31Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Ask the simulator once per question, not once per swept value (#572)\n\nComposition runs two container queries per distinct resolved `sim` block:\nwhich files the world is made of, and whether every override addresses a\ncomponent the world has. \"Distinct\" was keyed on the whole block, override\nvalues included, while the answers depend on the world and on which paths\nare overridden, not on what is written to them. A campaign sweeping a\nnumeric world value therefore compiled its world once per level, and one\ndrawing a contact parameter per seed compiled it a few hundred times, each\nin its own exec, for an answer that never changed. The function''s own\ncomment said the description depends on the world and not on the\nconfiguration; the key disagreed with the comment.\n\nThe component check is now keyed on the world plus the override paths, and\nkeeps the values only when the scenario names entities, since overrides can\nadd those. The input-files query is keyed on the block''s string leaves: a\nfile is named by a string, and a number or a flag names none.\n\nFour tests pin one query per question; two of them fail on the old keying.","tree":{"sha":"917ac433ce93ef862ddeda93f52362f484ea0f73","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/git/trees/917ac433ce93ef862ddeda93f52362f484ea0f73"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/git/commits/6b075b602882eddedbadf592798dbfaa10590fcc","verification":{"payload":"tree 917ac433ce93ef862ddeda93f52362f484ea0f73\nparent f3dac73e7b2a91cd8a1746a7b5e40ee9cbe077ed\nauthor fred-labs <fred-labs@mailbox.org> 1790104711 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790104711 +0200\n\nAsk the simulator once per question, not once per swept value (#572)\n\nComposition runs two container queries per distinct resolved `sim` block:\nwhich files the world is made of, and whether every override addresses a\ncomponent the world has. \"Distinct\" was keyed on the whole block, override\nvalues included, while the answers depend on the world and on which paths\nare overridden, not on what is written to them. A campaign sweeping a\nnumeric world value therefore compiled its world once per level, and one\ndrawing a contact parameter per seed compiled it a few hundred times, each\nin its own exec, for an answer that never changed. The function''s own\ncomment said the description depends on the world and not on the\nconfiguration; the key disagreed with the comment.\n\nThe component check is now keyed on the world plus the override paths, and\nkeeps the values only when the scenario names entities, since overrides can\nadd those. The input-files query is keyed on the block''s string leaves: a\nfile is named by a string, and a number or a flag names none.\n\nFour tests pin one query per question; two of them fail on the old keying.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqstSHCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAgwUQAHQsBgNSPykmLiBU6vuM+bk3\n77yk9ukPe9vHHQcL1l/3s+GKAiStJjJYrunOK3467+trAwyOF0D+ya85FashY9ra\nYdhcTmlWVPlDbaly5j9ktP5rylQB7zJXkGWJRFJEtcrBoV5lpEJ6IOdgQpHyb7D8\nBPvg+aqFaDynb59Pmrr5tIjAUD4DvUmclNFHGr/Y/Gyq3iFoH2gME0hiXEPQk4bw\nI+FZqz/c2mnHGVJRsWog59h39WLY7g6WCn0LkXDT9xxnVIKaQksW9s3e6DkPvDHm\nisVnIBGTIbu/ZWAE7TM2is50a+jHEzyvUWs8ExLXr9MHdk/2RvEKvOqsdNzZHLcS\nWeVKMGO/RvsMaplPuZRYMtWlmvs3+wBGYNZSrXHBwu2pSj3so/osSJcrpGFdRqpG\n418KvFAOCTBtfB5X0ZGyBu+H2DWzDJCSAtUsPnl0G5UE54ABgSVXbYC7pydxNCrd\nB+0Rm4lp0XDhCuQYvaua96Go2mxzVpgTmVkbcHYkjuSEAzjAB/JdPuz5BGdYgbE8\nTAwoXfEYBH0dvsRS1f+NdEjrBpQBsCHRRJubMYg1tcxedkQkoT/8Pld2w1arfhCL\nPvj5eS9OcPm2fleCAEca6oHlOP9nxdOV//lIQIzYOVT5sXBTYB9eoGUoCu8ZaD6L\nb4HsjE4ZxYg/kmiMr4Wf\n=7Fg7\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-22T19:18:31Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cps-test-lab/robovast/commit/6b075b602882eddedbadf592798dbfaa10590fcc","node_id":"C_kwDOPVaL7doAKDZiMDc1YjYwMjg4MmVkZGVkYmFkZjU5Mjc5OGRiZmFhMTA1OTBmY2M","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cps-test-lab/robovast/commit/f3dac73e7b2a91cd8a1746a7b5e40ee9cbe077ed","sha":"f3dac73e7b2a91cd8a1746a7b5e40ee9cbe077ed","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/commits/f3dac73e7b2a91cd8a1746a7b5e40ee9cbe077ed"}],"sha":"6b075b602882eddedbadf592798dbfaa10590fcc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/commits/6b075b602882eddedbadf592798dbfaa10590fcc"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83823539?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fred-labs","id":83823539,"login":"fred-labs","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzODIzNTM5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/commits/f3dac73e7b2a91cd8a1746a7b5e40ee9cbe077ed/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-22T19:17:02Z","email":"fred-labs@mailbox.org","name":"fred-labs"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-22T19:17:02Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Say why a tool lacks an argument when a call passes it (#641)\n\nA call carrying an argument a tool does not take is rejected before the tool\nruns, so the tool''s reply never gets to explain it. The rejection already lists\nthe arguments the tool takes. A tool can now also declare, with @lacks, the\narguments it lacks on purpose and what to do instead, and the rejection carries\nthat. It costs nothing until a caller needs it, where the same sentence in the\ndescription is sent with every request. A tool with no arguments is answered\nwith \"takes no arguments\" and its declared reason rather than a bare validation\nerror, and pydantic''s error type, echoed input and documentation link are left\nout of every rejection.\n\nDeclared where a sibling tool has the argument, which is what a caller carries\nover: exec_in_container lacks timeout, stop_container takes none,\nsearch_run_logs lacks the log tools'' tail, top and offset,\nquery_campaign_data_sql lacks offset, nav_get_obstacles and nav_get_map_info\nlack run_id, and get_campaign_log lacks job_name. search_run_logs drops the\nparagraph that said the same in its description. A test keeps every declaration\ntrue of the tool it is on.","tree":{"sha":"3b89baede7f8ea8c698fd3f65c23f88776fd82a1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/git/trees/3b89baede7f8ea8c698fd3f65c23f88776fd82a1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/git/commits/f3dac73e7b2a91cd8a1746a7b5e40ee9cbe077ed","verification":{"payload":"tree 3b89baede7f8ea8c698fd3f65c23f88776fd82a1\nparent bc6b555cd2422da9ba502bb65fd8d8a4ed4bd74f\nauthor fred-labs <fred-labs@mailbox.org> 1790104622 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790104622 +0200\n\nSay why a tool lacks an argument when a call passes it (#641)\n\nA call carrying an argument a tool does not take is rejected before the tool\nruns, so the tool''s reply never gets to explain it. The rejection already lists\nthe arguments the tool takes. A tool can now also declare, with @lacks, the\narguments it lacks on purpose and what to do instead, and the rejection carries\nthat. It costs nothing until a caller needs it, where the same sentence in the\ndescription is sent with every request. A tool with no arguments is answered\nwith \"takes no arguments\" and its declared reason rather than a bare validation\nerror, and pydantic''s error type, echoed input and documentation link are left\nout of every rejection.\n\nDeclared where a sibling tool has the argument, which is what a caller carries\nover: exec_in_container lacks timeout, stop_container takes none,\nsearch_run_logs lacks the log tools'' tail, top and offset,\nquery_campaign_data_sql lacks offset, nav_get_obstacles and nav_get_map_info\nlack run_id, and get_campaign_log lacks job_name. search_run_logs drops the\nparagraph that said the same in its description. A test keeps every declaration\ntrue of the tool it is on.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqstQuCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAHmAQAFAUdsozxRFsA6ltVwLa1t4Z\nLaEv8zXq2RlQ1SHaTEpVn/3JrJAIB2g518ObmuB3bBVLI6fuU2coCeJPvgQEbPNz\nhQLmUq6fCLguyzKLq7+BcwngQFPOn/N2xhPo9KuLtZoxTcEnK3cw/Bi0MGD1eLcn\nwWH7yk7qfNoshYUYLwnx3kv++RPNbTdiMc7f9OISFp/TibEP5pG8+CKmBbyWkUWS\nzsEdnUYqcLMKk+9DQDuQo1EFUJargcxBS3MiVvKNmDnukL5SpOeP+9DPFUf5nzTY\nqxIZiup/P7ixHH58NCmsaLO+oAbKl0/W35YVQF9SuzaSHDKTjBfsOqrm+i5xtED3\nPkQDxJFTv3GgZmWWINMQSk3zGzlZFhnS/4fPlG52fNmK2mD9dv1Ic3JPxs0/E+ij\nv3ftXImYF1N5MckRXs5s7uApTSW7CeuzUMEMe5t9SER48Z4m/r+Dh3F6ur6Gu/33\nHllZqATvOOl6uYTXXhZuBfaQuOBbskvlr4a+JQA+O4lMRiDhPxX6bwiYDhFAEvtP\nDTATvk/ViuXp4Pm3g1Vra/yZRUIDT7QrcqoDuIx5XIQNFQx9SFoxEPR/4OSLV+0q\nAquVdf5xs0sIab7gGTF6x0zqwvouoKW9eSI3PHmuTQCMM0CnPNki7zJ52pc+ZdG0\nq8gkK6ZOtuCeekmINkAa\n=zgi2\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-22T19:17:03Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"h