_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/commits/55c4f0645e9e059dbc3c2ea5e823ff31e86815d1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-21T20:02:51Z","email":"fred-labs@mailbox.org","name":"fred-labs"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-21T20:02:51Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Declare the argument vocabulary as an allowlist (#448)\n\nThe guard on MCP argument names listed the names it forbids, so a synonym nobody\nhad listed passed. It now lists every name the surface may use, and a tool with\nan argument outside that list fails the build until the name is added on purpose.\nThe retired names stay forbidden, and a test keeps the two lists disjoint.\n\nsearch_run_logs takes no tail, top or offset: it searches across runs rather than\npaging one. Its description says so and points at query_campaign_data_sql, and\nneither it nor the module docstring lists tail among the arguments it shares with\nthe other log tools.","tree":{"sha":"ca31e796ed591f32a6331677952fbdddc905c076","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/git/trees/ca31e796ed591f32a6331677952fbdddc905c076"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/git/commits/55c4f0645e9e059dbc3c2ea5e823ff31e86815d1","verification":{"payload":"tree ca31e796ed591f32a6331677952fbdddc905c076\nparent b3ff66906a2aeba7d14d7f54f45daf470236b1ac\nauthor fred-labs <fred-labs@mailbox.org> 1790020971 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790020971 +0200\n\nDeclare the argument vocabulary as an allowlist (#448)\n\nThe guard on MCP argument names listed the names it forbids, so a synonym nobody\nhad listed passed. It now lists every name the surface may use, and a tool with\nan argument outside that list fails the build until the name is added on purpose.\nThe retired names stay forbidden, and a test keeps the two lists disjoint.\n\nsearch_run_logs takes no tail, top or offset: it searches across runs rather than\npaging one. Its description says so and points at query_campaign_data_sql, and\nneither it nor the module docstring lists tail among the arguments it shares with\nthe other log tools.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqsY1rCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAB20QAIpcdgRF17zGcjCp2rn6j4oM\n544WrRMgS89TzBmYEypVVjPr+E5XCeBzsviNoTyiCVnehNbwciTHK17h9GS+cRoT\n4iag9myyvwTPEX/FxHGgxCVEJXRiZzLf+XYvK0XIbCBrersE/mf+MZIbX/Dq8JDU\nf4UQ7ISzJGx98DHEt42yNDFJpmxE6gHRF/YK3fn7F7E8zkKsTlbSKeA55lb0oz7/\naqnH0Zd992T1Zy3ExDZ8kp96HtIrqgjpI8Q5byT/xvZwxVbzCFZuoeCQHA02cW85\n0CSuhxPG6/jCHQHfIM0O+Kx3D2fQ/trrTIi1pagS5FCD6jKEvznaEyQIi/8awQD1\nEwWF/WU374wRWQjGV8FQxGBnIzwtxWMM1RFrejp7hPZOmwVKQ+do3w3cwvwE1bzq\nHg8p3YotkA/kGS5P6iKKkwe1XW13lWT2HAj2iENNuY2LXQPWHTzEP0GVwepb6QHC\nSm1X5iQZw5g1L70oCvpUraN8RiIDoyV+OJE4Q7lhPsUK1TD+w/aK+x5UdHl81WYg\nEZJ2j4JEV1xXbhbSLdngUg5Ldb3HbxKzdflpzNEsyAsAmjBOoLr35GR4Cr8wOq9c\n6de2ex2cB3pKj0oN822oaZ8xiorehBtJZE/aRAfYH5N67EvZxTVFwAdQGmrNK8c+\nnvZJPwK2kefhqEdMcDKc\n=QxGv\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-21T20:02:52Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cps-test-lab/robovast/commit/55c4f0645e9e059dbc3c2ea5e823ff31e86815d1","node_id":"C_kwDOPVaL7doAKDU1YzRmMDY0NWU5ZTA1OWRiYzNjMmVhNWU4MjNmZjMxZTg2ODE1ZDE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cps-test-lab/robovast/commit/b3ff66906a2aeba7d14d7f54f45daf470236b1ac","sha":"b3ff66906a2aeba7d14d7f54f45daf470236b1ac","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/commits/b3ff66906a2aeba7d14d7f54f45daf470236b1ac"}],"sha":"55c4f0645e9e059dbc3c2ea5e823ff31e86815d1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/commits/55c4f0645e9e059dbc3c2ea5e823ff31e86815d1"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83823539?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fred-labs","id":83823539,"login":"fred-labs","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzODIzNTM5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/commits/b3ff66906a2aeba7d14d7f54f45daf470236b1ac/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-21T19:42:38Z","email":"fred-labs@mailbox.org","name":"fred-labs"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-21T19:42:38Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Keep a message''s numeric array in one column (#570)\n\n* Keep a message''s numeric array in one column, and a non-finite float a number\n\nThe rosbag-to-CSV flattening emitted one column per element of every sequence\nfield, so a laser scan arrived as a table with a column per ray: a shape no index\nwill hold, and one in which the array itself is nowhere -- a column holds ray 417\nof every message, which is not a scan. Typing then worked against it. A\nnon-finite float is not a number the index can store, so it is kept verbatim as\ntext, and every ray column that ever saw a beam return nothing widened from REAL\nto TEXT. One such table is enough to end the ingest that was converting every\nother table beside it.\n\nA field *declared* as an array of a primitive number is now one cell, packed the\nway the occupancy-grid handler packs a costmap: the raw little-endian values,\nzlib, base64. The declaration decides it and not the values, so a table''s shape\nis the message definition, and two runs of a sensor that reported different ray\ncounts are one table. The cell names its element type and its count, which the\ncostmap''s does not have to -- that column holds int8 cells by definition, while\nany topic can be named here -- so decode_numeric_array needs nothing but the\nstring, and a reader outside robovast needs one frombuffer over the payload.\n\nKeeping the values as bytes is also what keeps a non-finite one. `inf` is the\nreading that says the beam hit nothing within range, and in the payload it is an\nIEEE-754 bit pattern like every other value. Where a non-finite float is a scalar\nfield of its own it becomes an empty cell, stored as NULL -- no number the index\ncan hold means no reading -- and the step names the columns it wrote one in, so\nthose NULLs read as the sensor''s answer and not as a gap in the recording.\n\nA sequence of sub-messages still gets a column per element per field: nothing\npacks a pose, and a handful of waypoints is what those columns are for.\n\n* A non-finite scalar goes into the CSV as the number it is\n\nThe ingest now stores inf and nan as double precision and keeps the column\nnumeric, so turning a non-finite float into an empty cell no longer protects\nanything: it merged a laser''s \"no return\" with a reading nobody took. The value\nis written as Python''s csv writes it, inf or nan, and the note naming the\ncolumns that received NULLs is gone with the NULLs.","tree":{"sha":"0636699bc2028ed16d781c41f2f5c3c556abd697","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/git/trees/0636699bc2028ed16d781c41f2f5c3c556abd697"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/git/commits/b3ff66906a2aeba7d14d7f54f45daf470236b1ac","verification":{"payload":"tree 0636699bc2028ed16d781c41f2f5c3c556abd697\nparent 75f84306ec28830ee4e905558927cbb3e9181de6\nauthor fred-labs <fred-labs@mailbox.org> 1790019758 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790019758 +0200\n\nKeep a message''s numeric array in one column (#570)\n\n* Keep a message''s numeric array in one column, and a non-finite float a number\n\nThe rosbag-to-CSV flattening emitted one column per element of every sequence\nfield, so a laser scan arrived as a table with a column per ray: a shape no index\nwill hold, and one in which the array itself is nowhere -- a column holds ray 417\nof every message, which is not a scan. Typing then worked against it. A\nnon-finite float is not a number the index can store, so it is kept verbatim as\ntext, and every ray column that ever saw a beam return nothing widened from REAL\nto TEXT. One such table is enough to end the ingest that was converting every\nother table beside it.\n\nA field *declared* as an array of a primitive number is now one cell, packed the\nway the occupancy-grid handler packs a costmap: the raw little-endian values,\nzlib, base64. The declaration decides it and not the values, so a table''s shape\nis the message definition, and two runs of a sensor that reported different ray\ncounts are one table. The cell names its