//github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cps-test-lab/robovast/commit/62300152938077cd80d206fbd902a0a8bb10c37d","node_id":"C_kwDOPVaL7doAKDYyMzAwMTUyOTM4MDc3Y2Q4MGQyMDZmYmQ5MDJhMGE4YmIxMGMzN2Q","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cps-test-lab/robovast/commit/c26991ae829ff58317a7489fd662abd67dd6cb02","sha":"c26991ae829ff58317a7489fd662abd67dd6cb02","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/commits/c26991ae829ff58317a7489fd662abd67dd6cb02"}],"sha":"62300152938077cd80d206fbd902a0a8bb10c37d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/commits/62300152938077cd80d206fbd902a0a8bb10c37d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83823539?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fred-labs","id":83823539,"login":"fred-labs","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzODIzNTM5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/commits/c26991ae829ff58317a7489fd662abd67dd6cb02/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-21T19:08:20Z","email":"fred-labs@mailbox.org","name":"fred-labs"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-21T19:08:20Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Report a run killed by a figure the campaign measured, and keep running (#615)\n\n* Report a run killed by a figure the campaign measured, and keep running\n\nUnder `sizing: calibrated` every run is sized from one probe''s peak, so a demand the probe\ndid not see is not met once: the same figure meets the next run, and the next. Nothing said\nso. The invalidation that follows such a kill says a trial was lost, which is equally true\nof a flake, and the campaign went on losing runs to a cause no surface named.\n\nThe runner records a kill at a MEASURED figure in the campaign''s ledger -- the fault cannot\nbe self-reported, because a container that was OOM-killed is not there to answer a health\ncommand and its Job is deleted moments later -- and the service reports it as an\nerror-level health finding, `calibrated-memory-oom`.\n\nThat is the existing channel rather than a new one: `vast campaign wait` already ends on an\nerror-level finding, and its edge is per check, so one fault is one exit however many runs\nit takes. One finding per fault with the count in its detail, for the same reason.\n\nThe campaign keeps running. A sweep that reaches its end having lost some runs is worth\nmore than one held halfway, and which of those somebody wants is not the runner''s call:\nwhat to state -- `calibration.min.memory`, a larger `resources.memory`, or nothing at all\n-- belongs to whoever wrote the `.vast`. Only a measured figure is reported this way; a\ncontainer killed at what its author declared is a campaign asking for too little.\n\n* Record a kill at a measured figure where the pod ends, not only where it restarts\n\nThe runner saw an OOM kill only on the restart path, which reads last_state and so\nonly a container the pod restarts: a native sidecar. The scenario container runs\nunder restartPolicy: Never, so its kill ends the pod instead, and it is sized from\na measured figure like the others. oom_killed_job_forensics reads that end state,\nand the runner records it through the same step, once per job and container\nhowever many polls see it. It lists pods only once some node has figures.\n\nThe health refresh''s docstring said nothing is inferred there; it now names the\nledger as the second source of findings.","tree":{"sha":"2a76b4cd8e70dc11070d06ceac0100600cdee857","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/git/trees/2a76b4cd8e70dc11070d06ceac0100600cdee857"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/git/commits/c26991ae829ff58317a7489fd662abd67dd6cb02","verification":{"payload":"tree 2a76b4cd8e70dc11070d06ceac0100600cdee857\nparent fab7adce493c494ef8d4faf35717a336e2e9569f\nauthor fred-labs <fred-labs@mailbox.org> 1790017700 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790017700 +0200\n\nReport a run killed by a figure the campaign measured, and keep running (#615)\n\n* Report a run killed by a figure the campaign measured, and keep running\n\nUnder `sizing: calibrated` every run is sized from one probe''s peak, so a demand the probe\ndid not see is not met once: the same figure meets the next run, and the next. Nothing said\nso. The invalidation that follows such a kill says a trial was lost, which is equally true\nof a flake, and the campaign went on losing runs to a cause no surface named.\n\nThe runner records a kill at a MEASURED figure in the campaign''s ledger -- the fault cannot\nbe self-reported, because a container that was OOM-killed is not there to answer a health\ncommand and its Job is deleted moments later -- and the service reports it as an\nerror-level health finding, `calibrated-memory-oom`.\n\nThat is the existing channel rather than a new one: `vast campaign wait` already ends on an\nerror-level finding, and its edge is per check, so one fault is one exit however many runs\nit takes. One finding per fault with the count in its detail, for the same reason.\n\nThe campaign keeps running. A sweep that reaches its end having lost some runs is worth\nmore than one held halfway, and which of those somebody wants is not the runner''s call:\nwhat to state -- `calibration.min.memory`, a larger `resources.memory`, or nothing at all\n-- belongs to whoever wrote the `.vast`. Only a measured figure is reported this way; a\ncontainer killed at what its author declared is a campaign asking for too little.\n\n* Record a kill at a measured figure where the pod ends, not only where it restarts\n\nThe runner saw an OOM kill only on the restart path, which reads last_state and so\nonly a container the pod restarts: a native sidecar. The scenario container runs\nunder restartPolicy: Never, so its kill ends the pod instead, and it is sized from\na measured figure like the others. oom_killed_job_forensics reads that end state,\nand the runner records it through the same step, once per job and container\nhowever many polls see it. It lists pods only once some node has figures.\n\nThe health refresh''s docstring said nothing is inferred there; it now names the\nledger as the second source of findings.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqsYCkCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA1/oQAGwZvqAKmu5TPlWSYsouAPAN\nDIwHZy5QkBOp+JcyWoFjgyRCJoaj4180ENqiGJeDaIMxXUhideuX1FYq3iaR3gOc\nERt2TsM6sJERP+n8CQwZMZPl5iMqL9UodW6JsQgvYxxU/NildKzhc2RdyHtdi7T3\nVeWoPGnLh6p2idgRx08NRI2KF0YaoNx2Y5ct2+iXzry4v8ivlcrLRdF++1c4ZuKo\nywh4KO2kGa8n1U4noTRYhsCoT9CO9GDsbwvJiXysyVyfTW8PrgC2UKCwipyW1HqV\n3IoYuS/hddjPLW0buO0A56JA9jkgi4mtQnzH0nVUO9bjm/K4UPyspbnZYTTnihBH\nv1KUhfBWexjosHQgFim+l1clK+y+xYXAmnKgfHdNOm+COBajabaKxtYFDG7Rptiz\npV9VC31t3MEiTh7a3tdbugVJNI3e4FJ4aYlUk3hQ20LZShJCV/z0u27Cf+rYTrLv\n5OXcQM0PeUh4HGryPiENwkzUTiRf+Y8a+eYPBd6X38d4dvGesLG3ukU9yeIh5U6d\nKJDR29sde6+fS3EHnQdBwjJbIE0j7lRKhs434RWMwRwGYp75flbjKf78nIeFi8zc\nX2wbkGOu7Zgjsvmalq2O4baCnPM8gp+qdkFARLWg0kTF5d4pltB4Ohcr5S0pwHFZ\nr/eKz77jRjyJZZTrb0IA\n=ONvE\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-21T19:08:21Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cps-test-lab/robovast/commit/c26991ae829ff58317a7489fd662abd67dd6cb02","node_id":"C_kwDOPVaL7doAKGMyNjk5MWFlODI5ZmY1ODMxN2E3NDg5ZmQ2NjJhYmQ2N2RkNmNiMDI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cps-test-lab/robovast/commit/fab7adce493c494ef8d4faf35717a336e2e9569f","sha":"fab7adce493c494ef8d4faf35717a336e2e9569f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/commits/fab7adce493c494ef8d4faf35717a336e2e9569f"}],"sha":"c26991ae829ff58317a7489fd662abd67dd6cb02","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/commits/c26991ae829ff58317a7489fd662abd67dd6cb02"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83823539?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fred-labs","id":83823539,"login":"fred-labs","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzODIzNTM5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/commits/fab7adce493c494ef8d4faf35717a336e2e9569f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-21T19:01:10Z","email":"fred-labs@mailbox.org","name":"fred-labs"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-21T19:01:10Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Free a calibration probe the batch can no longer use (#610)\n\n* Free a calibration probe the batch can no longer use\n\nA probe is pinned and is the largest pod a calibrated campaign asks for, so one\nnothing will read still holds its node against every other campaign. Two moments\nleft one running.\n\nOnce the batch has created every job it defined, no run of it can be placed on a\nnode still being measured. The probes the queue has not created are dropped there\nand then, rather than created later at a trial''s cost for a figure this batch\ncannot use. `drop_planned` is not `cancel`: it takes back only what is still\nplanned and leaves the holds behind an owner''s created items, which are pods that\nexist. A probe already created is left to finish -- it is most of a trial in, and\nits figure still spares the next batch of a search from re-probing that node.\n\nAt the end of the batch an outstanding probe was abandoned in the calibration\nwhile its Job was left to expire on its own activeDeadlineSeconds, a trial''s outer\nbackstop and many times a trial. It is deleted now, the step a crashed probe\nalready gets, and best-effort because this runs in the batch''s `finally` where a\nraise would replace the reason the campaign is unwinding.\n\nA dropped probe''s node stays outstanding in the calibration, so it still counts\ntoward UNMEASURED_BATCH_LIMIT: a node the campaign takes no work on has to be\nreported, not quietly dropped from the tally.\n\n* A probe cancelled for want of work does not count toward leaving its node out\n\nA node unmeasured in UNMEASURED_BATCH_LIMIT batches is left out of the campaign,\nbecause a probe that loses the race for capacity that often is not going to win it.\nA probe the batch cancels once every job it defined exists lost no such race: the\nbatch finished placing its work before the queue reached it. Charging that\nwould leave a node out of a multi-batch search on a busy cluster after two\nbatches that simply finished early.\n\nThe node stays held until the batch ends, so a retried run cannot land on it at\nthe declared sizing, and the batch names it in its own warning. It is not\ncharged, and the next batch probes it again. The end-of-batch warning for the\nnodes that are charged now says they are left out, which is what the limit does.","tree":{"sha":"d8e912e601363bd5242867553032bb9a0ce3c098","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/git/trees/d8e912e601363bd5242867553032bb9a0ce3c098"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/git/commits/fab7adce493c494ef8d4faf35717a336e2e9569f","verification":{"payload":"tree d8e912e601363bd5242867553032bb9a0ce3c098\nparent af476f485726ed6d02b3b5c61c6e7299a374be82\nauthor fred-labs <fred-labs@mailbox.org> 1790017270 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790017270 +0200\n\nFree a calibration probe the batch can no longer use (#610)\n\n* Free a calibration probe the batch can no longer use\n\nA probe is pinned and is the largest pod a calibrated campaign asks for, so one\nnothing will read still holds its node against every other campaign. Two moments\nleft one running.\n\nOnce the batch has created every job it defined, no run of it can be placed on a\nnode still being measured. The probes the queue has not created are dropped there\nand then, rather than created later at a trial''s cost for a figure this batch\ncannot use. `drop_planned` is not `cancel`: it takes back only what is still\nplanned and leaves the holds behind an owner''s created items, which are pods that\nexist. A probe already created is left to finish -- it is most of a trial in, and\nits figure still spares the next batch of a search from re-probing that node.\n\nAt the end of the batch an outstanding probe was abandoned in the calibration\nwhile its Job was left to expire on its own activeDeadlineSeconds, a trial''s outer\nbackstop and many times a trial. It is deleted now, the step a crashed probe\nalready gets, and best-effort because this runs in the batch''s `finally` where a\nraise would replace the reason the campaign is unwinding.\n\nA dropped probe''s node stays outstanding in the calibration, so it still counts\ntoward UNMEASURED_BATCH_LIMIT: a node the campaign takes no work on has to be\nreported, not quietly dropped from the tally.\n\n* A probe cancelled for want of work does not count toward leaving its node out\n\nA node unmeasured in UNMEASURED_BATCH_LIMIT batches is left out of the campaign,\nbecause a probe that loses the race for capacity that often is not going to win it.\nA probe the batch cancels once every job it defined exists lost no such race: the\nbatch finished placing its work before the queue reached it. Charging that\nwould leave a node out of a multi-batch search on a busy cluster after two\nbatches that simply finished early.\n\nThe node stays held until the batch ends, so a retried run cannot land on it at\nthe declared sizing, and the batch names it in its own warning. It is not\ncharged, and the next batch probes it again. The end-of-batch warning for the\nnodes that are charged now says they are left out, which is what the limit does.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqsX73CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAnroQAB/dFc25Lq4DmDvGZ1pa4K4E\noRiyguFGkV8YzH5NavZ1ITbLXN/kBwvJ7TItC25gcGp3ZMszMMHaoo4tW7d0vtly\nwCCMq2vT6PDPR+fSIAw2TRpBljqRhk4oqQsA2592uiVs/xr9R+sFwfYs0NM16h4F\nI5txyhurabH6iHKBgrm/ozqfx/ivrCyeuRe0v+thlCYnwmymXJdfu2A7Rm3e/n3H\n0fVgGfbYQnWaLNjH1y++lSBVf69U4Ka9AxbPfRSz1Wz5AX1jFqYAtvaLyNyOTNul\nYXUrPOiVDakitG0oO8FroiCXRd7Ah0nEEQW+0OQmbyZZNdJELCdC3n4eJIHDSuLd\nBumaxoMH1YFX2rV8H/4wHm7t6FETlCkpWKafxaqIWWHl9RGRidfx5140ztY87sx6\nlz0xKjBxH7Y/P7KQGyqsgB8pI1sJ951seJR8XogscVzhVLGLQlCvNFpqZ2xeyPmm\nuNKH0EN9vziK5MD3VnNyUNoJh5uftzVGPyLNwgY9u9lVEBJLNOTT6FSSSkBOqs1M\nKP5dtpoZtVT89F97NAj9ndQGh9bx5APsBdYyf9vr2BoNEtpxLGu6ReHghAgSJYxe\n3lA0NmWnTQkVB3DvIPolduhL1VIhPbM6S3m/TaJBYaRqiabFOUj5hNCvGjcVUpwN\nWRC4Tk0lVkc9c0eyuGk/\n=8Wss\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-21T19:01:11Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cps-test-lab/robovast/commit/fab7adce493c494ef8d4faf35717a336e2e9569f","node_id":"C_kwDOPVaL7doAKGZhYjdhZGNlNDkzYzQ5NGVmOGQ0ZmFmMzU3MTdhMzM2ZTJlOTU2OWY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cps-test-lab/robovast/commit/af476f485726ed6d02b3b5c61c6e7299a374be82","sha":"af476f485726ed6d02b3b5c61c6e7299a374be82","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/commits/af476f485726ed6d02b3b5c61c6e7299a374be82"}],"sha":"fab7adce493c494ef8d4faf35717a336e2e9569f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/commits/fab7adce493c494ef8d4faf35717a336e2e9569f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83823539?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fred-labs","id":83823539,"login":"fred-labs","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzODIzNTM5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/commits/af476f485726ed6d02b3b5c61c6e7299a374be82/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-21T18:46:04Z","email":"fred-labs@mailbox.org","name":"fred-labs"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-21T18:46:04Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Never size a calibrated container below what it needs to exist (#613)\n\n* Never size a calibrated container below what it needs to exist\n\nCalibration measures one run''s peak and sizes every later run of the campaign from it. A\nprobe reports a number, not whether its run got far enough for that number to mean\nanything: one that stopped during bring-up measures a fraction of what every later run\nneeds. CPU has always been floored against that; memory was not -- on the resource where\nthe cost is the run rather than its speed, as the comment beside the floor already said.\n\n- Memory keeps 512M, whatever was measured, as CPU keeps a quarter core. One figure for\n  every role: it bounds a measurement rather than describing a workload, and what a given\n  container needs is what `resources` and `calibration.min` are for.\n- `calibration.min` raises either floor for a container an author knows needs more. It is\n  what headroom cannot be: a multiplier scales a measurement that is wrong, a floor bounds\n  it. Never above `resources`, which stays the ceiling -- a floor stated above it is\n  refused, because no allocation satisfies both.\n\nTogether they are what lets a `.vast` say nothing about sizing and still get an allocation\nits containers can live in, which is the point of leaving measured sizing on by default.\n\n* State the memory floor as bytes, and give it the CPU floor''s reason\n\nMIN_MEMORY is a byte count, so nothing parses it at sizing time and no helper\nexists to fail on it. Its comment now agrees with MIN_CPU''s: both are last-resort\nfloors, the sample count and the verdict gate stay the defence against a short\nprobe, and the memory floor bounds what a probe that reached a failure verdict\nduring bring-up can do to later runs. The calibration.min field says the built-in\nfloors apply when it is omitted, and the ceiling check sits after the fields of\nContainerConfig rather than between them.","tree":{"sha":"726e815e2ea37efc7ab7fcae9e77ebb30119a8ac","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/git/trees/726e815e2ea37efc7ab7fcae9e77ebb30119a8ac"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/git/commits/af476f485726ed6d02b3b5c61c6e7299a374be82","verification":{"payload":"tree 726e815e2ea37efc7ab7fcae9e77ebb30119a8ac\nparent 644fe71a9b45b21da3fd038460ef7d2fa1cd80d3\nauthor fred-labs <fred-labs@mailbox.org> 1790016364 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790016364 +0200\n\nNever size a calibrated container below what it needs to exist (#613)\n\n* Never size a calibrated container below what it needs to exist\n\nCalibration measures one run''s peak and sizes every later run of the campaign from it. A\nprobe reports a number, not whether its run got far enough for that number to mean\nanything: one that stopped during bring-up measures a fraction of what every later run\nneeds. CPU has always been floored against that; memory was not -- on the resource where\nthe cost is the run rather than its speed, as the comment beside the floor already said.\n\n- Memory keeps 512M, whatever was measured, as CPU keeps a quarter core. One figure for\n  every role: it bounds a measurement rather than describing a workload, and what a given\n  container needs is what `resources` and `calibration.min` are for.\n- `calibration.min` raises either floor for a container an author knows needs more. It is\n  what headroom cannot be: a multiplier scales a measurement that is wrong, a floor bounds\n  it. Never above `resources`, which stays the ceiling -- a floor stated above it is\n  refused, because no allocation satisfies both.\n\nTogether they are what lets a `.vast` say nothing about sizing and still get an allocation\nits containers can live in, which is the point of leaving measured sizing on by default.\n\n* State the memory floor as bytes, and give it the CPU floor''s reason\n\nMIN_MEMORY is a byte count, so nothing parses it at sizing time and no helper\nexists to fail on it. Its comment now agrees with MIN_CPU''s: both are last-resort\nfloors, the sample count and the verdict gate stay the defence against a short\nprobe, and the memory floor bounds what a probe that reached a failure verdict\nduring bring-up can do to later runs. The calibration.min field says the built-in\nfloors apply when it is omitted, and the ceiling check sits after the fields of\nContainerConfig rather than between them.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqsXtsCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAZmMQAItriW47qRGB9zRmYzo7Ty45\nTl2yjHtqK8ghLAuVBnju0yo+wdkI7BSlWmjILU6YUnxlLk9K9S+itu8tDmQZb1mZ\nP7hAmuv3Dwh7f6Vi7tmRivOzel3aIlpArG85ZP0NJqKSURuhiFa0duep9hvR1BwI\nQKFqtc5sQe/bOX4pnoJgnF5Y3FjdXKTiGfHNvF65joH1eFuxYd1Ef0Hig1jVVXeR\n9Lf2qCntvDJiH7Am4Wf/dhwj+cfEkmQYg0UUyKVUn1TZHAnjhqVCot71OKEHXeUU\nmC8vwZwpahiOpuU30cfDJYqp46co1O/eZv6cHgD8ud74ntdtmCdsHAuAbEjN2Zs8\nKn5DdPJxmOT5BJnoObby+ZqGeOLdP+7OlacVNXXsLObGnuNfLCJ++8VcJHIETuQs\nrwWfRhpxEVEMatrAmpaXvGWp/BZDPj5zCU5AFKp/79c/FoWS7h6LAdYJBLdzE0jo\nP+LEdsBWgKs2jUWMioOCtkQMIlMEI/U8Q+C3+DQg9adXeQEaVxyFPjVwK/pBHn9w\nxdGlOV9vxMzvzlMhoRLlqyhkJEMOE2+uvn5xD3ggouIoeVOlgBGsrA+X8PTNd3wd\nOJQOpeEcJl9fpcFujpvUVhZZgYZVcgaIYPADzxVH2vL/7NEYUo+CjTFcGcBtnovA\nP5tbulbkUtE91oimxKn2\n=Znmg\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-21T18:46:04Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cps-test-lab/robovast/commit/af476f485726ed6d02b3b5c61c6e7299a374be82","node_id":"C_kwDOPVaL7doAKGFmNDc2ZjQ4NTcyNmVkNmQwMmIzYjVjNjFjNmU3Mjk5YTM3NGJlODI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cps-test-lab/robovast/commit/644fe71a9b45b21da3fd038460ef7d2fa1cd80d3","sha":"644fe71a9b45b21da3fd038460ef7d2fa1cd80d3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/commits/644fe71a9b45b21da3fd038460ef7d2fa1cd80d3"}],"sha":"af476f485726ed6d02b3b5c61c6e7299a374be82","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/commits/af476f485726ed6d02b3b5c61c6e7299a374be82"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83823539?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fred-labs","id":83823539,"login":"fred-labs","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzODIzNTM5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/commits/644fe71a9b45b21da3fd038460ef7d2fa1cd80d3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-21T18:35:06Z","email":"fred-labs@mailbox.org","name":"fred-labs"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-21T18:35:06Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Route an analysis question to the tools that answer it, from the plugin that has them (#631)\n\nThe SQL tool opened by saying it answers most questions, and nothing beside it named\nthe questions a plugin''s tools answer better: where the robot went is reduced over every\nrecorded pose by the nav tools, while the same question in SQL gets a different number\nover a thinned or unjoined result.\n\nThe routing belongs in the server instructions, the only text a client shows before a\ntool is chosen, and it has to come from the plugin: the core cannot name a tool of a\ndistribution that may not be installed. An MCP plugin may now carry an instructions\nparagraph, appended to the core text; the nav plugin names its tools there. The server\nrefuses to start when the whole exceeds INSTRUCTIONS_LIMIT, since a client would cut it\nwithout a mark. The SQL tool''s own description says, without naming a plugin, that a\ntool answering the question comes first.","tree":{"sha":"6841c1d0c3c76931fca197e98dccea6348f692e6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/git/trees/6841c1d0c3c76931fca197e98dccea6348f692e6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/git/commits/644fe71a9b45b21da3fd038460ef7d2fa1cd80d3","verification":{"payload":"tree 6841c1d0c3c76931fca197e98dccea6348f692e6\nparent 1b03f6b972ce494292f745809a3e7d96a74edd47\nauthor fred-labs <fred-labs@mailbox.org> 1790015706 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790015706 +0200\n\nRoute an analysis question to the tools that answer it, from the plugin that has them (#631)\n\nThe SQL tool opened by saying it answers most questions, and nothing beside it named\nthe questions a plugin''s tools answer better: where the robot went is reduced over every\nrecorded pose by the nav tools, while the same question in SQL gets a different number\nover a thinned or unjoined result.\n\nThe routing belongs in the server instructions, the only text a client shows before a\ntool is chosen, and it has to come from the plugin: the core cannot name a tool of a\ndistribution that may not be installed. An MCP plugin may now carry an instructions\nparagraph, appended to the core text; the nav plugin names its tools there. The server\nrefuses to start when the whole exceeds INSTRUCTIONS_LIMIT, since a client would cut it\nwithout a mark. The SQL tool''s own description says, without naming a plugin, that a\ntool answering the question comes first.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqsXjaCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAV7sQALFGUN1Q9B14hKnAvyofBKjQ\nl2+EFYsu42AmKW+u1u926eEkxeZsuynCktEs5F/rb2T9+IAVhBK7eJ+p5Fr8UXin\nLbJJBJJtJD/zitYK7EYD391cEFVi4bcIJ2cDZHdFzL4qKVuimxoZUv7KcBXG8v+E\nG+KvvEuahtOOY2xH/bYgGSV0vpmujgtIiwEH00pL++BrhFGfTMD4jhJrrFgwTMDp\nGLKJpZsuOkG0dz2mOAxZy1urnCvWTIKPI1OBoOY3RieDQkPgOwrMg/ublPN8cvZh\nHRQ/mA3ualhohxRTyUF3U7issNrzVcLOFsGyBdHdIrCphB6EhjJrZ3ZOqwi2XDOv\nNqfhV/5Gxlnc9e0NGS5wB1Wm25eUMVIo/9v+GdRgFGDiUH5QNXOHegT7SUBHo1Zk\nkqKd0nGAFLf7464LVrFVqFKsJCwwflB9MVUHxrP8adimXE5nVU+2zTE50WpUeYpE\nN0DHvjH5vqQdMoO1M9e/E0714rfl6S95GvBQEDC/VtiHYqfjcA1mHQvc13YjD4wD\nCtxPj8+lJ8UAbzjBYgG9sZtrPyqQZAYHcsbDh+SzmgWGzN9egJBxQqyIDvCGjEGc\n7piMTtiLaJ13tZ+okPFCXjypbAUzQtTwzuq1Kep9u/fbRoesRjHQMzFMJ2Ikk/jV\n1cti0uI9d1liRr75dXea\n=AQOE\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-21T18:35:06Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cps-test-lab/robovast/commit/644fe71a9b45b21da3fd038460ef7d2fa1cd80d3","node_id":"C_kwDOPVaL7doAKDY0NGZlNzFhOWI0NWIyMWRhM2ZkMDM4NDYwZWY3ZDJmYTFjZDgwZDM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cps-test-lab/robovast/commit/1b03f6b972ce494292f745809a3e7d96a74edd47","sha":"1b03f6b972ce494292f745809a3e7d96a74edd47","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/commits/1b03f6b972ce494292f745809a3e7d96a74edd47"}],"sha":"644fe71a9b45b21da3fd038460ef7d2fa1cd80d3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/commits/644fe71a9b45b21da3fd038460ef7d2fa1cd80d3"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83823539?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fred-labs","id":83823539,"login":"fred-labs","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzODIzNTM5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/commits/1b03f6b972ce494292f745809a3e7d96a74edd47/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-21T18:30:09Z","email":"fred-labs@mailbox.org","name":"fred-labs"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-21T18:30:09Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Keep the server instructions within what a client shows (#630)\n\n* Keep the server instructions within what a client shows\n\nClaude Code cuts a server''s MCP instructions at 2048 characters and drops the rest\nwithout a mark. The instructions were longer than that, so the model never saw the\nend of the rule to stop and report an unreachable service, nor where files live.\n\nThe instructions are shortened to the loop and the rules it cannot do without, and\nINSTRUCTIONS_LIMIT with a test over the server as built keeps them there.\n\n* Keep image building and checking out of the default loop\n\nThe loop is what every campaign walks: author, validate, preview, pilot, wait,\nread. Extending an image and testing one in a container are what some campaigns\nneed, so they stand in a section of their own. A campaign is queued, so the loop\ndoes not ask whether a lane has room first.\n\n* Name the upload in the loop, and move file bytes over HTTP\n\nA workspace is filled by write_file for a .vast or .osc and by create_upload for\neverything else, so the first step names both. File bytes belong on the HTTP\nroutes the file tools hand back, not in the model''s context.","tree":{"sha":"60ea2dec1216c78aca1c7c4d908bf076cb58c198","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/git/trees/60ea2dec1216c78aca1c7c4d908bf076cb58c198"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/git/commits/1b03f6b972ce494292f745809a3e7d96a74edd47","verification":{"payload":"tree 60ea2dec1216c78aca1c7c4d908bf076cb58c198\nparent 80b453d8653d1fee5c0eb9eccd4fef9aedfc0bab\nauthor fred-labs <fred-labs@mailbox.org> 1790015409 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790015409 +0200\n\nKeep the server instructions within what a client shows (#630)\n\n* Keep the server instructions within what a client shows\n\nClaude Code cuts a server''s MCP instructions at 2048 characters and drops the rest\nwithout a mark. The instructions were longer than that, so the model never saw the\nend of the rule to stop and report an unreachable service, nor where files live.\n\nThe instructions are shortened to the loop and the rules it cannot do without, and\nINSTRUCTIONS_LIMIT with a test over the server as built keeps them there.\n\n* Keep image building and checking out of the default loop\n\nThe loop is what every campaign walks: author, validate, preview, pilot, wait,\nread. Extending an image and testing one in a container are what some campaigns\nneed, so they stand in a section of their own. A campaign is queued, so the loop\ndoes not ask whether a lane has room first.\n\n* Name the upload in the loop, and move file bytes over HTTP\n\nA workspace is filled by write_file for a .vast or .osc and by create_upload for\neverything else, so the first step names both. File bytes belong on the HTTP\nroutes the file tools hand back, not in the model''s context.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqsXexCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAADxgQABCYWsnycaHHakBMSgZcwZA7\nxtIhTzfvtqJpcS40DfGsCIJ0/Q50yH+BxZRE5NBZY9DFNOq+CPwvqrdw1NfYD88e\n7zfq9jWptq+/k0EWaHL9vol6raH8hrqt+YX/wse5zQqceYgb4MvWJex3CfEgcYaI\nhw4n4vDccGScN92joULznC6P7qwsl1QNZv6hJTL72sg8SWo6AYhbmXTdbNDZT1Io\nnvfbqu2qTv/ob669tkAsPN5zNeLLoDVx9zuEao+l8/uLpVPi2h9wUGHqVC+qlWua\nveDONLepEMUgH6UbUAOyMYtEX9J2v7ixlkNv9rLFSav4+FBsRuGafFtZHjpKEexZ\n61IIMuvVBIzg0DRXO9l4KeEBberX/upbb4V+uhmUf3qZlS2nQxE3bSgspbEC4RUv\nPKKEW89lKhV8OdbniHiNKr9s3a772a22p