https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fred-labs","id":83823539,"login":"fred-labs","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzODIzNTM5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/commits/80b453d8653d1fee5c0eb9eccd4fef9aedfc0bab/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-21T18:10:22Z","email":"fred-labs@mailbox.org","name":"fred-labs"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-21T18:10:22Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Admit a job only onto a node with room for its disk request (#620)\n\nAdmission granted a node on cpu, memory and gpu, then pinned the pod to it.\nA postprocessing pod also requests ephemeral storage the size of what it\nstages, and the scheduler places on that too, so a grant to the node with\nthe most free cores could name one without room for the campaign: the pin\nexcluded every other node, and the pod waited Unschedulable for disk that\nanother node had free, until postprocessing gave up on it.\n\nEphemeral storage is now a dimension of a job''s sizing and of every node''s\nbudget and capacity, charged and released through the same ledger as cpu.\nThe budget reads what the scheduler reads: allocatable, less what bound pods\nrequest. A pod''s disk is charged as the scheduler charges it, the larger of\nits workload containers'' sum and its largest one-shot init container,\nbecause a postprocessing pod''s staging request is on an init container and\nsumming workload containers alone would report that disk as free.\n\nA refusal names disk only where a job asks for it, and quotes the node that\nis largest in the dimension that does not fit.","tree":{"sha":"b67b93700f27b8d455118be5bceb1e87449a7d49","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/git/trees/b67b93700f27b8d455118be5bceb1e87449a7d49"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/git/commits/80b453d8653d1fee5c0eb9eccd4fef9aedfc0bab","verification":{"payload":"tree b67b93700f27b8d455118be5bceb1e87449a7d49\nparent 249dd0c61f36a35f6e780e38d94affbb90e042e7\nauthor fred-labs <fred-labs@mailbox.org> 1790014222 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790014222 +0200\n\nAdmit a job only onto a node with room for its disk request (#620)\n\nAdmission granted a node on cpu, memory and gpu, then pinned the pod to it.\nA postprocessing pod also requests ephemeral storage the size of what it\nstages, and the scheduler places on that too, so a grant to the node with\nthe most free cores could name one without room for the campaign: the pin\nexcluded every other node, and the pod waited Unschedulable for disk that\nanother node had free, until postprocessing gave up on it.\n\nEphemeral storage is now a dimension of a job''s sizing and of every node''s\nbudget and capacity, charged and released through the same ledger as cpu.\nThe budget reads what the scheduler reads: allocatable, less what bound pods\nrequest. A pod''s disk is charged as the scheduler charges it, the larger of\nits workload containers'' sum and its largest one-shot init container,\nbecause a postprocessing pod''s staging request is on an init container and\nsumming workload containers alone would report that disk as free.\n\nA refusal names disk only where a job asks for it, and quotes the node that\nis largest in the dimension that does not fit.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqsXMOCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAWHEQAI5MgHXjqPpdxlH+/sGAvD2g\nMpWpVKFdTeNPFZ9D48gTO1oq2aSqlCaHmJHKXJiSZnYELMND3BhN2QhOUPTJZmU4\nMSOpYxFLRJ30SNPF2q4r0837TqlJtOBw+gyNU39deehIzi93wNsSoUZemgFKt8fC\nDjyNPzITiOzbcuuwC6DcPSU81FcNbKiQH1X04kp4bG/Std+ySmuvwd1FDJhWROSo\n97RhL6YY1CIIUitwBtOPTU5rz6PIGxiUOz7Hq44ENLfKyVskMK5DSSGd9a1Z0N0u\nab35z4t/A5CwG4RJnYZbTfUwGPDCp7i2dOA66Vg7zAbXdUl4RMBhxTdU8xGdbpzG\nZ6hb0HumKwZQo/j8AiRLK6FRKNek9SDf3NGu7jhuXeK1xJ5xhbpHGmhcUxCX9+CJ\nKk0kMMl17YJQ82ZVTMZ48m8jZP8Is/BIJjkA2NwugEzl7PkC21DBEHNVciknue1L\nVJ8qMZiXTYbCPc4Q2OJoi27cyfND0Ztg9q/LLp2HRwGOqCpZomCQ0NUCe2rHQEO6\neYsEdCYAU7CgW24/9kz14v7egeWB98XXklTL0YW+aIkH+H8tdB23cGAAb+6+eHvE\nH2s992JTma/8JAhqX4rr5iP3T9fvsw1J5V3KGMyHSjg+RNpVF8RyEu9lXOY3waqO\nXm4N/1YQFNNKnQ1Wz0yk\n=Logv\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-21T18:10:23Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cps-test-lab/robovast/commit/80b453d8653d1fee5c0eb9eccd4fef9aedfc0bab","node_id":"C_kwDOPVaL7doAKDgwYjQ1M2Q4NjUzZDFmZWU1YzBlYjllY2NkNGZlZjlhZWRmYzBiYWI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cps-test-lab/robovast/commit/249dd0c61f36a35f6e780e38d94affbb90e042e7","sha":"249dd0c61f36a35f6e780e38d94affbb90e042e7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/commits/249dd0c61f36a35f6e780e38d94affbb90e042e7"}],"sha":"80b453d8653d1fee5c0eb9eccd4fef9aedfc0bab","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/commits/80b453d8653d1fee5c0eb9eccd4fef9aedfc0bab"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83823539?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fred-labs","id":83823539,"login":"fred-labs","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzODIzNTM5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/commits/249dd0c61f36a35f6e780e38d94affbb90e042e7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-21T17:57:52Z","email":"fred-labs@mailbox.org","name":"fred-labs"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-21T17:57:52Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"A campaign''s frozen _config/ holds its sut: config sources (#628)\n\nA source the sut: channel declares is kept out of run_files, so a run mounts\nonly its configuration''s rewritten copy. The copy into <campaign>/_config/ read\nthe same list, so the original was never archived -- and composing the campaign\nagain from its snapshot, which a restart re-entering it, a retrigger and a\nworkspace rebuilt from it all do, failed on the missing file.\n\nWhat _config/ must hold is now defined once, by snapshot_files: the run files\nplus the declared sources. Staging copies that set, and the retrigger''s\ncompleteness check compares against it, so a snapshot that lacks a source is\nrefused by name instead of failing inside composition. What a run mounts, and\nthe configuration identity, are unchanged.","tree":{"sha":"826fda04c76da1d568981229bb89e1c94bf4b9f2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/git/trees/826fda04c76da1d568981229bb89e1c94bf4b9f2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/git/commits/249dd0c61f36a35f6e780e38d94affbb90e042e7","verification":{"payload":"tree 826fda04c76da1d568981229bb89e1c94bf4b9f2\nparent 001ccabb700f767495ebd7f18dd3957ddae318f9\nauthor fred-labs <fred-labs@mailbox.org> 1790013472 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790013472 +0200\n\nA campaign''s frozen _config/ holds its sut: config sources (#628)\n\nA source the sut: channel declares is kept out of run_files, so a run mounts\nonly its configuration''s rewritten copy. The copy into <campaign>/_config/ read\nthe same list, so the original was never archived -- and composing the campaign\nagain from its snapshot, which a restart re-entering it, a retrigger and a\nworkspace rebuilt from it all do, failed on the missing file.\n\nWhat _config/ must hold is now defined once, by snapshot_files: the run files\nplus the declared sources. Staging copies that set, and the retrigger''s\ncompleteness check compares against it, so a snapshot that lacks a source is\nrefused by name instead of failing inside composition. What a run mounts, and\nthe configuration identity, are unchanged.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATU