\n\nThe storage estimate for a part''s stage derived the batch to narrow to on its own:\na part carries a discriminator and host commands, so it was sized as a batch named\nafter the part and without its own runs. Which batch a stage is narrowed to and\nwhether it fetches the rosbags are now JobRole''s, and the manifest and the estimate\nboth read them there.\n\nThe tests that still used build_manifest''s removed batch_commands keyword name a\nrole, and the Job shapes they cover include a part and the Job that completes a\nsplit. The stage-query test checks that no Job but a search batch''s is narrowed to\na batch, and the fetch test counts requests rather than the word curl.","tree":{"sha":"c5b301fc7f35f0b464f753e2804fd9fcaf4ee55a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/git/trees/c5b301fc7f35f0b464f753e2804fd9fcaf4ee55a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/git/commits/f989ac134aac06121b4130329f0a45e62269885b","verification":{"payload":"tree c5b301fc7f35f0b464f753e2804fd9fcaf4ee55a\nparent c47e43c242a955e018f72d0544eda12f8a943a9e\nauthor fred-labs <fred-labs@mailbox.org> 1789990057 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789990057 +0200\n\nRead the split plan through the postprocess input seam, and size a part for its runs (#624)\n\npostprocess_campaign read the split plan outside _read_submit_inputs, the one seam\nthrough which it reads a campaign tree, so everything that stubs that seam met the\n.vast anyway. The plan is now the fifth fact the seam returns, and _plan_split reads\nthe .vast it is handed instead of looking it up twice.\n\nThe storage estimate for a part''s stage derived the batch to narrow to on its own:\na part carries a discriminator and host commands, so it was sized as a batch named\nafter the part and without its own runs. Which batch a stage is narrowed to and\nwhether it fetches the rosbags are now JobRole''s, and the manifest and the estimate\nboth read them there.\n\nThe tests that still used build_manifest''s removed batch_commands keyword name a\nrole, and the Job shapes they cover include a part and the Job that completes a\nsplit. The stage-query test checks that no Job but a search batch''s is narrowed to\na batch, and the fetch test counts requests rather than the word curl.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqsRSpCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAfXMQAGuC6Y/sjIpHuL0fFl8IJTPK\nufvvlfam9DJMhLk+afZ5xdTvkuL87f8Y3JBFHHNvleU1mgC49TxuVWN9cwptdsA3\nj8bnQusL04ckNmvvCsmEHMt/gUfP9/D5vCp8wq5sGmNlg0egTHRSA6KOIpLINezp\nIOE+QX1lDpAOcTqOXDIy1OTvFzZtY7slIRJeQFzJmr9G55S7A4PUN1FrJpMOtTAz\nzMLaWZNRxCP75kFM20iJa1lywvDr0KDa1FudniplBTcQPpfV7/pci9vRSs2aHkT8\nTKSjebH7ZI1dOfFlae5LpHsUVHxpMRkxbI1q0IvJOrKlA6ZiG6F06N5HmFOjjA0w\nFPN9rIHqcBXInTH0GqGnhkBjcmQ04dqEq2L0zI6GsyNQskanBl6pklXzDrI9T2/K\nIyObu2I/AmzNUfNFJpwlaAMDiBdlBlrIlpAq9r9qrEBrjVnrdIFcyQX0LsSGFYDI\nCUYHt8qK68fYcXXcXEAhNDMKcGdRyJB1liPbw/OABKEVq/tGVGBw4h11fbqbIc1D\nGH1lQAjsV/DAYqGw2J5MT4NuRK9ozu5JZg1agnjPCxYZ/wHy8Wsh0LjjwkCIiDNJ\njao5OeZ3mOguPygJWHBx1A3cKJ7l5ahL7sAaq3ofu64L6isJiBee0DfFD/6KP4R4\nZeHL/0xS7FYk+WaeJyQw\n=xwcZ\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-21T11:27:38Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cps-test-lab/robovast/commit/f989ac134aac06121b4130329f0a45e62269885b","node_id":"C_kwDOPVaL7doAKGY5ODlhYzEzNGFhYzA2MTIxYjQxMzAzMjlmMGE0NWU2MjI2OTg4NWI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cps-test-lab/robovast/commit/c47e43c242a955e018f72d0544eda12f8a943a9e","sha":"c47e43c242a955e018f72d0544eda12f8a943a9e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/commits/c47e43c242a955e018f72d0544eda12f8a943a9e"}],"sha":"f989ac134aac06121b4130329f0a45e62269885b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/commits/f989ac134aac06121b4130329f0a45e62269885b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83823539?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fred-labs","id":83823539,"login":"fred-labs","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzODIzNTM5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/commits/c47e43c242a955e018f72d0544eda12f8a943a9e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-21T07:37:20Z","email":"fred-labs@mailbox.org","name":"fred-labs"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-21T07:37:20Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"A fetch retries its whole pipeline, on the schedule every transfer follows (#622)\n\nA pod''s fetch is `curl | tar`, and it retried inside curl. curl cannot rewind a\npipe, so a stream cut short and retried sent a second archive after the part of the\nfirst it had already passed to tar, which refused it: a service restarted during a\nfetch failed the Job even though the service came back within the retries. Those\nretries were also far shorter than the service''s startup budget.\n\nEvery attempt now re-runs the whole pipeline and extracts over what the last one\nleft. The retry schedule moves to pod_access and is shared by the fetch, the pod\nuploader and the postprocessing host''s delivery, sized to outlast a service\nupgrade. A 4xx is not retried, nor a whole stream that will not extract. The fetch\nexits with curl''s code when the transfer failed and tar''s when the extraction did,\nso a stage failure now names its cause.","tree":{"sha":"98c79bf85e906f3293dc702d74c25d010228096e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/git/trees/98c79bf85e906f3293dc702d74c25d010228096e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/git/commits/c47e43c242a955e018f72d0544eda12f8a943a9e","verification":{"payload":"tree 98c79bf85e906f3293dc702d74c25d010228096e\nparent 436d9329f7db5649c21f9d53bcc6b05f43843428\nauthor fred-labs <fred-labs@mailbox.org> 1789976240 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789976240 +0200\n\nA fetch retries its whole pipeline, on the schedule every transfer follows (#622)\n\nA pod''s fetch is `curl | tar`, and it retried inside curl. curl cannot rewind a\npipe, so a stream cut short and retried sent a second archive after the part of the\nfirst it had already passed to tar, which refused it: a service restarted during a\nfetch failed the Job even though the service came back within the retries. Those\nretries were also far shorter than the service''s startup budget.\n\nEvery attempt now re-runs the whole pipeline and extracts over what the last one\nleft. The retry schedule moves to pod_access and is shared by the fetch, the pod\nuploader and the postprocessing host''s delivery, sized to outlast a service\nupgrade. A 4xx is not retried, nor a whole stream that will not extract. The fetch\nexits with curl''s code when the transfer failed and tar''s when the extraction did,\nso a stage failure now names its cause.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqsN6wCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA+V8QAG5N7zp17B+/c3rhGRD9b1sy\n/tJ+8bN2oylpV2sZ9On5s0jndP4K1tn75DZDZ1ANv4Bi4vmPivupyfd+018b2btU\ntNBY1yRObNLLf0qqxIz4IOtlVZJ5/dfIWRuGFQ2PAmw8qnmLX3Wzq5hnbYfEpxQd\nvVVt4gQEk+Kd8odgsUCsJkeKcr0BwiLs5WsPPvbyRRZSq48+ykcNx1IJjw6meq7r\nZJk2bqN4TE6RfBT2HXNyk0jTlz5hSTvzvmNuZ9bbNm5jimYUpKdOaI0M+4tUwlwN\nBA5D87X25WNzI1vbaeRJ7weGqVnvNZpa+J9M1FyAJcs+5ymasTGfmyJ0utkvCSpj\nzTqbaoeCVQwkp4wyiEJzL4oUBi7ov5rvFBvM9pPQPzwHkvhX8TfgqYa9phPZSOmm\nNGwr7INnDWaE/umDggFYWj8EQh/P6qG9pIxEMJdxV5g9faCCg3CgCO3zsPLSBybl\nO+sqF5+Tt+DAFg4jEQ8+EZLSTcWhJRwpWvSQg45zzD3FGXEouUgkWgXepQe0TjYQ\n11j+SSVlDPa0RioXw2Skebr6bqfOe6r6N5GrW/R/GmV1XIIAEY5rmnn6aht82XtY\ne5PqswvmxhU00BNkK4Ef1lerY/tM2CX0gE4Sj6utb28doMaOMymHnE9fMev2iF2A\nyQawobrD6wu74Q5UQeKk\n=7ZEt\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-21T07:37:20Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cps-test-lab/robovast/commit/c47e43c242a955e018f72d0544eda12f8a943a9e","node_id":"C_kwDOPVaL7doAKGM0N2U0M2MyNDJhOTU1ZTAxOGY3MmQwNTQ0ZWRhMTJmOGE5NDNhOWU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cps-test-lab/robovast/commit/436d9329f7db5649c21f9d53bcc6b05f43843428","sha":"436d9329f7db5649c21f9d53bcc6b05f43843428","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/commits/436d9329f7db5649c21f9d53bcc6b05f43843428"}],"sha":"c47e43c242a955e018f72d0544eda12f8a943a9e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/commits/c47e43c242a955e018f72d0544eda12f8a943a9e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83823539?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fred-labs","id":83823539,"login":"fred-labs","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzODIzNTM5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/commits/436d9329f7db5649c21f9d53bcc6b05f43843428/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-21T06:38:59Z","email":"fred-labs@mailbox.org","name":"fred-labs"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-21T06:38:59Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Mount the git token into a postprocessing Job''s host container (#619)\n\nThe host container re-installs the campaign''s `plugins:` before its steps\nrun. A `git+https` spec for a private repository is cloned by that install,\nand the token the service pod holds never reached a postprocessing Job, so\nthe clone asked for a username with no terminal to read one from. Since a\nlarge campaign''s postprocessing moved into Jobs of its own, every such\ncampaign logged a refused plugin install in each part.\n\nThe host container now mounts the same Secret, at the same path, as the\nservice pod, so `config_plugins` finds the token where it already looks.\nOnly the host: the conversion runs the campaign''s own image and the stage\nonly fetches bytes, so neither is given a credential. The volume is\noptional because the Secret exists only where setup was given a token; a\nrequired one naming nothing would hold the pod in ContainerCreating instead\nof letting the install report which token is missing.","tree":{"sha":"bfbbc41acf164ae1a20692e7e5cf95a13b2262f0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/git/trees/bfbbc41acf164ae1a20692e7e5cf95a13b2262f0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/git/commits/436d9329f7db5649c21f9d53bcc6b05f43843428","verification":{"payload":"tree bfbbc41acf164ae1a20692e7e5cf95a13b2262f0\nparent 92a5ba50a237dec371eaa504a7adf93189568dd6\nauthor fred-labs <fred-labs@mailbox.org> 1789972739 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789972739 +0200\n\nMount the git token into a postprocessing Job''s host container (#619)\n\nThe host container re-installs the campaign''s `plugins:` before its steps\nrun. A `git+https` spec for a private repository is cloned by that install,\nand the token the service pod holds never reached a postprocessing Job, so\nthe clone asked for a username with no terminal to read one from. Since a\nlarge campaign''s postprocessing moved into Jobs of its own, every such\ncampaign logged a refused plugin install in each part.\n\nThe host container now mounts the same Secret, at the same path, as the\nservice pod, so `config_plugins` finds the token where it already looks.\nOnly the host: the conversion runs the campaign''s own image and the stage\nonly fetches bytes, so neither is given a credential. The volume is\noptional because the Secret exists only where setup was given a token; a\nrequired one naming nothing would hold the pod in ContainerCreating instead\nof letting the install report which token is missing.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqsNEDCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAjSAQAFrIhXs2FalQPsrVtpYKVmuE\nBye6GP+grTBNHo1Ypigteeu6aiY3A6+TvO3zHrp+eaEm0WmHks4xtxPZiEfRaM7q\nUhwXww4ezidTbhgHu5YS5eXKhjNsDalJAu73gqdMbV0gzy/W0fETTWnOwB7q6VaD\nBdMl4EVHyLBwpv1oyBKhq4yJeQrg8QI7RIZJk7AjW0Sif4vqobQeBO1pXQvQb5a5\nGQ1iKc3xiGUG9ABbHnB0PP87WS8W91hd16D2xdLU/jOcoF3BdF0i/QZkP584gRAU\nZm1zl65aixcLsVb9eBhifo4dMdBJ2JTcaFNAmGQl7oK7B8J09TIEIeN8OxPNO+S6\nz9GE/Ob4uNBi6nirOxf5lx/sXb31VpXfo4faVWFtpRm0LligfO5tYfvEL7rXdqUd\nQy+FTo2Hcu1y7kWlgVaN1uAvlftbjfj8wGRAXWDo72C8SZQgy3bWVOdqITkbfLGO\nLB6nv362kSI8ZPAEKNXh0798ELnocXDq+8/d3jdBt16FWjIjdDEmrp+K4LGfM+4k\noSNllCnmu2WKM9BjuPaVtxQKPhgbblMv17h5xlvdo5sy4BejxGNNEnCAB3B1usi/\n9mRAbIFpy1MW531qUh1wERfl9m7/IEJWeCyrrSWtziuUIMCWeLZhhBcH5/RIlMjv\nti4FRSUfb8aBca1xm2to\n=tQdN\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-21T06:39:00Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cps-test-lab/robovast/commit/436d9329f7db5649c21f9d53bcc6b05f43843428","node_id":"C_kwDOPVaL7doAKDQzNmQ5MzI5ZjdkYjU2NDljMjFmOWQ1M2JjYzZiMDVmNDM4NDM0Mjg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cps-test-lab/robovast/commit/92a5ba50a237dec371eaa504a7adf93189568dd6","sha":"92a5ba50a237dec371eaa504a7adf93189568dd6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/commits/92a5ba50a237dec371eaa504a7adf93189568dd6"}],"sha":"436d9329f7db5649c21f9d53bcc6b05f43843428","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/commits/436d9329f7db5649c21f9d53bcc6b05f43843428"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83823539?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fred-labs","id":83823539,"login":"fred-labs","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzODIzNTM5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/commits/92a5ba50a237dec371eaa504a7adf93189568dd6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-21T06:19:24Z","email":"fred-labs@mailbox.org","name":"fred-labs"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-21T06:19:24Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"A campaign''s auxiliary containers end with it (#618)\n\nA variation that needs a helper image runs it while it composes, which is the longest a\ncampaign goes before its first run, and it is the one piece of a campaign a flag cannot\nreach: a process somewhere else, under a client that detaches when it is signalled.\n\nLocally, the runner names each container and, for a span that can be stopped, removes it\n(`docker rm -f`) rather than signalling the client -- a signalled `docker run` detaches\nand leaves the container running, and an entrypoint that ignores SIGTERM ignores a\nforwarded one. The flag reaches the runner where the runner is built, through a\nspan-scoped predicate beside the existing runner factory rather than through a factory of\nits own: the fallback that builds the local runner is also what resolves a `family:` ref\nand what refuses when there is no docker, and a factory installed only to carry the flag\nwould have had to repeat both.\n\nIn-cluster, `exec_stream` reads the predicate between polls, closes the stream and ends\nthe campaign, and every exec a runner makes -- mirroring the workspace in, the command,\nmirroring it back -- carries it. Closing a stream does not signal the process in the pod;\nthe pod goes when its span does, which the stopped path reaches in seconds.\n\nA stop that removes the container a variation was waiting on is passed through as a stop.\nThe composition''s handler calls anything else out of a variation a bug in the plugin,\nwhich would put an operator''s own request on the plugin and make a search read the\ngeneration as unscorable.\n\nTwo properties of the shared helper this depends on. Removing a container ends the client\nattached to it, but a removal that fails would leave the caller blocked on a stream that\nnever closes, so the client''s own group is ended afterwards as a backstop. And signalling\na child''s group is only safe when the child has a session of its own: one that shares the\ncaller''s would take the caller with it, so such a child is signalled alone, and the\ncontainer runner only starts a new session where something may end it, which keeps an\ninteractive Ctrl+C reaching a command nobody else can stop.","tree":{"sha":"6549cec544f000036cc1d8d16f360198068b6069","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/git/trees/6549cec544f000036cc1d8d16f360198068b6069"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/git/commits/92a5ba50a237dec371eaa504a7adf93189568dd6","verification":{"payload":"tree 6549cec544f000036cc1d8d16f360198068b6069\nparent 9a47359041a2ba519fbbc7e55aae9bec22557f76\nauthor fred-labs <fred-labs@mailbox.org> 1789971564 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789971564 +0200\n\nA campaign''s auxiliary containers end with it (#618)\n\nA variation that needs a helper image runs it while it composes, which is the longest a\ncampaign goes before its first run, and it is the one piece of a campaign a flag cannot\nreach: a process somewhere else, under a client that detaches when it is signalled.\n\nLocally, the runner names each container and, for a span that can be stopped, removes it\n(`docker rm -f`) rather than signalling the client -- a signalled `docker run` detaches\nand leaves the container running, and an entrypoint that ignores SIGTERM ignores a\nforwarded one. The flag reaches the runner where the runner is built, through a\nspan-scoped predicate beside the existing runner factory rather than through a factory of\nits own: the fallback that builds the local runner is also what resolves a `family:` ref\nand what refuses when there is no docker, and a factory installed only to carry the flag\nwould have had to repeat both.\n\nIn-cluster, `exec_stream` reads the predicate between polls, closes the stream and ends\nthe campaign, and every exec a runner makes -- mirroring the workspace in, the command,\nmirroring it back -- carries it. Closing a stream does not signal the process in the pod;\nthe pod goes when its span does, which the stopped path reaches in seconds.\n\nA stop that removes the container a variation was waiting on is passed through as a stop.\nThe composition''s handler calls anything else out of a variation a bug in the plugin,\nwhich would put an operator''s own request on the plugin and make a search read the\ngeneration as unscorable.\n\nTwo properties of the shared helper this depends on. Removing a container ends the client\nattached to it, but a removal that fails would leave the caller blocked on a stream that\nnever closes, so the client''s own group is ended afterwards as a backstop. And signalling\na child''s group is only safe when the child has a session of its own: one that shares the\ncaller''s would take the caller with it, so such a child is signalled alone, and the\ncontainer runner only starts a new session where something may end it, which keeps an\ninteractive Ctrl+C reaching a command nobody else can stop.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqsMxsCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAQasQAGEkWN92jFnuyPlJCjq8ZDeR\nlrhT9TXGw2cmBoOHI1wi/lz2quCzinBwaboX11rT0xQQeMreQsCbW2qQ511A6g1u\nlPnobhCoF0+Bfn9opCz6INnjvwRd+v03oRLedKLRv6KjcKKD797pcDeXSlTiV45D\n0LXj/Jd3Th/lqE1ueym+Cnixoe/4A9LXDWw3IY1aUubsGEpQi70W1VByKiVcizc/\n6M4nC4aJKGBGlRBmAhseafu56PTc57rnnohKNbWzvLpU0jpnzlVpoVIkNgczEw8J\ncNXC8u98x1xOlG/32nBbvCgp9U5HNWF3hsqOw9HrlVm368z4LFpNPcbLLaD5Nz51\ngzvq0wQdIGmgxta/IUwyIpYa9B5UIAMfYbdBZITctMe/XsAoMHg0+L0n89h923Dt\ne1POqd3C1jhAT3qEVZFT6b/ByAZxrTvD5tm8WBkybhsfXVzy+XLNaqwPK7Z8AWby\nuLxGl/mVUnlqq2sKWHxzWSYKCgTmtPiwi3CCurj7FsCedurqLgzlqQbq40WpDPd7\na3AYKBA0kaFWltsTrU0HPM8NIhVBcBIKadGC01aptu7sIe2T4wwprRVgMiOcBEKt\n8rxKYGsWtKkOJ5RS+vlQ5cXGqlIss8SraTjbVfgGkwX9SpSzWhnu+F0tVkts6tU3\nUClImteI5veuujpgk2XN\n=MTK4\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-21T06:19:25Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cps-test-lab/robovast/commit/92a5ba50a237dec371eaa504a7adf93189568dd6","node_id":"C_kwDOPVaL7doAKDkyYTViYTUwYTIzN2RlYzM3MWVhYTUwNGE3YWRmOTMxODk1NjhkZDY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cps-test-lab/robovast/commit/9a47359041a2ba519fbbc7e55aae9bec22557f76","sha":"9a47359041a2ba519fbbc7e55aae9bec22557f76","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/commits/9a47359041a2ba519fbbc7e55aae9bec22557f76"}],"sha":"92a5ba50a237dec371eaa504a7adf93189568dd6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/commits/92a5ba50a237dec371eaa504a7adf93189568dd6"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83823539?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fred-labs","id":83823539,"login":"fred-labs","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzODIzNTM5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/commits/9a47359041a2ba519fbbc7e55aae9bec22557f76/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-21T06:18:32Z","email":"fred-labs@mailbox.org","name":"fred-labs"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-21T06:18:32Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Deleting a campaign removes what it owns beside its directory, or says what it left (#617)\n\nThe local lane writes each archive it shares into `_archives/` next to the campaign\ndirs, a full gzip copy each, and a failed import keeps the copy it fetched from the\nshare under `_imports/<campaign-id>.tar.gz`. A delete removed neither, so it freed\nthe campaign directory and left up to a second copy of the campaign on the same\nvolume.\n\nThe directory itself was removed with `ignore_errors=True`, and the result was\n`ok=True` whatever stayed behind. Run output written by a container user other than\nthe service''s (`execution.run_as_user`) cannot be unlinked by the service, so such a\ndelete answered \"deleted\" while the space stayed taken.\n\nA delete now removes the directory, the campaign''s local archives (and the `.part` of\na killed writer) and a share copy an import staged, then reports `ok=false` naming the\nfirst path it could not remove and why. Everything removable still goes, so a second\ndelete retries only what is left. The per-campaign memo caches are dropped too, so a\nlater campaign under the same id is not described by the old one. The copy on an\nexternal share provider is still never touched.\n\nThe archive directory is resolved by one function, `local_archive_dir`, that the\nwriter and the delete share. The web UI shows a partial delete as an error instead of\n\"Deleted\". The `run_as_user` docs state the default each lane actually uses, and the\nstaging sweep''s docstring no longer claims that a failed extraction deletes its copy.","tree":{"sha":"198883ac4efc53c1289fed152b9770b1cd791dbc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/git/trees/198883ac4efc53c1289fed152b9770b1cd791dbc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/git/commits/9a47359041a2ba519fbbc7e55aae9bec22557f76","verification":{"payload":"tree 198883ac4efc53c1289fed152b9770b1cd791dbc\nparent 4c5cf2c61a2bf0f8550dcb7e878b14ae7dafa329\nauthor fred-labs <fred-labs@mailbox.org> 1789971512 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789971512 +0200\n\nDeleting a campaign removes what it owns beside its directory, or says what it left (#617)\n\nThe local lane writes each archive it shares into `_archives/` next to the campaign\ndirs, a full gzip copy each, and a failed import keeps the copy it fetched from the\nshare under `_imports/<campaign-id>.tar.gz`. A delete removed neither, so it freed\nthe campaign directory and left up to a second copy of the campaign on the same\nvolume.\n\nThe directory itself was removed with `ignore_errors=True`, and the result was\n`ok=True` whatever stayed behind. Run output written by a container user other than\nthe service''s (`execution.run_as_user`) cannot be unlinked by the service, so such a\ndelete answered \"deleted\" while the space stayed taken.\n\nA delete now removes the directory, the campaign''s local archives (and the `.part` of\na killed writer) and a share copy an import staged, then reports `ok=false` naming the\nfirst path it could not remove and why. Everything removable still goes, so a second\ndelete retries only what is left. The per-campaign memo caches are dropped too, so a\nlater campaign under the same id is not described by the old one. The copy on an\nexternal share provider is still never touched.\n\nThe archive directory is resolved by one function, `local_archive_dir`, that the\nwriter and the delete share. The web UI shows a partial delete as an error instead of\n\"Deleted\". The `run_as_user` docs state the default each lane actually uses, and the\nstaging sweep''s docstring no longer claims that a failed extraction deletes its copy.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqsMw4CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAphQQAEMeq9u2Ega56UR7EZsBbjZ/\n7tmYsM4g2xvc+5bPDlHZYFaqrBAIDdBorXMEr7uBZppOYqp/cGpy0z9YaJq9ThAy\n6M1W9Yw7tTGGLIKQGhXXxWMC2KM0x4CpfBLHlgqWTlZWU53UO4FWHhzPSzOYF+D/\nd6k9u6+5bAZuSEz6N1a4oPL5sQyOOUuoQJbHMXXxRKa+D9cUc6lSHo01+nWjEUdW\n39Sk3zrWxDag47bbEwl3bI3EWdTc2qAXjDqG2LA2n9OkbHR4eu2bj4DLKz0gSIrt\n49Ag9wu6BDdN/c3ZRaXQtGmxP5iXcLkbojeB9q81oAdcuoDZUlNWJ34KLkUtUuPz\n7yMM8DnMJjwdmZYd5Mzx9A2frKksgh3dtdf++O1Hnzef2kNjI8byqJDQrjbDmvo7\nDL71QsLkywrLzORc8DfxYESpEsnKI5z7hfXSNO+D1GjD+TlKyUbfPBg2XGfPAEoP\niMhVaCHCga8tyooZFtQWWYYf9vr3aPyPDS/kQqyVk09modV3Driuq69C9gElDuXw\nk6fagQYjOr8a/ZKgW3Bqr/SwqpiV+EwduFIpmMcYcPTvco3pjJxts1xFGQzgPXkP\n9zFWwB+Rf5sL1IN4FyvX3KPVU291n01PjzbWx9Gy8/563HmhFmDaWUrv6F2lY0SJ\nEgxdwYh1f9pMgBOlrzcv\n=hpko\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-21T06:18:32Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cps-test-lab/robovast/commit/9a47359041a2ba519fbbc7e55aae9bec22557f76","node_id":"C_kwDOPVaL7doAKDlhNDczNTkwNDFhMmJhNTE5ZmJiYzdlNTVhYWU5YmVjMjI1NTdmNzY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cps-test-lab/robovast/commit/4c5cf2c61a2bf0f8550dcb7e878b14ae7dafa329","sha":"4c5cf2c61a2bf0f8550dcb7e878b14ae7dafa329","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/commits/4c5cf2c61a2bf0f8550dcb7e878b14ae7dafa329"}],"sha":"9a47359041a2ba519fbbc7e55aae9bec22557f76","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/commits/9a47359041a2ba519fbbc7e55aae9bec22557f76"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83823539?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fred-labs","id":83823539,"login":"fred-labs","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzODIzNTM5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/commits/4c5cf2c61a2bf0f8550dcb7e878b14ae7dafa329/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-21T06:14:26Z","email":"fred-labs@mailbox.org","name":"fred-labs"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-21T06:14:26Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"A stop is read wherever a campaign waits (#616)\n\nThe cooperative flag was set correctly and read in a handful of places, so how long a\nstop took was decided by whichever wait the campaign happened to be in: a poll loop\nnoticed it at the end of its interval, and a step with no check at all -- a plugin\ninstall, a composition, a config upload, a conversion queued for capacity -- ran to its\nown end first. The phase a campaign was in decided whether a stop took a second or an\nhour, which is not something an operator can know before pressing it.\n\nTwo primitives now carry it, and nothing else does. `ControllerState.wait_for_stop`\nreplaces `time.sleep` in every poll loop the campaign''s own thread runs, so a wait ends\nwhen the flag is set rather than when the interval expires; `raise_if_stopped` ends the\ncampaign at a boundary between two steps, where the cheapest honest place to give up is\nbefore the next one. Below the execution layer the same thing is a `should_stop`\npredicate, which `stop_checker` now builds for any scope, and the helpers in\n`common.stop`: one implementation of \"watch this subprocess and kill its group\", where\nthere were three that had drifted.\n\nWhat that closes, in order of how long it used to take: the plugin install and the\nisolated composition worker are run under the watch, so pip and a composing sweep end;\nthe driver checks between staging, installing, building and starting; the cluster batch\nchecks before it stages anything and before it creates a Job, and waits on the flag\ninstead of sleeping between polls; a search''s per-batch conversion takes the runs-scope\npredicate and ends the campaign rather than scoring a generation whose metrics were\nnever derived; and postprocessing queued for capacity gives its place in the queue back\ninstead of holding it for the length of its timeout.\n\nA batch that ends while stopped sweeps its own Jobs once more on the way out. The\nservice''s teardown runs when the stop lands, but the queue can create a Job between that\nand the loop''s next read of the flag, and nothing else would collect it.\n\nA stop that surfaces as some other exception -- a worker killed mid-line, a container\nremoved under the command it was running -- is recorded as a stop rather than a failure.\nThe exception describes the consequence and the flag describes the cause, and filing it\nas a failure sends whoever reads it after a bug in a step that was working.\n\nScope semantics are unchanged: what a runs-stop, a postprocessing-stop and a share-stop\neach leave behind, and a building campaign detaching rather than cancelling a shared\nimage build. The per-phase table in the architecture doc now states all of it in one\nplace, including where the two lanes deliberately differ.","tree":{"sha":"0dadbc29e40ad5f83b6cfbe04e4177c420699c2c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/git/trees/0dadbc29e40ad5f83b6cfbe04e4177c420699c2c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/git/commits/4c5cf2c61a2bf0f8550dcb7e878b14ae7dafa329","verification":{"payload":"tree 0dadbc29e40ad5f83b6cfbe04e4177c420699c2c\nparent f90d45b4b5dabda57af82586baddcaa1b57cc9e1\nauthor fred-labs <fred-labs@mailbox.org> 1789971266 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789971266 +0200\n\nA stop is read wherever a campaign waits (#616)\n\nThe cooperative flag was set correctly and read in a handful of places, so how long a\nstop took was decided by whichever wait the campaign happened to be in: a poll loop\nnoticed it at the end of its interval, and a step with no check at all -- a plugin\ninstall, a composition, a config upload, a conversion queued for capacity -- ran to its\nown end first. The phase a campaign was in decided whether a stop took a second or an\nhour, which is not something an operator can know before pressing it.\n\nTwo primitives now carry it, and nothing else does. `ControllerState.wait_for_stop`\nreplaces `time.sleep` in every poll loop the campaign''s own thread runs, so a wait ends\nwhen the flag is set rather than when the interval expires; `raise_if_stopped` ends the\ncampaign at a boundary between two steps, where the cheapest honest place to give up is\nbefore the next one. Below the execution layer the same thing is a `should_stop`\npredicate, which `stop_checker` now builds for any scope, and the helpers in\n`common.stop`: one implementation of \"watch this subprocess and kill its group\", where\nthere were three that had drifted.\n\nWhat that closes, in order of how long it used to take: the plugin install and the\nisolated composition worker are run under the watch, so pip and a composing sweep end;\nthe driver checks between staging, installing, building and starting; the cluster batch\nchecks before it stages anything and before it creates a Job, and waits on the flag\ninstead of sleeping between polls; a search''s per-batch conversion takes the runs-scope\npredicate and ends the campaign rather than scoring a generation whose metrics were\nnever derived; and postprocessing queued for capacity gives its place in the queue back\ninstead of holding it for the length of its timeout.\n\nA batch that ends while stopped sweeps its own Jobs once more on the way out. The\nservice''s teardown runs when the stop lands, but the queue can create a Job between that\nand the loop''s next read of the flag, and nothing else would collect it.\n\nA stop that surfaces as some other exception -- a worker killed mid-line, a container\nremoved under the command it was running -- is recorded as a stop rather than a failure.\nThe exception describes the consequence and the flag describes the cause, and filing it\nas a failure sends whoever reads it after a bug in a step that was working.\n\nScope semantics are unchanged: what a runs-stop, a postprocessing-stop and a share-stop\neach leave behind, and a building campaign detaching rather than cancelling a shared\nimage build. The per-phase table in the architecture doc now states all of it in one\nplace, including where the two lanes deliberately differ.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqsMtCCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAxoQQACrABJIHwx5IPA9Jh8d5EFQo\nW0CagmLWR8dmTyNA7jkpb1VSbNPoxqpqNFByJ/LTVZS8K+1JJJfTSBIlPZvQSoN6\n3za57w/Rh839MVofkAdPA6nT7+NdFP1vHK/Ja2WD1Rbd5tQhGEF+BzgQhu/DFwff\n2ww88TCb/AMG0Xjae3zFh6gEcKh9qsC4PCQiVlYhDetQtzXiJPumkoszzenV/joD\ndqHPLiXEicf81pcpvlSo9aD9/gibDvpCo86Lx/+mOJpLauLLMnR7UL0eekzLniVP\nIweBhC0JZaUPs1vAG7JftnzypUq+fjFkvB15FmABuJ9dZ7kLsa6C0UO+dI5/L+9h\nm2VXXmhRDgGd0Ix3vadUMeJkfbX4YcxZ03kA+qrqdban1ZPdspZSBcmfEfFJjG1R\nsWp9KQbRnCx79i6aeCG3hk8g0pUmAX/9ewBdN4RBiGCF2cEFeaULK8EZkcm58jF+\nT4txP+DqQMTFhSMMFu6PRp1+HLJp1/iraQAC5zJaADupjqbyfkqqlrbdc+H/+WXh\ntqZJRANxbWazPBXNNqmiW9ojYvgobX4dDYmELKS5smivFZWMHrPvZ24YD3x3XSCW\n/lOimJOE1PmG8BK+ZYeWgKiKUMR7cGc+6GiMX8KsbVnQtU/Airq7oEydhc/0QPhM\nHzAd72xGrTKjJTFdZLik\n=T6y6\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-21T06:14:27Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cps-test-lab/robovast/commit/4c5cf2c61a2bf0f8550dcb7e878b14ae7dafa329","node_id":"C_kwDOPVaL7doAKDRjNWNmMmM2MWEyYmYwZjg1NTBkY2I3ZTg3OGIxNGFlN2RhZmEzMjk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cps-test-lab/robovast/commit/f90d45b4b5dabda57af82586baddcaa1b57cc9e1","sha":"f90d45b4b5dabda57af82586baddcaa1b57cc9e1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/commits/f90d45b4b5dabda57af82586baddcaa1b57cc9e1"}],"sha":"4c5cf2c61a2bf0f8550dcb7e878b14ae7dafa329","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/commits/4c5cf2c61a2bf0f8550dcb7e878b14ae7dafa329"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83823539?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fred-labs","id":83823539,"login":"fred-labs","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzODIzNTM5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/commits/f90d45b4b5dabda57af82586baddcaa1b57cc9e1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-20T19:51:37Z","email":"fred-labs@mailbox.org","name":"fred-labs"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-20T19:51:37Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Staging a re-entered campaign copies nothing onto itself (#609)\n\n* Staging a re-entered campaign copies nothing onto itself\n\nA campaign a restart picks up is relaunched from the _config/ it froze, so the\nproject tree and the campaign tree are one directory and every staging copy is\na file onto itself. shutil.copy2 refuses that outright, so the campaign failed\nwith SameFileError -- one whose Jobs were still running and had already\ndelivered results. The copies go through a helper that skips a file already in\nplace; copying the project into the campaign is what makes the campaign\nself-contained, and where it already is the campaign, that is done.\n\n* The conversion Job''s submitter imports only what it raises on\n\nrun_conversion_job carries a local import of ApiException that nothing in it\ncatches, which the linter refuses.\n\n* The JUnit reader''s docstring names the keys it returns\n\nread_test_result returns ''success'', not ''passed'', and also start_epoch and\nfailure_message. An extractor written against the docstring raises KeyError on its\nfirst cell.","tree":{"sha":"af214ab0c40013b600604d3fd65af1fcacc6cb86","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/git/trees/af214ab0c40013b600604d3fd65af1fcacc6cb86"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/git/commits/f90d45b4b5dabda57af82586baddcaa1b57cc9e1","verification":{"payload":"tree af214ab0c40013b600604d3fd65af1fcacc6cb86\nparent 941bc8fa4f712af0a24003e0523667113b3dc01c\nauthor fred-labs <fred-labs@mailbox.org> 1789933897 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789933897 +0200\n\nStaging a re-entered campaign copies nothing onto itself (#609)\n\n* Staging a re-entered campaign copies nothing onto itself\n\nA campaign a restart picks up is relaunched from the _config/ it froze, so the\nproject tree and the campaign tree are one directory and every staging copy is\na file onto itself. shutil.copy2 refuses that outright, so the campaign failed\nwith SameFileError -- one whose Jobs were still running and had already\ndelivered results. The copies go through a helper that skips a file already in\nplace; copying the project into the campaign is what makes the campaign\nself-contained, and where it already is the campaign, that is done.\n\n* The conversion Job''s submitter imports only what it raises on\n\nrun_conversion_job carries a local import of ApiException that nothing in it\ncatches, which the linter refuses.\n\n* The JUnit reader''s docstring names the keys it returns\n\nread_test_result returns ''success'', not ''passed'', and also start_epoch and\nfailure_message. An extractor written against the docstring raises KeyError on its\nfirst cell.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqsDlJCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA6NMQAIJ4Sz7alVkMEHYKZGGm0Hnm\n6xLA5+kYnGX7l0fjJVGSSTKB4/sGLQXmC5qNfdqDAnmOz66h6X5ajLrQh0OPXW7F\nS0gGV2iJxN8Nppo5KSykgk4Yjkb9LztXHsNJqZA5gjMoMhn6qUQtoRgzkNn26sZl\nqwj1aj3Snbk8apgbzBB+DbTaH1Hmc+A7oEIsWIduAsGSTVh5uHLIqKaikCpS6LrK\naS5BiyJkA7RqvcYfbbhfv9vJcRy1cxvcOlBCJbfdELmcgR1q7zoexAhnLZihSpxE\nC8tbO74DHL64QBwOzJ7XDjuTyTWEKpzRRRgmcvwKtjbg7YkOZ9VHD3FOYb24AOPo\nLQNC515wvq8fNT8VK9wh7cODe9iaCOy/9ephc9t6sV3cg1eczbYRycM0bvsaXN72\nWkjRMwiF9qdCb7tHuqZluB0wlmhJ5IpQuGEzNWptsXI0pSMuOaZaDnL3Kj5ahbv8\na5MuwBlVk9VmwYAECQgIDfuJ0zkTV2TQ9fQjSGxEipztKTERTz1WQQko0ldWyMKE\nNIh/4cZQbQ/9cpMA8lDHRzpX7s57iDeDGSxQ+M/QsaksNWAN7drUFfUVOBZqe/z6\nwolJ+O3aq3T5Mk0w/9d84pvmbSxZqeU49Hhgj4ZxEcdeJ1/nQYjF