f0a24003e0523667113b3dc01c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83823539?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fred-labs","id":83823539,"login":"fred-labs","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzODIzNTM5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/commits/ea0eabf5939b9b5ec4fb8c9b321e492440ffe018/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-20T19:33:26Z","email":"fred-labs@mailbox.org","name":"fred-labs"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-20T19:33:26Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"The runner and what it spawns can be interrupted (#612)\n\nThe cluster entrypoint starts the runner as a background job, so that the done-marker is\nwritten however the runner ends. A shell without job control sets SIGINT and SIGQUIT to\nSIG_IGN for such a job, and an ignored disposition is inherited through every exec below\nit: the runner, the scenario''s children, a bag recorder.\n\nNothing downstream can undo it. exec preserves SIG_IGN, Popen(restore_signals=True) resets\nonly SIGPIPE/SIGXFZ/SIGXFSZ, and a non-interactive shell may not reset a signal that was\nignored on entry -- so it has to be right where the job is forked.\n\n`ros2 bag record` closes its bag on SIGINT and on nothing else. Ignored, it is killed after\na timeout instead, and a recording that was never closed has no metadata.yaml, which makes\nthe directory unreadable to every converter: the runs pass, the campaign reports success,\nand every bag-derived table is empty.\n\n`env --default-signal` restores exactly those two dispositions for the runner and everything\nunder it; where coreutils is too old for the flag, job control does the same by giving the\njob its own process group. Both paths are tested, as is the requirement that the job stay a\nsimple command, since $! is what the TERM trap forwards to.","tree":{"sha":"0625cf4e220bf2253b728f4848b17a846c802b31","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/git/trees/0625cf4e220bf2253b728f4848b17a846c802b31"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/git/commits/ea0eabf5939b9b5ec4fb8c9b321e492440ffe018","verification":{"payload":"tree 0625cf4e220bf2253b728f4848b17a846c802b31\nparent 275b459f5a45c17e8b1bf608ea315202b54216f1\nauthor fred-labs <fred-labs@mailbox.org> 1789932806 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789932806 +0200\n\nThe runner and what it spawns can be interrupted (#612)\n\nThe cluster entrypoint starts the runner as a background job, so that the done-marker is\nwritten however the runner ends. A shell without job control sets SIGINT and SIGQUIT to\nSIG_IGN for such a job, and an ignored disposition is inherited through every exec below\nit: the runner, the scenario''s children, a bag recorder.\n\nNothing downstream can undo it. exec preserves SIG_IGN, Popen(restore_signals=True) resets\nonly SIGPIPE/SIGXFZ/SIGXFSZ, and a non-interactive shell may not reset a signal that was\nignored on entry -- so it has to be right where the job is forked.\n\n`ros2 bag record` closes its bag on SIGINT and on nothing else. Ignored, it is killed after\na timeout instead, and a recording that was never closed has no metadata.yaml, which makes\nthe directory unreadable to every converter: the runs pass, the campaign reports success,\nand every bag-derived table is empty.\n\n`env --default-signal` restores exactly those two dispositions for the runner and everything\nunder it; where coreutils is too old for the flag, job control does the same by giving the\njob its own process group. Both paths are tested, as is the requirement that the job stay a\nsimple command, since $! is what the TERM trap forwards to.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqsDUGCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAuAcQACD2NnhmchWgx73p5xoYODbW\n1O3dmj8WgoBthv1QJUmIwk8G0DNLd5UrI4JjPOWMh+FzGS7eNQs2ONa3qoX/Cw22\nh8g67ah7j4/5kSGzAZjv4Wdvaj79PvXP49k7Uoucl9sbr5BdJabVHan2RrT3nRBh\noCcBlbY0WfIXYMwb5v+4aVt6uHv32VOEj9Tvg5r7sV1VyGwlEfgQEw+5y9EtzanA\nHj6TFMzwbOWmuKp5mujvuvSDtdB1EBhzvGxoI6wwZwOGoa8GR9HXXpxvYQma9kaV\nvfA+CHq+84V9Xs558Z+8n82SY2J8AZ2HDUl91QBtjo24TCBMoXpEpnvc5jS6bDy8\niEFEQxZ5wLTX0a9NJp1CRvV3St8tcFMqTeZUJD9VXO4TQSHxAZgYe06pc6Nc6Gjs\nD53CRtyr0Pwe6Wvzkf7pF1uYvtykurvxdnkqQmgJOmW6cDfKctSpo9g2qFGhzvmZ\nj2Vu70SrSriWRiIUYC8CcQz6zpNFdjFtasfOQndAV9BMM3HyEMlq3KLUqAUXB+8c\nlY9PcnhhyOwAnXZEltufCH75HJQYU/kkHsajDZ5tV4obUgTZVtP3MNP3kMNuspqX\nBIKTFKNAwfhOA8rkfYWuopPJHkebr9WeX1y7JReu8ChbrdJ6+vasTeBZiVbPTWil\nWC0spM0UslEtDmj+wH2e\n=A3Y0\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-20T19:33:27Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cps-test-lab/robovast/commit/ea0eabf5939b9b5ec4fb8c9b321e492440ffe018","node_id":"C_kwDOPVaL7doAKGVhMGVhYmY1OTM5YjliNWVjNGZiOGM5YjMyMWU0OTI0NDBmZmUwMTg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cps-test-lab/robovast/commit/275b459f5a45c17e8b1bf608ea315202b54216f1","sha":"275b459f5a45c17e8b1bf608ea315202b54216f1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/commits/275b459f5a45c17e8b1bf608ea315202b54216f1"}],"sha":"ea0eabf5939b9b5ec4fb8c9b321e492440ffe018","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/commits/ea0eabf5939b9b5ec4fb8c9b321e492440ffe018"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83823539?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fred-labs","id":83823539,"login":"fred-labs","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzODIzNTM5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/commits/275b459f5a45c17e8b1bf608ea315202b54216f1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-19T22:08:21Z","email":"fred-labs@mailbox.org","name":"fred-labs"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-19T22:08:21Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Split a campaign''s postprocessing across Jobs (#601)\n\nA cluster campaign''s postprocessing ran in one pod: one stage of the whole\ncampaign, one conversion pool, one host pass. Most of that work is per\nrun, and the rest of the cluster sat idle while it ran.\n\nA plugin now declares scope = \"run\" when a run''s output depends only on\nthat run, the scenario jobs it links, the other runs of those jobs and the\ncampaign-level inputs. The rosbag conversion, run_log, resource_usage and\nnav2_bt_tree do; a plugin that says nothing is never split.\nsplit_postprocessing() takes the longest run-scoped prefix of the ordered\nsteps as the map and leaves the rest, in order, as the reduce, so no step\nis ever moved ahead of one it may read.\n\nThe map then runs in one Job per PART of the campaign''s runs, submitted\nthrough the admission queue with the shared tracker, and the reduce runs\nafter all of them in one ordinary campaign-level Job with the map steps\nskipped, which completes the campaign. How many parts is the cluster''s\nanswer: its recorded size over what one conversion reserves, so a\ndeployment that configures nothing postprocesses with the cluster it has.\nROBOVAST_POSTPROCESS_MAX_PARALLEL caps that where an operator wants a cap,\nand 1 keeps the whole postprocessing in one Job.\n\n- A part is a set of whole scenario jobs with their runs, balanced by\n  rosbag bytes, so no bag is converted twice and re-planning over a\n  campaign some parts delivered into gives the same parts.\n- The planner records each part''s membership in the campaign, and the\n  archive route stages a part by name (part=), pruning other parts'' runs\n  and jobs; an unplanned part is a 404.\n- A part''s log, provenance and usage record are named for it, so the\n  parts'' deliveries never replace each other''s; the reduce reads every\n  part''s provenance, and the POSTPROCESSING section shows each part''s log\n  under a heading naming it and how many there are.\n- A failed or unfinished map never starts the reduce; a stop deletes every\n  part; a part never created is reported with the queue''s refusal.\n- After a service restart, a split with a part still running is resumed\n  with the options it recorded: running parts are waited for, not created\n  again.\n\nOne JobRole says which postprocessing Job is being built -- the campaign''s\nown, a search''s per-batch conversion, one part, or the Job that completes a\nsplit -- instead of four flags that only make sense together, and\nsubmit_postprocess_job() is the one place a postprocessing Job is created,\nwith its Secret, its scripts and the conflict it may meet. The Job module''s\nseams the split needs are public rather than reached into.","tree":{"sha":"33345eb532fa85931202b938e6e28d8dceeba5ba","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/git/trees/33345eb532fa85931202b938e6e28d8dceeba5ba"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/git/commits/275b459f5a45c17e8b1bf608ea315202b54216f1","verification":{"payload":"tree 33345eb532fa85931202b938e6e28d8dceeba5ba\nparent 2e946f304d4103afd875362ea4c2a5166e7cac8d\nauthor fred-labs <fred-labs@mailbox.org> 1789855701 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789855701 +0200\n\nSplit a campaign''s postprocessing across Jobs (#601)\n\nA cluster campaign''s postprocessing ran in one pod: one stage of the whole\ncampaign, one conversion pool, one host pass. Most of that work is per\nrun, and the rest of the cluster sat idle while it ran.\n\nA plugin now declares scope = \"run\" when a run''s output depends only on\nthat run, the scenario jobs it links, the other runs of those jobs and the\ncampaign-level inputs. The rosbag conversion, run_log, resource_usage and\nnav2_bt_tree do; a plugin that says nothing is never split.\nsplit_postprocessing() takes the longest run-scoped prefix of the ordered\nsteps as the map and leaves the rest, in order, as the reduce, so no step\nis ever moved ahead of one it may read.\n\nThe map then runs in one Job per PART of the campaign''s runs, submitted\nthrough the admission queue with the shared tracker, and the reduce runs\nafter all of them in one ordinary campaign-level Job with the map steps\nskipped, which completes the campaign. How many parts is the cluster''s\nanswer: its recorded size over what one conversion reserves, so a\ndeployment that configures nothing postprocesses with the cluster it has.\nROBOVAST_POSTPROCESS_MAX_PARALLEL caps that where an operator wants a cap,\nand 1 keeps the whole postprocessing in one Job.\n\n- A part is a set of whole scenario jobs with their runs, balanced by\n  rosbag bytes, so no bag is converted twice and re-planning over a\n  campaign some parts delivered into gives the same parts.\n- The planner records each part''s membership in the campaign, and the\n  archive route stages a part by name (part=), pruning other parts'' runs\n  and jobs; an unplanned part is a 404.\n- A part''s log, provenance and usage record are named for it, so the\n  parts'' deliveries never replace each other''s; the reduce reads every\n  part''s provenance, and the POSTPROCESSING section shows each part''s log\n  under a heading naming it and how many there are.\n- A failed or unfinished map never starts the reduce; a stop deletes every\n  part; a part never created is reported with the queue''s refusal.\n- After a service restart, a split with a part still running is resumed\n  with the options it recorded: running parts are waited for, not created\n  again.\n\nOne JobRole says which postprocessing Job is being built -- the campaign''s\nown, a search''s per-batch conversion, one part, or the Job that completes a\nsplit -- instead of four flags that only make sense together, and\nsubmit_postprocess_job() is the one place a postprocessing Job is created,\nwith its Secret, its scripts and the conflict it may meet. The Job module''s\nseams the split needs are public rather than reached into.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqrwfVCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAIpcQAJPHXBfEsRlJovMqDYscSn4z\nWBMekzsVuciROwv6C70oiGl1S6IwNQSUEpSkdQbsPAU5R+HmBOXmtuV7IVGSCp9i\nWw4OwBT9vDq5JPfoX4Zv4V/FniB/5kuvGYCuaBVofpgDNHv3JGt5+cScKOnFGxFN\nAE2nOEBbxXhtJli1u+sYlbmjt44x3GTLOj3QDmwAco7nEvgf1R/k3zEeLOMSE6b2\nZ8Rstggq+tMg7ypGnRlgJAicoitBytnXgcPrga2tW1vuecJxaIeDsRaa+LTY97fh\nmtvvMd+0LDeAiTjZjN9RL9c/qmyFrT/iRVV3+Taq20kPVRLy+tFgLwmk+n0+3xQh\nMSFjUsF/6UUCo1wBl9tdX2Sio+H5WITsarixp1pF1oR4jkAHJL2wE7o3LXCepzjl\noEBFZO3iSEkwtAV//+ODk0nwDURUfFCdZiNHse4S/NYw6X0dHdVNgQd7EFmVyUHt\nzpuPXCpUz71fBN+r22SFmbOZWTnblgS9dTsPVvhp4sIkpATlIHOfkFOIhRjIkQ1B\nbTK/RQyFG7tPIv1CarIN13Aznkd6n+U9zNGpXsn4YFL202kXYzMKWnvilqT5y5re\nWahJf65yxVPYO4yBgGQDlvFOOoFYtKYam0XdrP72f42F1Zk+E15jjb7GKrJs/evO\nvNmO5SmfXRjXAoCcAXr2\n=wu0d\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-19T22:08:22Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cps-test-lab/robovast/commit/275b459f5a45c17e8b1bf608ea315202b54216f1","node_id":"C_kwDOPVaL7doAKDI3NWI0NTlmNWE0NWMxN2U4YjFiZjYwOGVhMzE1MjAyYjU0MjE2ZjE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cps-test-lab/robovast/commit/2e946f304d4103afd875362ea4c2a5166e7cac8d","sha":"2e946f304d4103afd875362ea4c2a5166e7cac8d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/commits/2e946f304d4103afd875362ea4c2a5166e7cac8d"}],"sha":"275b459f5a45c17e8b1bf608ea315202b54216f1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/commits/275b459f5a45c17e8b1bf608ea315202b54216f1"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83823539?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fred-labs","id":83823539,"login":"fred-labs","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzODIzNTM5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fred-labs","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/commits/2e946f304d4103afd875362ea4c2a5166e7cac8d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-19T22:05:47Z","email":"fred-labs@mailbox.org","name":"fred-labs"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-19T22:05:47Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Adopt a restart''s campaigns after the secret is bound, not before (#608)\n\nA campaign a restart picks up mints its pods'' data-plane token from the\nservice''s secret, and that secret is bound to the transport by build_app --\nafter the transport is constructed. The cluster service adopted in its\nconstructor, so every campaign a restart resumed failed with \"no auth token\nbound to this service\", after its compute was already spent. Observed on a\npilot: the interrupted run''s own pod delivered its results, and the driver that\nwas meant to pick it up died.\n\nAdoption moves to start_serving(), which build_app calls once the secret is\nbound and before the port is -- keeping both properties the constructor held\none of: a resumed campaign can mint, and no launch over the API can race a\ncampaign about to be adopted.\n\nThe restart message and the web UI''s page said Kubernetes starts the new pod\nbefore stopping the old. The campaigns are on a volume one node may mount at a\ntime, so the deployment replaces rather than overlaps: both now say the API is\naway for a few seconds, and longer where the replacement has campaigns to pick\nup.","tree":{"sha":"e210fbac446da18463551c783d5d0460583b7c17","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/git/trees/e210fbac446da18463551c783d5d0460583b7c17"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cps-test-lab/robovast/git/commits/2e946f304d4103afd875362ea4c2a5166e7cac8d","verification":{"payload":"tree e210fbac446da18463551c783d5d0460583b7c17\nparent 1836f3792f25a0747197f34b1494814a6f63141b\nauthor fred-labs <fred-labs@mailbox.org> 1789855547 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789855547 +0200\n\nAdopt a restart''s campaigns after the secret is bound, not before (#608)\n\nA campaign a restart picks up mints its pods'' data-plane token from the\nservice''s secret, and that secret is bound to the transport by build_app --\nafter the transport is constructed. The cluster service adopted in its\nconstructor, so every campaign a restart resumed failed with \"no auth token\nbound to this service\", after its compute was already spent. Observed on a\npilot: the interrupted run''s own pod delivered its results, and the driver that\nwas meant to pick it up died.\n\nAdoption moves to start_serving(), which build_app calls once the secret is\nbound and before the port is -- keeping both properties the constructor held\none of: a resumed campaign can mint, and no launch over the API can race a\ncampaign about to be adopted.\n\nThe restart message and the web UI''s page said Kubernetes starts the new pod\nbefore stopping the old. The campaigns are on a volume one node may mount at a\ntime, so the deployment replaces rather than overlaps: both now say the API is\naway for a few seconds, and longer where the replacement has campaigns to pick\nup.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqrwc7CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAulcQAHmWfxCwkHyTJmb20SBbd7I1\np9liBeyaFAWtcWf5HTKJf1kB8ZrxBHv8z6oNV/zWa5iAknFD1MYB93n02PO6lIMe\njc8KyqHQh7QKVfMgm07QW3N8rnAfmgpbaREDlhdlr3Tf+Zrb14ACOltK9fS3Putc\n/F+JNe4hji9UIFGuhTNL7YdB1YIY9Aq3DyYd+qkw7jri/4Fw+FmfVfNkl5jtFwUN\nHZt8rnF9C8a3M5wDFg0LNNocpAguS7vXao43ZXEm6re5DagOEWTA6GRw55uhsv2z\nu7AKjxEkghvQwZgXXDQXJz9VH6YzF2yo6JhiFnqYtAEEWgC+WrxwKviCDVZ9DuUE\nTDcoL5GFKCGRcQJqW2aS8KjBA8tInIOW+tX11JV+xV03PZ5ckADCUxdjUAIWD977\ns3zEktLqSNP0UxpQUH7FandORY0B7sCq3piC75EG5qSptJLhDD52cCSJFBLuPpqs\n/he2rHd+Iyu22Jnk21r7kh+BB6XCa54EQFAC9u4aVfqb+CKwj8ZV/evY5CgAfI3z\nGdIgfWpj8AQ5QJ21NnJS0AvafP48yRla0EgTV2AFMH1s+9vXwpspRO/hSz5N9RjE\nBiVk8kiiIN82Na1P/rf0o5JoeqySHJPCGoFHcY/cj7CmxHeBnysVcZ80xd/98KLJ\nCYM2Z7KDYdNjn1qTWuV1\n=cWem\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-19T22:05:47Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.c